        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is: Option 1 i.e. Dethronement.\n\nKey Points\nDethronement means the act of removing someone from their position of power, especially a monarch or ruler. (\u0938\u093F\u0902\u0939\u093E\u0938\u0928 \u0938\u0947 \u0939\u091F\u093E\u0928\u093E)\nExample: The dethronement of the king led to a period of political instability in the country.\nThe word fits the context as Robert is described as being removed from a high position of authority.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is: Option 1 i.e. Dethronement.\n\nAdditional Information\nHere are the other options explained along with their Hindi meanings and example sentences:\n\nAbdication (\u0930\u093E\u091C \u0924\u094D\u092F\u093E\u0917): Refers to voluntarily renouncing a throne or position of power.\nExample: The king\u2019s abdication shocked the entire nation.\nRevolution (\u0915\u094D\u0930\u093E\u0902\u0924\u093F): Refers to a sudden, radical, or complete change, often in politics or government.\nExample: The industrial revolution transformed the way people lived and worked.\nCoronation (\u0930\u093E\u091C\u094D\u092F\u093E\u092D\u093F\u0937\u0947\u0915): Refers to the ceremony of crowning a monarch.\nExample: The coronation of the new king was attended by dignitaries from all over the world.",
