        solution: 'Solution\n\nThe correct answer is: Option 2 (Rumbling).\n\nKey Points\nThe word "Brontide" refers to the low, muffled, and distant sound of thunder or rumbling. (\u0926\u0942\u0930 \u0938\u0947 \u0906\u0928\u0947 \u0935\u093E\u0932\u0940 \u0917\u0921\u093C\u0917\u0921\u093C\u093E\u0939\u091F \u0915\u0940 \u0906\u0935\u093E\u091C)\nExample: The brontide echoed softly across the valley after the storm.\n"Rumbling" relates to a continuous, deep, resonant sound, similar to thunder. (\u0917\u0921\u093C\u0917\u0921\u093C\u093E\u0939\u091F)\nExample: We heard a rumbling sound as the earthquake began to shake the ground.\nHence, we can conclude that the synonym of "Brontide" is "Rumbling."\nTherefore, the correct answer is: Option 2 (Rumbling).\n\nAdditional Information\nHere are the other options explained along with their Hindi meanings and example sentences:\n\nSilence (\u0936\u093E\u0902\u0924\u093F): The absence of sound or noise.\nExample: The silence in the library was broken by the sound of a dropped book.\nLight (\u092A\u094D\u0930\u0915\u093E\u0936): A natural agent that makes things visible.\nExample: The morning light streamed through the windows, filling the room with warmth.\nExplosion (\u0935\u093F\u0938\u094D\u092B\u094B\u091F): A violent and sudden outbreak, often with a loud noise.\nExample: The explosion of fireworks lit up the night sky during the festival.',
