        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is 'BADC'.\n\nKey Points\nHere is a detailed explanation of the correct order of the sentences to form a coherent paragraph:\nSentence B states that a metal detector is an electronic instrument that is used to detect the presence of metals nearby. This sentence provides an introductory statement about what a metal detector is and sets the context for the subsequent sentences.\nSentence A follows sentence B by explaining the usefulness of metal detectors. It states that metal detectors are valuable tools for locating hidden metal within objects or even metal objects buried underground. This sentence elaborates on the purpose and application of metal detectors.\nSentence D comes after sentence A. It describes the common features of metal detectors. It mentions that they often consist of a handheld unit with a sensor probe. This probe can be swept over the ground or other objects to detect the presence of metal. Sentence D provides information about the physical structure and usage of metal detectors.\nFinally, sentence C concludes the paragraph by explaining how metal detectors work. It states that when the sensor probe of the metal detector comes near a piece of metal, it is indicated by a changing tone in earphones or a needle moving on an indicator. Sentence C describes the mechanism by which metal detectors provide feedback to the user when metal is detected.\nTherefore, the correct order to form a coherent paragraph is 1) BADC:\nB. Metal detector is an electronic instrument that detects the presence of metals nearby.\nA. Metal detectors are useful for finding metal hidden within objects or metal objects buried underground.\nD. They often consist of a handheld unit with a sensor probe that can be swept over the ground or other objects.\nC. If the sensor comes near a piece of metal, this is indicated by a changing tone in earphones or a needle moving on an indicator.",
