        question: "The following passage consists of six sentences. The first and the sixth sentences are given. The middle four sentences in each have been removed and jumbled up. These are labelled P, Q, R and S. Find the proper sequence of the four sentences.\nS1: The empowerment of women and the improvement of their political, social, economic and health status is a highly important end in itself.\nP: In addition, it is essential for the achievement of sustainable development.\nQ: In all parts of the world, women are facing threats to their lives, health and well-being as a result of being overburdened with work and of their lack of power and influence.\nR: In most regions of the world, women receive less formal education than men, and at the same time, women's own knowledge, abilities and coping mechanisms often go unrecognized.\nS: The full participation and partnership of both women and men is required in productive and reproductive life, including shared responsibilities for the care and nurturing of children and maintenance of the household.\nS6: The power relations that impede women's attainment of healthy and fulfilling lives operate at many levels of society, from the most personal to the highly public.",
