        answer: "a",
        solution: 'Solution\n\nThe correct answer is "QSRP"\n\nKey Points\nS1 introduces the main topic of the passage, which is a poll conducted by Elon Musk on Twitter asking if he should step down as head of the platform.\nQ provides background information on the poll, stating that it was open for 24 hours and received a total of 17.5 million responses, with a majority of 57% voting against Musk remaining as head of Twitter.\nS describes the idea of a CEO asking their subscribers whether they should remain in their position as being intriguing.\nR adds further context to the situation by stating that nothing can be more democratic than this, although corporations are not typically democratic.\nP confirms that Musk has a reputation for being a true believer in free speech, the rule of law, and keeping his promises.\nS6 highlights the fact that Musk has previously turned to Twitter polls for other important decisions regarding his company.\n\nThus, QSRP is the correct answer.\n\nCorrect paragraph: S1 Elon Musk, the billionaire owner of Twitter, ran a poll that just concluded today. Like all musk polls, the question was very simple. \u201CShould I step down as head of Twitter? I will abide by the results of this poll.\u201D Q Twitter subscribers had about 24 hours to respond. Over 17.5 million responded and the vote was overwhelmingly against him running Twitter, 57 per cent to 43 per cent. S The idea that a CEO of a company would ask his subscribers whether or not he should be at the helm is in and of itself very intriguing. R Nothing can be more democratic than this, although corporations are anything but democratic. P And if we know something about him, he\u2019s a true believer in free speech, the rule of law, and keeping the promises that he has made. S6 Musk has turned to Twitter polls for other seismic decisions about the company.',
