        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is: Option (2) i.e. Governments became increasingly controlled by the interests of stockholders.\n\nKey Points\nThe passage explains that as governments became more indebted, they depended on the goodwill of stockholders, giving these financial interests the power to influence national policy and military decisions.\nHume observed that even monarchies could lose true sovereign control as public debt increased, with stockholders able to direct government action for their own benefit.\nThe other options are contradicted by Hume\u2019s analysis in the passage.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is- Governments became increasingly controlled by the interests of stockholders.\n\nAdditional Information\nOption 1: The passage states the opposite.\nOption 3: The monarchy\u2019s authority was weakened, not strengthened.\nOption 4: Public debt had significant influence on military decisions.",
