        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is 'Who won the match yesterday?'\n\nKey Points\n'Wh questions' are the questions that start with WH words. They include:\n\u200BWhat, where, why, when, who, whom, which, whose, how.\n\u200BStructure of 'WH questions' with an/a auxiliary/modal verb: Wh word + auxiliary/modal verb + subject + main verb (V1) + ....?\n\u200BExample: What are you doing at the shop?\n\u200B\u200BStructure of 'WH questions' without an/a auxiliary/modal verb: Wh word + main verb + ....?\u200B\u200B\n\u200BExample: Who killed the dog?\nLet's discuss the given options:\nOption 1) 'When you went to Delhi?' is INCORRECT.\nThe sentence is in simple past tense and the structure for the same is given below:\nWh word + did + subject + V1 + object?\nCorrect sentence: When did you go to Delhi?\nOption 2) 'What did you broke in the kitchen?' is INCORRECT.\nThe sentence is in simple past tense and the structure for the same is given below:\nWh word + did + subject + V1 + object?\n'Broke (V2)' should be replaced with 'break (V1)'\nCorrect sentence: What did you break in the kitchen?\n\u200BOption 3) 'Why does the students not obey their teachers?' is INCORRECT.\u200B\n'Does' should be replaced with 'do' as subject 'students' is a plural noun.\nCorrect sentence: Why do the students not obey their teachers?\nOption 4) 'Who won the match yesterday?' is CORRECT.\nThe sentence is in simple present tense and is following the Structure \u200B\u200Bof 'WH questions' without an/a auxiliary/modal verb.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is option 4).",
