        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nThe numbers 3, 7, 13, and 37 are all prime numbers.\n\nTheir LCM is simply their product: 3 \xD7 7 \xD7 13 \xD7 37 = 10101.\n\nThis is already the least five-digit number divisible by all four.\n\nTo get a remainder of 2, simply add 2 to this LCM: 10101 + 2 = 10103.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 10103.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nDivisors: 3, 7, 13, 37\nRemainder: 2\nFormula: Required Number = LCM(Divisors) \xD7 k + Remainder\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 LCM(3, 7, 13, 37) = 3 \xD7 7 \xD7 13 \xD7 37\n\u21D2 21 \xD7 13 \xD7 37\n\u21D2 273 \xD7 37\n\u21D2 10101\n\nThe number must be of the form 10101k + 2.\n\nFor the least five-digit number, we take k = 1:\n\u21D2 Number = 10101 \xD7 1 + 2\n\u21D2 Number = 10101 + 2\n\u21D2 Number = 10103\n\u2234 The correct answer is 10103.\n\nAdditional Information\nGeneral Remainder Rule\n\nIf a number gives the same remainder R when divided by a, b, and c, then the general form is LCM(a, b, c) \xD7 k + R.\n\nLCM of Prime Numbers\n\nThe Least Common Multiple of any set of prime numbers is always equal to their product.\n\nDivisibility by 10101\n\nThe number 10101 is a unique number that can be expressed as 3 \xD7 7 \xD7 13 \xD7 37 or 101 \xD7 100 + 1.",
        topic: "Number System",
