        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nGiven:\nThe speed of a boat in still water is 9 km/h.\n\nDistance covered in downstream = 35 km\nDistance covered in upstream = 28 km\n\nConcept used:\n\nSpeed = Distance/Time\nDownstream speed = (v + u)\nUpstream speed = (v - u)\nWhere, v = Speed of the boat in still water, u = Speed of the stream\n\nCalculation:\nLet the speed of the stream be 's' km/h\n\nAccording to the question,\n\n35\n(9+s) = 28\n(9-s)\xB35\n(\n9\n+\ns\n) = 28\n(\n9\n-\ns\n)\n\n\u21D2 35(9 - s) = 28(9 + s)\n\u21D2 5(9 - s) = 4(9 + s)\n\u21D2 45 - 5s = 36 + 4s\n\u21D2 9 = 9s\n\u21D2 s = 1 km/h\n\u2234 The speed of the stream is 1 km/h.\nHence, the correct answer is 1 km/h.",
