        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nGiven Fraction = 2/7\nTotal Students = 7 units\nGirls = 2 units\nBoys = 7 - 2 = 5 units\n\nAlso Given, there are 111 more boys than girls\n\nAccording to the fraction,\n\nMore Number = 5 - 2 = 3 units\n3 units = 111\n1 unit = 37\nNumber of boys = 5 units = 5 \xD7 37 = 185\n\nGiven:\nTotal number of girls = 2/7 of total students\n\nThe total number of boys is 111 more than girls.\n\nCalculation:\nSuppose, the total number of girls in the school auditorium = x\nThen, total number of boys in the school auditorium = (x + 111)\nTotal students in the school auditorium = x + (x + 111) = 2x + 111\nTherefore, x = 2/7 \xD7 (2x + 111)\n\u21D2 x = (4x + 222)/7\n\u21D2 7x = 4x + 222\n\u21D2 7x - 4x = 222\n\u21D2 3x = 222\n\u21D2 x = 222/3 = 74\nTotal number of boys = 74 + 111 = 185\n\u2234 Total of 185 boys are there in the school auditorium.",
