        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nRatio of Amount to Principal for 3 years = (25500 + 8440.50) \xF7 25500 = 33940.5 \xF7 25500 = 1331 / 1000.\nEquivalent ratio for 1 year = 3\u221A(1331 / 1000) = 11 / 10.\nInterest rate\n(R) = (11 - 10) \xF7 10 \xD7 100% = 10%.\nSimple Interest for 3 years = 30% of Principal = 30% of 25500 = 7650.\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 7650.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nPrincipal\n(P) = Rs. 25,500\nTime (T) = 3 years\nCompound Interest (CI) = Rs. 8,440.50\n\nFormula Used:\nAmount (A) = P(1 + R / 100)T\nSimple Interest (SI) = (P \xD7 R \xD7 T) \xF7 100\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Amount (A) = P + CI\n\u21D2 A = 25500 + 8440.50 = 33940.50\n\u21D2 33940.50 = 25500 \xD7 (1 + R / 100)\xB3\n\u21D2 (1 + R / 100)\xB3 = 33940.50 \xF7 25500\n\u21D2 (1 + R / 100)\xB3 = 339405 / 255000\n\u21D2 (1 + R / 100)\xB3 = 1331 / 1000 (dividing by 255)\n\u21D2 (1 + R / 100)\xB3 = (11 / 10)\xB3\n\u21D2 1 + R / 100 = 11 / 10\n\u21D2 R / 100 = 1 / 10\n\u21D2 R = 10%\n\u21D2 SI = (25500 \xD7 10 \xD7 3) \xF7 100\n\u21D2 SI = 255 \xD7 30 = 7650\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 7650.\n\nAdditional Information\nEffective Compound Interest Rate\n\nFor a 10% per annum rate, the effective CI for 2 years is 21%, and for 3 years, it is 33.1%.\n\nDifference Between CI and SI (2 Years)\nDifference = P \xD7 (R \xF7 100)2. It determines the extra interest earned through compounding over exactly two years.\nDifference Between CI and SI (3 Years)\nDifference = P \xD7 (R \xF7 100)2 \xD7 (3 + R \xF7 100). Essential formula for efficiently finding the three-year CI and SI differences without complete calculations.",
