        question: "Two numbers are in the ratio 17 : 45. One-third of the smaller is less than one-fifth of bigger by 15. The smaller number is?",
        options: {
          a: "25.5",
          b: "67.5",
          c: "76.5",
          d: "86.5"
        },
        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nLet the two numbers be 17 units and 45 units.\n1/3 of the smaller number = 17/3 units, and 1/5 of the bigger number = 45/5 = 9 units.\nDifference = 9 - 17/3 = (27 - 17) / 3 = 10/3 units.\nGiven, 10/3 units = 15 \u21D2 1 unit = 15 \xD7 3 \xF7 10 = 4.5\nSmaller number = 17 units = 17 \xD7 4.5 = 76.5\n\u2234 The correct answer is 76.5.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nRatio of the two numbers = 17 : 45\n\nThe difference between 1/5 of the bigger number and 1/3 of the smaller number = 15\n\nCalculation:\n\u21D2 Let the smaller number be 17x and the bigger number be 45x.\n\u21D2 One-third of the smaller number = 17x / 3\n\u21D2 One-fifth of the bigger number = 45x / 5 = 9x\n\u21D2 According to the question, 9x - 17x / 3 = 15\n\u21D2 (27x - 17x) / 3 = 15\n\u21D2 10x / 3 = 15\n\u21D2 10x = 45\n\u21D2 x = 4.5\n\u21D2 Smaller number = 17x = 17 \xD7 4.5 = 76.5\n\u2234 The correct answer is 76.5.\n\nAdditional Information\nCompound Ratio\n\nIf two ratios are a : b and c : d, then their compound ratio is given by ac : bd.\n\nDuplicate & Sub-duplicate Ratio\n\nThe duplicate ratio of a : b is a2 : b2, and the sub-duplicate ratio is \u221Aa : \u221Ab.\n\nComponendo and Dividendo\n\nIf a : b = c : d, then by the rule of componendo and dividendo (a + b) : (a - b) = (c + d) : (c - d).",
