        status: "Correct (Slow)",
        chosenOption: "B",
        correctOption: "B",
        userTime: "00:38",
        avgTime: "00:21",
        question: "The average age of a class of 40 students and a teacher reduces by 0.5 years, if we exclude the teacher. If the initial average age is 18 years, then what is the age of the teacher?",
        options: {
          a: "41 years",
          b: "38 years",
          c: "40 years",
          d: "39 years"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nAge of excluded person = Initial Average + (Remaining members \xD7 Drop in average)\n\u21D2 Age of teacher = 18 + (40 \xD7 0.5)\n\u21D2 Age of teacher = 18 + 20\n\u21D2 Age of teacher = 38 years\n\u2234 The correct answer is 38 years.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nNumber of students = 40\nTotal persons initially (40 students + 1 teacher) = 41\nInitial average age = 18 years\nNew average age (teacher excluded) = 18 - 0.5 = 17.5 years\n\nFormula Used:\nTotal Age = Average Age \xD7 Number of Persons\nAge of Teacher = (Total age of 41 persons) - (Total age of 40 students)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total age initially = 41 \xD7 18 = 738 years\n\u21D2 Total age after excluding teacher = 40 \xD7 17.5 = 700 years\n\u21D2 Age of teacher = 738 - 700\n\u21D2 Age of teacher = 38 years\n\u2234 The correct answer is 38 years.\n\nAdditional Information\nWeighted Average\n\nWhen two or more groups with different averages are combined, the combined average is calculated as (n1A1 + n2A2) \xF7 (n1 + n2).\n\nConcept of Replacement\n\nWhen a person is replaced by a new person, the change in total value is: New Value - Old Value = Total Members \xD7 Change in Average.\n\nConcept of Inclusion\n\nWhen a new person joins a group, their value = Old Average + (New Total Members \xD7 Increase in Average).",
