        userTime: "00:37",
        avgTime: "00:23",
        question: "If A : B = 8 : 13, B : C = 5 : 8 and C : D = 4 : 5, then A : B : C : D is equal to:",
        options: {
          a: "20 : 50 : 105 : 119",
          b: "38 : 65 : 111 : 120",
          c: "40 : 60 : 103 : 112",
          d: "40 : 65 : 104 : 130"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nUsing the vertical and cross multiplication shortcut for continuous ratios:\n\nA = 8 \xD7 5 \xD7 4 = 160, B = 13 \xD7 5 \xD7 4 = 260\nC = 13 \xD7 8 \xD7 4 = 416, D = 13 \xD7 8 \xD7 5 = 520\nA : B : C : D = 160 : 260 : 416 : 520 \u21D2 40 : 65 : 104 : 130\n\u2234 The correct answer is 40 : 65 : 104 : 130.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nA : B = 8 : 13\nB : C = 5 : 8\nC : D = 4 : 5\n\nConcept Used:\n\nWe use the adjacent block fill method. Write the given ratios in rows and fill the empty spaces with the adjacent number in that row, then multiply the columns downwards.\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Multiply the values in each column to get the combined ratio.\n\u21D2 Column A = 8 \xD7 5 \xD7 4 = 160\n\u21D2 Column B = 13 \xD7 5 \xD7 4 = 260\n\u21D2 Column C = 13 \xD7 8 \xD7 4 = 416\n\u21D2 Column D = 13 \xD7 8 \xD7 5 = 520\n\u21D2 A : B : C : D = 160 : 260 : 416 : 520\n\u21D2 Dividing each term by 4 to simplify the ratio, we get:\n\u21D2 A : B : C : D = 40 : 65 : 104 : 130\n\u2234 The correct answer is 40 : 65 : 104 : 130.\n\nAdditional Information\nCompound Ratio\n\nWhen two or more ratios are multiplied together, it is known as a compound ratio. For ratios a : b and c : d, the compound ratio is ac : bd.\n\nDuplicate & Sub-duplicate Ratio\n\nFor a ratio a : b, its duplicate ratio is a2 : b2, and its sub-duplicate ratio is \u221Aa : \u221Ab.\n\nComponendo and Dividendo\n\nIf a : b = c : d, then by the componendo and dividendo rule, (a + b) : (a - b) = (c + d) : (c - d).",
        topic: "Ratio & Proportion",
