        userTime: "01:00",
        avgTime: "00:44",
        question: "6 persons running around a ground complete one round in 6, 10, 12, 18, 30 and 40 minutes respectively. After how much time will they meet for the first time if they started running at the same time?",
        options: {
          a: "6 hours",
          b: "5 hours",
          c: "4.5 hours",
          d: "4 hours"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nThe time taken by the runners to meet for the first time at the starting point is simply the LCM of their individual round times.\n\nRequired time = LCM(6, 10, 12, 18, 30, 40)\nRequired time = 360 minutes\nTime in hours = 360 \xF7 60 = 6 hours\n\u2234 The correct answer is 6 hours.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTimes taken by 6 persons to complete one round = 6, 10, 12, 18, 30, and 40 minutes.\n\nFormula Used:\nTime to meet again at the starting point = LCM of individual times to complete one round.\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 We need to find the Least Common Multiple (LCM) of 6, 10, 12, 18, 30, and 40.\n\u21D2 Prime factorization of 6 = 2 \xD7 3\n\u21D2 Prime factorization of 10 = 2 \xD7 5\n\u21D2 Prime factorization of 12 = 22 \xD7 3\n\u21D2 Prime factorization of 18 = 2 \xD7 32\n\u21D2 Prime factorization of 30 = 2 \xD7 3 \xD7 5\n\u21D2 Prime factorization of 40 = 23 \xD7 5\n\u21D2 LCM is the product of the highest powers of all prime factors involved.\n\u21D2 Highest power of 2 = 23\n\u21D2 Highest power of 3 = 32\n\u21D2 Highest power of 5 = 5\n\u21D2 LCM = 23 \xD7 32 \xD7 5 = 8 \xD7 9 \xD7 5 = 360 minutes.\n\u21D2 Converting the time into hours = 360 \xF7 60 = 6 hours.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 6 hours.\n\nAdditional Information\nMeeting at the Starting Point on Circular Track\n\nWhen multiple people are moving around a circular track starting at the same time and place, they meet at the starting point simultaneously after a time equal to the LCM of the times taken by each to complete one round independently.\n\nFirst Meeting Anywhere on Circular Track\n\nIf two runners move in the same direction, the time to meet for the first time anywhere on the track = Track Length \xF7 (S1 - S2). If they move in opposite directions, Time to meet = Track Length \xF7 (S1 + S2).\n\nLCM Formula for Fractions\n\nIf the individual completion times are given as fractions, you can find the meeting time using: LCM of fractions = (LCM of Numerators) \xF7 (HCF of Denominators).",
