        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nSide of the square base = Base Perimeter \xF7 4 = 36 \xF7 4 = 9 inches.\nHeight of the pyramid = Side of the base = 9 inches.\nVolume of right pyramid = (1/3) \xD7 Base Area \xD7 Height\nVolume = (1/3) \xD7 (9 \xD7 9) \xD7 9 = 243 cubic inches.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 243 cubic inches.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nPerimeter of the square base = 36 inches.\nHeight of the pyramid (h) = Side length of the square base (a).\n\nFormula Used:\nPerimeter of square = 4 \xD7 a\nArea of square base = a2\nVolume of a pyramid (V) = (1/3) \xD7 Base Area \xD7 Height (h)\n\nCalculation:\n\u21D2 4 \xD7 a = 36\n\u21D2 a = 36 \xF7 4 = 9 inches\n\u21D2 Height (h) = a = 9 inches\n\u21D2 Area of square base = 9 \xD7 9 = 81 sq. inches\n\u21D2 Volume (V) = (1/3) \xD7 81 \xD7 9\n\u21D2 Volume = 27 \xD7 9\n\u21D2 Volume = 243 cubic inches\n\u2234 The correct answer is 243 cubic inches.\n\nAdditional Information\nRight Pyramid\n\nA 3D shape where the apex aligns directly above the geometric center of the base. In a regular right pyramid, all lateral faces are identical isosceles triangles.\n\nSlant Height (l)\n\nThe altitude of the triangular faces on the side. For a square pyramid of base length 'a' and height 'h', the slant height is determined using the Pythagorean theorem: l = \u221A(h2 + (a \xF7 2)2).\n\nTotal Surface Area (TSA)\nTSA = Base Area + Lateral Surface Area = a2 + 2 \xD7 a \xD7 l",
