        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nWhen a solid object is melted to form another, the total volume remains conserved.\n\n\u21D2 Volume of Sphere = Volume of Cone\n\u21D2 (4/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 (3)\xB3 = (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2 \xD7 (r / 2)\n\u21D2 4 \xD7 27 = r3 / 2\n\u21D2 r3 = 216 \u21D2 r = 6 cm\n\u2234 The correct answer is 6 cm.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nRadius of the sphere\n(R) = 3 cm\nLet the radius of the cone be r cm.\nHeight of the cone (h) = r / 2\n\nFormula Used:\nVolume of Sphere = (4/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 R3\nVolume of Cone = (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2 \xD7 h\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Volume of Cone = Volume of Sphere\n\u21D2 (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2 \xD7 h = (4/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 R3\n\nSubstituting the given values into the equation:\n\n\u21D2 (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2 \xD7 (r / 2) = (4/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 33\n\nCanceling out (\u03C0 / 3) from both sides of the equation:\n\n\u21D2 r3 / 2 = 4 \xD7 27\n\u21D2 r3 / 2 = 108\n\u21D2 r3 = 216\n\u21D2 r = (216)1/3\n\u21D2 r = 6 cm\n\u2234 The correct answer is 6 cm.\n\nAdditional Information\nPrinciple of Melting and Recasting\n\nWhenever a 3D solid figure is melted and converted into another solid, the initial volume is exactly equal to the final volume regardless of the shape.\n\nTotal Surface Area of Cone\n\nThe total surface area of a cone involves the curved area plus the circular base area: TSA = \u03C0 \xD7 r \xD7 l + \u03C0 \xD7 r2, where l is the slant height.\n\nSurface Area of Sphere\n\nA complete sphere has a continuous curved surface with an area given by the formula: SA = 4 \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 R2.",
