        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nUsing the MDH rule for compound proportion directly:\n\n(M1 \xD7 D1 \xD7 H1) / W1 = (M2 \xD7 D2 \xD7 H2) / W2\n\u21D2 (15 \xD7 12 \xD7 7) / 1 = (M2 \xD7 14 \xD7 9) / 3\n\u21D2 1260 = M2 \xD7 42\n\u21D2 M2 = 30\n\u2234 The correct answer is 30 men.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nCase 1: M1 = 15 men, D1 = 12 days, H1 = 7 hours, W1 = 1 unit\nCase 2: M2 = ? men, D2 = 14 days, H2 = 9 hours, W2 = 3 units\n\nFormula Used:\nChain Rule: (M1 \xD7 D1 \xD7 H1) / W1 = (M2 \xD7 D2 \xD7 H2) / W2\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 (15 \xD7 12 \xD7 7) / 1 = (M2 \xD7 14 \xD7 9) / 3\n\u21D2 1260 = (M2 \xD7 126) / 3\n\u21D2 1260 = M2 \xD7 42\n\u21D2 M2 = 1260 \xF7 42\n\u21D2 M2 = 30\n\u2234 The correct answer is 30 men.\n\nAdditional Information\nChain Rule (MDH Rule)\n\nUsed when multiple variables affect the total work. Formula: (M1 \xD7 D1 \xD7 H1 \xD7 E1) / W1 = (M2 \xD7 D2 \xD7 H2 \xD7 E2) / W2, where M is Men, D is Days, H is Hours, E is Efficiency, and W is Work done or Wages earned.\n\nWork and Wages\n\nWhen multiple workers complete a job together, the total wages are divided strictly in the ratio of the actual work done by each individual. If they work for the same number of days, wages are distributed in the ratio of their efficiencies.\n\nTime and Efficiency Ratio\n\nEfficiency is inversely proportional to the time taken to complete the work. If the efficiency ratio of person A to person B is x:y, then the ratio of time taken by them to complete the same work is y:x.",
