        status: "Correct (Slow)",
        chosenOption: "D",
        correctOption: "D",
        userTime: "00:38",
        avgTime: "00:27",
        question: "What is the value of $\\left(\\frac{1 + \\sec^2 A}{1 + \\cos^2 A}\\right) \\times \\left(\\frac{1 + \\sin^2 A}{1 + \\operatorname{cosec}^2 A}\\right)$?",
        options: {
          a: "cos\xB2A",
          b: "cosec\xB2A",
          c: "sec\xB2A",
          d: "tan\xB2A"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nAssume an angle, say A = 45\xB0, to quickly evaluate the expression.\n\u21D2 sec245\xB0 = 2, cos245\xB0 = 1/2, sin245\xB0 = 1/2, cosec245\xB0 = 2\n\u21D2 Expression = [(1 + 2) \xF7 (1 + 1/2)] \xD7 [(1 + 1/2) \xF7 (1 + 2)]\n\u21D2 Expression = (3 \xF7 3/2) \xD7 (3/2 \xF7 3) = 2 \xD7 1/2 = 1\nFrom the given options, tan245\xB0 = (1)\xB2 = 1.\n\u2234 The correct answer is tan\xB2A.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nExpression = [(1 + sec\xB2A) \xF7 (1 + cos\xB2A)] \xD7 [(1 + sin\xB2A) \xF7 (1 + cosec\xB2A)]\n\nFormula Used:\nsec A = 1 / cos A, cosec A = 1 / sin A, tan A = sin A / cos A\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 First part = (1 + 1/cos\xB2A) \xF7 (1 + cos\xB2A)\n\u21D2 First part = [(cos\xB2A + 1) / cos\xB2A] \xF7 (1 + cos\xB2A) = 1 / cos\xB2A\n\u21D2 Second part = (1 + sin\xB2A) \xF7 (1 + 1/sin\xB2A)\n\u21D2 Second part = (1 + sin\xB2A) \xF7 [(sin\xB2A + 1) / sin\xB2A] = sin\xB2A\n\u21D2 Complete Expression = (1 / cos\xB2A) \xD7 sin\xB2A\n\u21D2 Expression = sin\xB2A / cos\xB2A = tan\xB2A\n\u2234 The correct answer is tan\xB2A.\n\nAdditional Information\nReciprocal Trigonometric Identities\n\nFunctions that are inverted forms of each other: sec \u03B8 = 1 \xF7 cos \u03B8 and cosec \u03B8 = 1 \xF7 sin \u03B8.\n\nQuotient Identities\n\nThese identities relate tan and cot to sine and cosine: tan \u03B8 = sin \u03B8 \xF7 cos \u03B8 and cot \u03B8 = cos \u03B8 \xF7 sin \u03B8.\n\nValue Putting Technique\n\nIn the simplification of trigonometric expressions, substituting an angle like \u03B8 = 45\xB0 easily converts complex variables into numerals, aiding rapid elimination of wrong options.",
