        chosenOption: "C",
        correctOption: "C",
        userTime: "00:32",
        avgTime: "00:20",
        question: "The average age of 35 children of the class is 16 years. 15 more children joined whose average age is 14 years. What is the average age of all the 50 children together?",
        options: {
          a: "13.4 years",
          b: "14.5 years",
          c: "15.4 years",
          d: "16.5 years"
        },
        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nRatio of number of children = 35 : 15 = 7 : 3.\nLet base average be 14 years.\nDeviation of the first group from 14 = +2 years.\nNet deviation per child = (7 \xD7 2) \xF7 (7 + 3) = 14 \xF7 10 = +1.4 years.\nCombined Average = Base average + Net deviation = 14 + 1.4 = 15.4 years.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 15.4 years.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nNumber of children in group 1 = 35, Average age = 16 years.\nNumber of children in group 2 = 15, Average age = 14 years.\n\nFormula Used:\nCombined Average = (Total age of all groups) \xF7 (Total number of members)\xB35 children, Avg = 16 / 15, Avg = 14\nCombined 50 children, Avg = 15.4\nTotal Age = (35 \xD7 16) + (15 \xD7 14) = 770\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total age of 35 children = 35 \xD7 16 = 560 years\n\u21D2 Total age of 15 children = 15 \xD7 14 = 210 years\n\u21D2 Total age of 50 children = 560 + 210 = 770 years\n\u21D2 Combined Average age = 770 \xF7 50\n\u21D2 Combined Average age = 15.4 years\n\u2234 The correct answer is 15.4 years.\n\nAdditional Information\nCombined Average Formula\n\nWhen two groups of sizes n1 and n2 have averages A1 and A2 respectively, their combined average is given by: A = (n1A1 + n2A2) \xF7 (n1 + n2).\n\nDeviation Method for Averages\n\nAssume a base average and calculate the net deviation. Combined Average = Base Average + (Net Deviation \xF7 Total Items). This reduces calculation time significantly.\n\nWeighted Average Ratio Trick\n\nInstead of using the actual number of items, use the simplified ratio of the number of items in each group to calculate the combined average or net deviation.",
