        avgTime: "00:23",
        question: "A retailer bought 50 kg of Arhar Dal at a discount of 20%. Besides 2 kg dal was freely offered to him by the wholesaler at the purchase of 50 kg. Now he sells the dal at the marked price to a customer. Find the profit percentage of the retailer?",
        options: {
          a: "30%",
          b: "12%",
          c: "15%",
          d: "22%"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nLet the marked price (MP) of 1 kg dal be 10 units.\nCost Price (CP) for retailer = 50 kg \xD7 8 units (due to 20% discount) = 400 units.\nTotal quantity to sell = 50 kg + 2 kg free = 52 kg.\nSelling Price (SP) of 52 kg at MP = 52 \xD7 10 units = 520 units.\nProfit % = [(SP - CP) \xF7 CP] \xD7 100 = [(520 - 400) \xF7 400] \xD7 100 = 30%.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 30%.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nQuantity purchased by the retailer = 50 kg\nDiscount on purchase = 20%\nFree quantity received = 2 kg\n\nRetailer sells the entire dal at the marked price.\n\nFormula Used:\nProfit = Selling Price - Cost Price\nProfit % = (Profit \xF7 Cost Price) \xD7 100\n\nCalculations:\nLet the marked price of 1 kg of Arhar Dal be \u20B9100.\n\u21D2 Marked Price of 50 kg = 50 \xD7 100 = \u20B95000\n\u21D2 Discount given to the retailer = 20% of 5000 = \u20B91000\n\u21D2 Cost Price (CP) for the retailer = 5000 - 1000 = \u20B94000\n\u21D2 Total quantity the retailer gets = 50 kg + 2 kg free = 52 kg\n\u21D2 Since he sells at the marked price, Selling Price (SP) of 52 kg = 52 \xD7 100 = \u20B95200\n\u21D2 Profit earned = SP - CP = 5200 - 4000 = \u20B91200\n\u21D2 Profit % = (1200 \xF7 4000) \xD7 100\n\u21D2 Profit % = 30%\n\u2234 The correct answer is 30%.\n\nAdditional Information\nMarked Price and Discount\n\nDiscount is always calculated on the Marked Price of an article. Selling Price = Marked Price - Discount.\n\nProfit and Loss Calculation\n\nProfit and Loss are strictly calculated on the total out-of-pocket Cost Price unless specified otherwise. Profit % = (Profit \xF7 CP) \xD7 100.\n\nBuy X Get Y Free\n\nIn any promotional scheme where items are given free, the actual effective discount percentage is given by (Free Items \xF7 Total Items Received) \xD7 100.",
        topic: "Profit, Loss & Discount",
        subtopic: "Discount & Free Items (Buy X Get Y Free)",
        conceptTested: "Profit percentage is calculated as [(Selling Price - Cost Price) / Cost Price] \xD7 100, where Cost Price accounts for discounts received on bulk purchases.",
