        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nLet the total marks of both students be 100%.\n\nOne student scored 56%, so the other student scored (100% - 56%) = 44%.\n\nDifference in percentage = 56% - 44% = 12%.\n\nAccording to the question, this 12% difference is equal to 9 marks.\n\n12% = 9 marks \u21D2 1% = 0.75 marks.\nMarks obtained = 56 \xD7 0.75 = 42 and 44 \xD7 0.75 = 33.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 33 and 42.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven: Difference in marks = 9. Student 1 marks = 56% of total.\nFormula: Value = Percentage \xD7 Total Sum\n\u21D2 Let the marks of the two students be x and (x - 9).\n\u21D2 Sum of their marks = x + (x - 9) = 2x - 9.\n\u21D2 According to the condition: x = 56% \xD7 (2x - 9)\n\u21D2 x = (56 / 100) \xD7 (2x - 9)\n\u21D2 100x = 112x - 504\n\u21D2 112x - 100x = 504\n\u21D2 12x = 504\n\u21D2 x = 504 \xF7 12 = 42 marks.\n\u21D2 Second student marks = 42 - 9 = 33 marks.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 33 and 42.\n\nAdditional Information\nPercentage to Ratio Conversion\n\nCalculating results using ratios is often faster. Here, the ratio of marks is 56 : 44 which simplifies to 14 : 11. The difference of 3 units corresponds to the 9 marks given.\n\nComplementary Percentages\n\nIf one part is x%, the other part of the whole is always (100 - x)%. This is a fundamental concept in data interpretation and percentage problems.\n\nBase Value in Percentages\n\nAlways identify the base on which the percentage is calculated. In this problem, the base is the sum of marks of both students.",
