        userTime: "01:15",
        avgTime: "00:48",
        question: "If \\((5x + 3y)^3 + (5x - 3y)^3 = 10(Cx^3 + Dxy^2)\\), then find the value of \\(2\\sqrt{C} - D\\) :",
        options: {
          a: "-19",
          b: "-17",
          c: "17",
          d: "23"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nUsing identity: (a + b)\xB3 + (a - b)\xB3 = 2a(a2 + 3b2)\nSubstitute a = 5x and b = 3y: 2(5x)((5x)\xB2 + 3(3y)\xB2)\n= 10x(25x2 + 27y2) = 250x3 + 270xy2\nComparing with 10(Cx3 + Dxy2) \u21D2 C = 25, D = 27\n2\u221AC - D = 2\u221A25 - 27 = 10 - 27 = -17\n\u2234 The correct answer is -17.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven: (5x + 3y)\xB3 + (5x - 3y)\xB3 = 10(Cx3 + Dxy2)\nFormula Used: (A + B)\xB3 + (A - B)\xB3 = 2A3 + 6AB2\n\u21D2 Let A = 5x and B = 3y\n\u21D2 LHS = 2(5x)\xB3 + 6(5x)(3y)\xB2\n\u21D2 LHS = 2(125x3) + 30x(9y2)\n\u21D2 LHS = 250x3 + 270xy2\n\u21D2 10(Cx3 + Dxy2) = 250x3 + 270xy2\n\u21D2 Cx3 + Dxy2 = 25x3 + 27xy2\n\u21D2 C = 25 and D = 27\n\u21D2 Required value = 2\u221AC - D\n\u21D2 2\u221A25 - 27 = 2 \xD7 5 - 27\n\u21D2 10 - 27 = -17\n\u2234 The correct answer is -17.\n\nAdditional Information\nDifference of Cubes Expansion\n(a + b)\xB3 - (a - b)\xB3 = 2b3 + 6a2b = 2b(b2 + 3a2)\n\nSum and Difference of Two Cubes\n\na3 + b3 = (a + b)(a2 - ab + b2) and a3 - b3 = (a - b)(a2 + ab + b2)\n\nStandard Algebraic Identity\n\n(a + b)\xB3 = a3 + b3 + 3ab(a + b) and (a - b)\xB3 = a3 - b3 - 3ab(a - b)",
        topic: "Algebra",
        subtopic: "Algebraic Identities & Cubes",
        conceptTested: "Sum of cubes expansion identity: (a + b)^3 + (a - b)^3 = 2a(a^2 + 3b^2).",
