        userTime: "00:31",
        avgTime: "00:22",
        question: "Sudarsan and Abraham appear for an interview for two vacancies. The probability of Sudarsan's selection is 1/3 and that of Abraham's selection is 1/5. Find the probability that none of them be selected.",
        options: {
          a: "8/15",
          b: "4/15",
          c: "2/15",
          d: "1/15"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nProbability of Sudarsan not being selected = 1 - 1/3 = 2/3\nProbability of Abraham not being selected = 1 - 1/5 = 4/5\n\nSince the events are independent, the required probability is the product of individual non-selection probabilities.\n\nRequired Probability = 2/3 \xD7 4/5 = 8/15\n\u2234 The correct answer is 8/15.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nProbability of Sudarsan's selection P(S) = 1/3\nProbability of Abraham's selection P(A) = 1/5\n\nFormula Used:\nFor independent events A and B, P(none selected) = P(A') \xD7 P(B'), where P(X') = 1 - P(X).\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Probability that Sudarsan is not selected P(S') = 1 - 1/3 = 2/3\n\u21D2 Probability that Abraham is not selected P(A') = 1 - 1/5 = 4/5\n\u21D2 Probability (None selected) = P(S') \xD7 P(A')\n\u21D2 Required Probability = (2/3) \xD7 (4/5)\n\u21D2 Required Probability = (2 \xD7 4) / (3 \xD7 5) = 8/15\n\u2234 The correct answer is 8/15.\n\nAdditional Information\nIndependent Events\n\nTwo events are independent if the occurrence of one does not affect the occurrence of the other. For such events, P(A and B) = P(A) \xD7 P(B).\n\nComplementary Events\n\nThe probability of an event not occurring is 1 minus the probability of the event occurring: P(A') = 1 - P(A).\n\nAt Least One Selected\n\nThe probability that at least one of them is selected is given by 1 - P(None selected). In this case, 1 - 8/15 = 7/15.",
        topic: "Probability",
