        question: "\\(\\frac{1}{7}\\) of a number equal to \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\) of another number. What is the ratio of the first number to the second number?",
        options: {
          a: "15 \u2236 28",
          b: "5 \u2236 21",
          c: "14 \u2236 5",
          d: "5 \u2236 14"
        },
        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nLet the first number be A and the second number be B.\nGiven: (1/7) \xD7 A = (2/5) \xD7 B\nDirect ratio A : B = (Numerator of B \xD7 Denominator of A) : (Denominator of B \xD7 Numerator of A)\nA : B = (2 \xD7 7) : (5 \xD7 1) = 14 : 5\n\u2234 The correct answer is 14 : 5.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nFirst number (let it be x) \xD7 1/7 = Second number (let it be y) \xD7 2/5\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 (1/7) \xD7 x = (2/5) \xD7 y\n\u21D2 x/7 = 2y/5\n\nBy cross-multiplying the denominators:\n\n\u21D2 5 \xD7 x = 7 \xD7 2y\n\u21D2 5x = 14y\n\u21D2 x / y = 14 / 5\n\u21D2 x : y = 14 : 5\n\u2234 The correct answer is 14 : 5.\n\nAdditional Information\nRatio and Proportion\n\nIf a \xD7 A = b \xD7 B, then the ratio A : B is equal to b : a. This is known as the inverse coefficient rule.\n\nCompound Ratio\n\nThe compound ratio of (a : b) and (c : d) is (ac : bd). It is found by multiplying the corresponding terms of the ratios.\n\nCross Multiplication Rule\n\nIn the equation A/B = C/D, the relationship is expressed as A \xD7 D = B \xD7 C.",
