        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nIdentify the conditional algebraic identity:\nIf $a + b + c = 0$, then $a^3 + b^3 + c^3 = 3abc$.\n\nRewrite the given equation:\n$\\Rightarrow x^{\\frac{1}{3}} - y^{\\frac{1}{3}} - z^{\\frac{1}{3}} = 0$\n\nLet $a = x^{\\frac{1}{3}}$, $b = -y^{\\frac{1}{3}}$, and $c = -z^{\\frac{1}{3}}$.\nThen $a + b + c = x^{\\frac{1}{3}} + (-y^{\\frac{1}{3}}) + (-z^{\\frac{1}{3}}) = 0$.\n\nApplying the identity $a^3 + b^3 + c^3 = 3abc$:\n$\\Rightarrow \\left(x^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\right)^3 + \\left(-y^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\right)^3 + \\left(-z^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\right)^3 = 3 \\cdot \\left(x^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\right) \\cdot \\left(-y^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\right) \\cdot \\left(-z^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\right)$\n$\\Rightarrow x - y - z = 3(xyz)^{\\frac{1}{3}}$\n\nCubing both sides:\n$\\Rightarrow (x - y - z)^3 = \\left[3(xyz)^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\right]^3 = 27xyz$\n\nSubtracting $27xyz$ from both sides:\n$\\Rightarrow (x - y - z)^3 - 27xyz = 0$\n\n\u2234 The correct answer is 0.",
