        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nStep 1: Verify the options against the sum condition (Father + Son = 45).\nStep 2: Verify the product condition 5 years ago: (F - 5) \xD7 (S - 5) = 124.\nOption (1): 36 + 9 = 45. 5 years ago: 31 \xD7 4 = 124. (Correct)\nOption (2): 40 + 5 = 45. 5 years ago: 35 \xD7 0 = 0. (Incorrect)\nOption (4): 35 + 10 = 45. 5 years ago: 30 \xD7 5 = 150. (Incorrect)\n\u2234 The correct answer is 36 years and 9 years.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nSum of present ages = 45 years\nProduct 5 years ago = 124\n\nFormula Used:\nSum: F + S = 45 \u21D2 S = 45 - F\nEquation: (F - 5) \xD7 (S - 5) = 124\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Let father present age be F and son present age be (45 - F).\n\u21D2 (F - 5) \xD7 ((45 - F) - 5) = 124\n\u21D2 (F - 5) \xD7 (40 - F) = 124\n\u21D2 40F - F2 - 200 + 5F = 124\n\u21D2 F2 - 45F + 324 = 0\n\u21D2 F2 - 36F - 9F + 324 = 0\n\u21D2 F(F - 36) - 9(F - 36) = 0\n\u21D2 (F - 36)(F - 9) = 0\n\u21D2 F = 36 or F = 9 (Father age must be 36)\n\u21D2 Son age = 45 - 36 = 9\n\u2234 The correct answer is 36 years and 9 years.\n\nAdditional Information\nConstant Age Difference\n\nThe difference between the ages of two people always remains constant, regardless of the number of years that pass.\n\nSum of Ages after n Years\n\nIf the current sum of ages of k people is S, then after n years, the new sum will be S + (n \xD7 k).\n\nNature of Roots in Age Equations\n\nIn quadratic equations derived from age problems, the product of the roots (c/a) equals the product of the ages, and the sum of roots (-b/a) equals the sum of the ages.",
