        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nTotal Distance = 35 + 45 = 80 km\nTotal Time = 15 + 25 = 40 minutes\nAverage Speed = (Total Distance \xF7 Total Time) \xD7 60\nAverage Speed = (80 \xF7 40) \xD7 60 = 2 \xD7 60 = 120 km/h\n\u2234 The correct answer is 120 km/h.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nFirst distance (d1) = 35 km, Time (t1) = 15 minutes\nSecond distance (d2) = 45 km, Time (t2) = 25 minutes\n\nFormula Used:\nAverage Speed = Total Distance \xF7 Total Time\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total distance = 35 km + 45 km = 80 km\n\u21D2 Total time = 15 min + 25 min = 40 minutes\n\u21D2 Converting time into hours: 40 minutes = 40 \xF7 60 hours = 2 \xF7 3 hours\n\u21D2 Average Speed = 80 \xF7 (2/3)\n\u21D2 Average Speed = 80 \xD7 (3/2)\n\u21D2 Average Speed = 40 \xD7 3 = 120 km/h\n\u2234 The correct answer is 120 km/h.\n\nAdditional Information\nAverage Speed (Equal Distances)\n\nIf a car covers two equal distances at speeds x and y, the average speed is given by (2 \xD7 x \xD7 y) \xF7 (x + y).\n\nSpeed Unit Conversion\n\nTo convert km/h to m/s, multiply by 5/18. To convert m/s to km/h, multiply by 18/5.\n\nRelative Speed\n\nWhen two objects move in the same direction, relative speed = S1 - S2. When they move in opposite directions, relative speed = S1 + S2.",
