        solution: "Solution\n\nGiven:\nNumbers to compare: $(125)^{\\frac{1}{6}}$, $(11)^{\\frac{1}{3}}$, $(12)^{\\frac{1}{6}}$, $(5)^{\\frac{1}{4}}$\n\nShortcut Trick\nTake the LCM of all denominator powers $(6, 3, 6, 4)$:\n$\\text{LCM}(6, 3, 6, 4) = 12$\n\nRaise each number to the power of 12:\n1. $\\left[(125)^{\\frac{1}{6}}\\right]^{12} = (125)^2 = 15625$\n2. $\\left[(11)^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\right]^{12} = (11)^4 = 14641$ ... wait, $(125)^2 = 15625 > 14641$,\n   also $(125)^{1/6} = (5^3)^{1/6} = 5^{1/2} = \\sqrt{5} \\approx 2.236$\n   $(11)^{1/3} \\approx 2.2239$\n   $(12)^{1/6} \\approx 1.513$\n   $(5)^{1/4} \\approx 1.495$\n\n\u2234 The largest number is $(11)^{\\frac{1}{3}}$ or $(125)^{\\frac{1}{6}}$.",
