        question: "If $x + \\frac{1}{x} = 1 - \\sqrt{2}$, then find the value of $x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3}$.",
        options: {
          a: "4 - 2\\sqrt{2}",
          b: "2 - 2\\sqrt{2}",
          c: "2\\sqrt{2} - 4",
          d: "4 + 2\\sqrt{2}"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nIf x + 1/x = k, then x\xB3 + 1/x\xB3 = k(k\xB2 - 3).\nGiven k = 1 - \u221A2, we first find k\xB2 = (1 - \u221A2)2 = 3 - 2\u221A2.\nThen, k\xB2 - 3 = 3 - 2\u221A2 - 3 = -2\u221A2.\nNow multiply by k: (1 - \u221A2) \xD7 (-2\u221A2) = -2\u221A2 + 4 = 4 - 2\u221A2.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 4 - 2\u221A2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nx + 1/x = 1 - \u221A2\n\nFormula Used:\n(a + b)\xB3 = a\xB3 + b\xB3 + 3ab(a + b)\n\u21D2 x\xB3 + 1/x\xB3 = (x + 1/x)\xB3 - 3(x + 1/x)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Let x + 1/x = k = 1 - \u221A2\n\u21D2 x\xB3 + 1/x\xB3 = k\xB3 - 3k = k(k\xB2 - 3)\n\u21D2 Now, squaring both sides of k = 1 - \u221A2\n\u21D2 k\xB2 = 12 + (\u221A2)2 - 2 \xD7 1 \xD7 \u221A2\n\u21D2 k\xB2 = 1 + 2 - 2\u221A2 = 3 - 2\u221A2\n\u21D2 Now compute the term (k\xB2 - 3):\n\u21D2 k\xB2 - 3 = (3 - 2\u221A2) - 3 = -2\u221A2\n\u21D2 Substitute the values back into the expression k(k\xB2 - 3):\n\u21D2 x\xB3 + 1/x\xB3 = (1 - \u221A2) \xD7 (-2\u221A2)\n\u21D2 x\xB3 + 1/x\xB3 = (1 \xD7 -2\u221A2) - (\u221A2 \xD7 -2\u221A2)\n\u21D2 x\xB3 + 1/x\xB3 = -2\u221A2 - (-4) = 4 - 2\u221A2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 4 - 2\u221A2.\n\nAdditional Information\nCube of a Binomial\n\nThe formula for the sum of cubes is derived from: (a + b)\xB3 = a\xB3 + b\xB3 + 3ab(a + b). Rearranging this gives a\xB3 + b\xB3 = (a + b)\xB3 - 3ab(a + b).\n\nAlgebraic Identities for Squares\n\nIf x + 1/x = k, then x\xB2 + 1/x\xB2 = k\xB2 - 2. This identity is extremely useful for stepping up to higher even powers directly.\n\nAlgebraic Identities for Differences\n\nIf x - 1/x = k, then the corresponding difference formulas are x\xB3 - 1/x\xB3 = k\xB3 + 3k, and x\xB2 + 1/x\xB2 = k\xB2 + 2.",
