        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nL + B = Perimeter \xF7 2 = 34 \xF7 2 = 17 m\nArea of Rectangle = L \xD7 B = 60 m\xB2\nDiagonal of Rectangle (D) = \u221A(L\xB2 + B\xB2)\nArea of Square = D\xB2 = L\xB2 + B\xB2 = (L + B)\xB2 - 2 \xD7 L \xD7 B\nArea = 172 - 2 \xD7 60 = 289 - 120 = 169 m\xB2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 169 m\xB2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nArea of rectangular room = 60 m\xB2\nPerimeter of rectangular room = 34 m\nSide of the square = Diagonal of the rectangular room\n\nFormula Used:\nPerimeter of rectangle = 2 \xD7 (L + B)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 2 \xD7 (L + B) = 34\n\u21D2 L + B = 17\n\u21D2 L \xD7 B = 60\n\u21D2 Diagonal of rectangle = \u221A(L\xB2 + B\xB2)\n\u21D2 Side of square = \u221A(L\xB2 + B\xB2)\n\u21D2 Area of square = L\xB2 + B\xB2\n\u21D2 We know that (L + B)\xB2 = L\xB2 + B\xB2 + 2 \xD7 L \xD7 B\n\u21D2 L\xB2 + B\xB2 = 172 - 2 \xD7 60\n\u21D2 Area of square = 289 - 120 = 169 m\xB2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 169 m\xB2.\n\nAdditional Information\nAlgebraic Identities\n\nThe expansion formula (a + b)\xB2 = a\xB2 + b\xB2 + 2 \xD7 a \xD7 b is heavily utilized in geometry to directly deduce sum of squares or diagonals without having to find the precise values of the individual side lengths.\n\nProperties of a Rectangle\n\nOpposite sides are parallel and strictly equal in length. All interior angles are equal to 90\xB0, and diagonals are equal in length and bisect each other.\n\nProperties of a Square\n\nAll four sides are equal, making the area simply square of its side. Both diagonals are precisely equal, intersect perpendicularly at 90\xB0, and have a total length of a\u221A2.",
