        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nWhen the total sum and difference of two values are given, the larger value is half of their sum.\n\nPrice of Bread = (Total Cost + Difference) \xF7 2\nPrice of Bread = (75.50 + 25) \xF7 2\nPrice of Bread = 100.50 \xF7 2 = 50.25\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 50.25.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal cost of Bread and Jam = Rs. 75.50\nDifference in cost (Bread is more expensive than Jam) = Rs. 25\nLet the price of the Jam be x.\nThen, the price of the Bread = x + 25\n\nJam (x)\n\nBread (x + 25)\n\nTotal Cost = 75.50\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total Cost = Price of Jam + Price of Bread\n\u21D2 x + (x + 25) = 75.50\n\u21D2 2x + 25 = 75.50\n\u21D2 2x = 75.50 - 25\n\u21D2 2x = 50.50\n\u21D2 x = 50.50 \xF7 2\n\u21D2 x = 25.25\n\u21D2 Price of Bread = x + 25 = 25.25 + 25 = 50.25\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 50.25.\n\nAdditional Information\nSum and Difference Formula\n\nIf the sum of two numbers is S and their difference is D, the larger number is (S + D) \xF7 2 and the smaller number is (S - D) \xF7 2.\n\nLinear Equations in One Variable\n\nA linear equation is an algebraic equation where the highest exponent of the variable is exactly 1. It represents a straight line when plotted on a graph and is easily solved by isolating the unknown quantity on one side.",
