        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal time: A = 15 days, B = 10 days. Total work = LCM(15, 10) = 30 units.\nEfficiencies: A = 2, B = 3. Together they did (2 + 3) \xD7 4 = 20 units in 4 days.\nRemaining work = 30 - 20 = 10 units, completed by C in 6 days \u2192 C's efficiency = 10 \xF7 6 = 5/3 units/day.\nTarget work = 70% of 30 = 21 units. Combined efficiency of B and C = 3 + 5/3 = 14/3 units/day.\nTime taken by (B + C) = 21 \xF7 (14/3) = (21 \xD7 3) \xF7 14 = 41\u20442 days.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 41\u20442 days.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nA's time for complete work = 6 \xD7 (5/2) = 15 days\nB's time for complete work = 3 \xD7 (100/30) = 10 days\nLet Total Work = LCM(15, 10) = 30 units.\n\nPerson Days Total Work Efficiency\n\nA 15 30 30 \xF7 15 = 2\nB 10 30 \xF7 10 = 3\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Work done by (A + B) in 4 days = (2 + 3) \xD7 4 = 20 units\n\u21D2 Remaining work = 30 - 20 = 10 units\n\u21D2 C completes 10 units in 6 days \u2192 Efficiency of C = 10 \xF7 6 = 5/3 units/day\n\u21D2 Target work = 70% of 30 units = (70 \xF7 100) \xD7 30 = 21 units\n\u21D2 Combined efficiency of (B + C) = 3 + (5/3) = 14/3 units/day\n\u21D2 Time taken by (B + C) = Target work \xF7 Combined Efficiency\n\u21D2 Time taken = 21 \xF7 (14/3) = (21 \xD7 3) \xF7 14 = 9/2 = 41\u20442 days\n\u2234 The correct answer is 41\u20442 days.\n\nAdditional Information\nTotal Work and Efficiency\n\nEfficiency is inversely proportional to time. Total Work = Efficiency \xD7 Time Taken.\n\nPipes and Cisterns Concept\n\nWorks similarly to Time and Work, but involves negative efficiency for emptying pipes which drain the total volume.\n\nWages and Work\n\nWages are always distributed in the ratio of the total work done by each individual, not strictly by their time taken or days spent.",
