        status: "Correct (Slow)",
        chosenOption: "B",
        correctOption: "B",
        userTime: "00:38",
        avgTime: "00:22",
        question: "Two girls travel in opposite directions, the former from 'A' at a speed of 25 km/h and takes 20 hours to reach her destination 'B'. The latter from 'B' takes 25 hours to reach her destination 'A' meeting the former on her way. What is the latter's speed?",
        options: {
          a: "25 km/h",
          b: "20 km/h",
          c: "15 km/h",
          d: "18 km/h"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nWhen the total distance traveled by two bodies is the same, their speed is inversely proportional to the time taken.\n\nS1 / S\xB2 = T\xB2 / T1\n25 / S\xB2 = 25 / 20\nS\xB2 = 20 km/h\n\u2234 The correct answer is 20 km/h.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nSpeed of the former girl (S1) = 25 km/h\nTime taken by the former girl (T1) = 20 hours\nTime taken by the latter girl (T\xB2) = 25 hours\n\nFormula Used:\nDistance = Speed \xD7 Time\nSpeed = Distance \xF7 Time\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total Distance from A to B = S1 \xD7 T1\n\u21D2 Distance = 25 \xD7 20 = 500 km\n\u21D2 The latter girl covers the exact same distance of 500 km from B to A.\n\u21D2 Speed of the latter girl (S\xB2) = Distance \xF7 T\xB2\n\u21D2 S\xB2 = 500 \xF7 25\n\u21D2 S\xB2 = 20 km/h\n\u2234 The correct answer is 20 km/h.\n\nAdditional Information\nConstant Distance Rule\n\nWhen the distance is constant, the ratio of speeds of two traveling bodies is inversely proportional to the ratio of the times taken (S1 : S\xB2 = T\xB2 : T1).\n\nRelative Speed\n\nWhen two objects travel in opposite directions towards each other, their relative speed is the sum of their individual speeds (S1 + S\xB2). The meeting time depends strictly on their total relative speed.\n\nAverage Speed\n\nIf a certain distance is covered at speed x and the same distance is returned at speed y, the average speed for the whole journey is given by (2xy) \xF7 (x + y).",
