        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nLet the assumed average be 70.\nNet deviation from assumed average = (+8) + (+5) + (-2) + (-6) + (-12) = -7\nDeviation per subject = -7 \xF7 5 = -1.4\nActual Average = 70 - 1.4 = 68.6 marks\n\u2234 The correct answer is 68.6 marks.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nMarks obtained by S in five subjects: Hindi = 78, English = 75, Chemistry = 68, Physics = 64, Mathematics = 58\n\nFormula Used:\nAverage = Sum of all observations \xF7 Total number of observations\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Sum of marks = 78 + 75 + 68 + 64 + 58 = 343\n\u21D2 Total subjects = 5\n\u21D2 Average marks = 343 \xF7 5\n\u21D2 Average marks = 68.6\n\u2234 The correct answer is 68.6 marks.\n\nAdditional Information\nDeviation Method for Averages\n\nIt simplifies large calculations by selecting an assumed mean and finding the net difference of all actual values from it. True Average = Assumed Mean + (Sum of Deviations \xF7 Number of Values).\n\nWeighted Average\n\nUsed when items have different counts or importance. Formula: Aw = (w1 \xD7 x1 + w\xB2 \xD7 x\xB2 + ...) \xF7 (w1 + w\xB2 + ...).\n\nCombined Average\n\nIf group 1 has n1 items with average A1, and group 2 has n\xB2 items with average A\xB2, then the Combined Average = (n1 \xD7 A1 + n\xB2 \xD7 A\xB2) \xF7 (n1 + n\xB2).",
