        avgTime: "00:25",
        question: "Two cards are drawn successively without replacement from a well-shuffled pack of 52 cards. The probability of drawing two aces is",
        options: {
          a: "3/223",
          b: "1/13",
          c: "4/223",
          d: "1/221"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nProbability of the first card being an ace = 4/52 = 1/13.\nSince the first card is not replaced, remaining cards = 51 and remaining aces = 3.\nProbability of the second card being an ace = 3/51 = 1/17.\nTotal probability = (1/13) \xD7 (1/17) = 1/221.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1/221.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal number of cards in a well - shuffled pack = 52\nTotal number of aces in the pack = 4\nNumber of cards drawn successively without replacement = 2\n\nFormula Used:\nProbability = Number of Favorable Outcomes \xF7 Total Number of Possible Outcomes\nNumber of ways to choose r items from n items = nCr = n! \xF7 [r! \xD7 (n - r)!]\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total ways to draw 2 cards from 52 cards = 52C\xB2\n\u21D2 52C\xB2 = (52 \xD7 51) \xF7 (2 \xD7 1) = 26 \xD7 51 = 1326\n\u21D2 Favorable ways to draw 2 aces from 4 aces = 4C\xB2\n\u21D2 4C\xB2 = (4 \xD7 3) \xF7 (2 \xD7 1) = 2 \xD7 3 = 6\n\u21D2 Probability of drawing two aces = Favorable ways \xF7 Total ways\n\u21D2 Probability = 6 \xF7 1326\n\u21D2 Probability = 1/221\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1/221.\n\nAdditional Information\nIndependent Events (With Replacement)\n\nIf the first card is replaced before drawing the second, the events are independent. The probability formula is P(A and B) = P(A) \xD7 P(B).\n\nDependent Events (Without Replacement)\n\nIf the card is not replaced, the second draw depends on the first draw's outcome. The formula is P(A and B) = P(A) \xD7 P(B|A).\n\nStandard Deck of Cards\n\nA standard deck contains 52 cards divided into 4 suits (Hearts, Diamonds, Clubs, Spades) of 13 cards each. There are 4 Aces in total, one in each suit.",
