        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nDownstream speed (D) = 65 \xF7 5 = 13 km/h\nUpstream speed (U) = 65 \xF7 13 = 5 km/h\nSpeed of boat in still water = (D + U) \xF7 2\n\u21D2 (13 + 5) \xF7 2 = 9 km/h\n\u2234 The correct answer is 9 km/h.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nDistance covered downstream = 65 km\nTime taken downstream = 5 hours\nDistance covered upstream = 65 km\nTime taken upstream = 13 hours\n\nFormula Used:\nSpeed = Distance \xF7 Time\nSpeed of boat in still water = (Downstream Speed + Upstream Speed) \xF7 2\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Downstream Speed = 65 \xF7 5 = 13 km/h\n\u21D2 Upstream Speed = 65 \xF7 13 = 5 km/h\n\u21D2 Speed of boat in still water = (13 + 5) \xF7 2\n\u21D2 Speed of boat in still water = 18 \xF7 2 = 9 km/h\n\u2234 The correct answer is 9 km/h.\n\nAdditional Information\nSpeed of Stream\n\nIt is the speed at which the river flows. Formula: Speed of stream = (Downstream speed - Upstream speed) \xF7 2.\n\nDownstream Speed\n\nWhen a boat travels in the direction of the flow of the stream. Formula: Downstream speed = Speed of boat + Speed of stream.\n\nUpstream Speed\n\nWhen a boat travels against the direction of the flow of the stream. Formula: Upstream speed = Speed of boat - Speed of stream.",
