        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nDistance covered by Train 1 from 6:00 A.M. to 7:00 A.M. = 50 km/h \xD7 1 hr = 50 km.\nRemaining distance at 7:00 A.M. = 275 - 50 = 225 km.\nRelative speed (opposite directions) = 50 + 62.5 = 112.5 km/h.\nTime to meet = 225 \xF7 112.5 = 2 hours.\nMeeting time = 7:00 A.M. + 2 hours = 09:00 A.M.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 09:00 A.M.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal distance between station A and station B = 275 km\nSpeed of Train 1 = 50 km/h, starting time = 6:00 A.M.\nSpeed of Train 2 = 62.5 km/h, starting time = 7:00 A.M.\n\nFormula Used:\nDistance = Speed \xD7 Time\nRelative Speed (when moving in opposite directions) = S1 + S\xB2\nTime = Distance \xF7 Relative Speed\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Distance covered by Train 1 in 1 hour (from 6:00 A.M. to 7:00 A.M.) = 50 \xD7 1 = 50 km\n\u21D2 Remaining distance between the two trains at 7:00 A.M. = 275 - 50 = 225 km\n\u21D2 Relative speed of the trains = 50 + 62.5 = 112.5 km/h\n\u21D2 Time required to meet after 7:00 A.M. = 225 \xF7 112.5 = 2 hours\n\u21D2 Therefore, they will meet 2 hours after 7:00 A.M.\n\u21D2 Meeting time = 7:00 A.M. + 2 hours = 09:00 A.M.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 09:00 A.M.\n\nAdditional Information\nRelative Speed (Opposite Directions)\n\nWhen two bodies move towards each other, their relative speed is the sum of their individual speeds: Srel = S1 + S\xB2.\n\nRelative Speed (Same Direction)\n\nWhen two bodies move in the same direction, their relative speed is the difference of their individual speeds: Srel = |S1 - S2|.\n\nAverage Speed\n\nIf equal distances are covered at different speeds x and y, the average speed for the whole journey is given by (2 \xD7 x \xD7 y) \xF7 (x + y).",
        topic: "Trains",
        subtopic: "Relative Speed & Delayed Starts",
        conceptTested: "Time to meet after simultaneous motion = Remaining Distance \xF7 Sum of Speeds (Relative Speed)",
