        platform: "Testbook",
        status: "Correct (Slow)",
        chosenOption: "B",
        correctOption: "B",
        userTime: "01:01",
        avgTime: "00:43",
        question: "A circle is inscribed in a triangle ABC touching the sides of the triangle AB, BC and AC at D, E and F, such that AC = 10, EC = 4 and BD = 8, then find the perimeter of the triangle?",
        options: {
          a: "30",
          b: "36",
          c: "64",
          d: "25"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nLengths of tangents from an external point to a circle are equal.\n\n\u2234 AD = AF, BD = BE, and CE = CF.\nGiven EC = 4 \u21D2 CF = 4, and since AC = 10 \u21D2 AF = 10 - 4 = 6 \u21D2 AD = 6.\nGiven BD = 8 \u21D2 BE = 8.\nPerimeter of \u0394ABC = 2 \xD7 (AD + BD + CE) = 2 \xD7 (6 + 8 + 4) = 36.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 36 units.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nAC = 10, EC = 4, BD = 8\nConcept Used: Tangents drawn from an external point to a circle are equal in length.\n\nA / B\n\nC / D\n\nF / E\n\n6 / 8\n\n8 / 4\n\n4 / 6\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 From point C, tangents CE and CF are equal.\n\u21D2 CF = CE = 4\n\u21D2 We know that AC = AF + CF\n\u21D2 10 = AF + 4 \u21D2 AF = 6\n\u21D2 From point A, tangents AD and AF are equal, so AD = 6.\n\u21D2 From point B, tangents BD and BE are equal, so BE = 8.\n\u21D2 The lengths of the sides of \u0394ABC are:\n\u21D2 AB = AD + BD = 6 + 8 = 14\n\u21D2 BC = BE + EC = 8 + 4 = 12\n\u21D2 AC = 10 (Given)\n\u21D2 Perimeter of \u0394ABC = AB + BC + AC\n\u21D2 Perimeter = 14 + 12 + 10 = 36\n\u2234 The correct answer is 36 units.\n\nAdditional Information\nProperties of Tangents\n\nThe tangent at any point of a circle is perpendicular to the radius through the point of contact.\n\nTangents from External Point\n\nThe lengths of tangents drawn from an external point to a circle are exactly equal, and they subtend equal angles at the center.\n\nIncircle of a Triangle\n\nThe circle that touches all three sides of a triangle internally is called its incircle. Its center is the point of intersection of the angle bisectors of the triangle.\n\nSemi - perimeter and Inradius Relation\n\nThe area of a triangle (\u0394) is related to its inradius (r) and semi - perimeter (s) by the formula: \u0394 = r \xD7 s.",
        topic: "Geometry",
