        userTime: "01:07",
        avgTime: "00:46",
        question: "Sara\u2019s expenditure and savings are in the ratio of 5 : 1. Her income increases by 10%. If her savings increase by 8%, then by how much percentage has her expenditure increased?",
        options: {
          a: "12.2%",
          b: "10.4%",
          c: "13.4%",
          d: "14.2%"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal Income % change = (Exp Ratio \xD7 Exp % + Sav Ratio \xD7 Sav %) \xF7 Total Ratio\nLet the percentage increase in expenditure be x.\n10 = (5 \xD7 x + 1 \xD7 8) \xF7 (5 + 1)\n60 = 5x + 8\n5x = 52 \u21D2 x = 10.4\n\u2234 The correct answer is 10.4%.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nRatio of Expenditure to Savings = 5 \u2236 1\n\nIncome increases by 10%\n\nSavings increase by 8%\n\nFormula Used:\nIncome = Expenditure + Savings\nPercentage Change = (New Value - Initial Value) \xF7 Initial Value \xD7 100\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Let initial Expenditure = 500 and Savings = 100.\n\u21D2 Initial Income = 500 + 100 = 600\n\u21D2 New Income = 600 + (10% of 600) = 600 + 60 = 660\n\u21D2 New Savings = 100 + (8% of 100) = 100 + 8 = 108\n\u21D2 New Expenditure = New Income - New Savings = 660 - 108 = 552\n\u21D2 Increase in Expenditure = 552 - 500 = 52\n\u21D2 Percentage increase in Expenditure = (52 \xF7 500) \xD7 100 = 10.4%\n\u2234 The correct answer is 10.4%.\n\nAdditional Information\nIncome, Expenditure, and Savings\n\nIncome is always the sum of expenditure and savings (Income = Expenditure + Savings). The percentage change in income is distributed as a weighted average of the changes in expenditure and savings.\n\nPercentage Change\n\nCalculated as % Change = (Final Value - Initial Value) \xF7 Initial Value \xD7 100. It measures the degree of change over time.\n\nAlligation Method\n\nIt provides a shortcut to calculate the unknown percentage change using the cross - difference of ratio terms: Ratio of Exp to Sav = (Change in Sav - Change in Income) : (Change in Income - Change in Exp).",
