        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nMean proportional = \u221A(24.2 \xD7 7.2) = \u221A(174.24) = 13.2\nThird proportional = 4.22 \xF7 2.8 = 17.64 \xF7 2.8 = 6.3\nRequired Ratio = 13.2 : 6.3 = 132 : 63 = 44 : 21\n\u2234 The correct answer is 44 : 21.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nNumbers for finding the mean proportional = 24.2 and 7.2\nNumbers for finding the third proportional = 2.8 and 4.2\n\nFormula Used:\nMean proportional between a and b = \u221A(a \xD7 b)\nThird proportional c of a and b \u21D2 c = b\xB2 \xF7 a\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Mean proportional = \u221A(24.2 \xD7 7.2)\n\u21D2 Mean proportional = \u221A(242/10 \xD7 72/10)\n\u21D2 Mean proportional = \u221A(17424 / 100) = 132 / 10 = 13.2\n\u21D2 Third proportional = (4.2 \xD7 4.2) \xF7 2.8\n\u21D2 Third proportional = 17.64 \xF7 2.8 = 6.3\n\u21D2 Required Ratio = Mean proportional : Third proportional\n\u21D2 Required Ratio = 13.2 : 6.3\n\u21D2 Multiply by 10 to remove decimals = 132 : 63\n\u21D2 Divide both terms by 3 = 44 : 21\n\u2234 The correct answer is 44 : 21.\n\nAdditional Information\nMean Proportional\n\nIf three numbers a, b, and c are in continued proportion (a : b = b : c), then b is called the mean proportional between a and c. It is calculated using the formula: b = \u221A(a \xD7 c).\n\nThird Proportional\n\nIn a continued proportion of three numbers (a : b = b : c), the third term c is called the third proportional. It is calculated using the formula: c = b\xB2 \xF7 a.\n\nFourth Proportional\n\nIf four numbers a, b, c, and d are in strict proportion (a : b = c : d), then d is called the fourth proportional. It is calculated using the formula: d = (b \xD7 c) \xF7 a.",
