        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nRatio of Length to Width = 2 : 1\nSemi - perimeter = Perimeter \xF7 2 = 60 \xF7 2 = 30 cm\nSum of ratio parts = 2 + 1 = 3 parts\n3 parts = 30 cm \u21D2 1 part = 10 cm\nLength = 20 cm, Width = 10 cm\nArea = Length \xD7 Width = 20 \xD7 10 = 200 cm\xB2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 200 cm\xB2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\n\u21D2 Perimeter of the rectangle = 60 cm\n\u21D2 Length (L) = 2 \xD7 Width (W)\n\nFormula Used:\n\u21D2 Perimeter = 2 \xD7 (L + W)\n\u21D2 Area = L \xD7 W\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Perimeter = 2 \xD7 (2W + W) = 60\n\u21D2 2 \xD7 3W = 60\n\u21D2 6W = 60\n\u21D2 W = 60 \xF7 6 = 10 cm\n\u21D2 L = 2 \xD7 10 = 20 cm\n\u21D2 Area = 20 \xD7 10 = 200 cm\xB2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 200 cm\xB2.\n\nAdditional Information\nArea of a Rectangle\n\nThe area represents the region enclosed by the boundaries of a rectangle. It is calculated by Area = Length \xD7 Width.\n\nDiagonal of a Rectangle\n\nThe diagonal splits the rectangle into two congruent right - angled triangles. It is calculated using the Pythagorean theorem: Diagonal = \u221A(L\xB2 + W\xB2).\n\nProperties of a Rectangle\n\nA rectangle is a cyclic quadrilateral with four right angles where opposite sides are parallel and equal in length. The diagonals bisect each other and are of equal length.",
