        chosenOption: "D",
        correctOption: "D",
        userTime: "00:35",
        avgTime: "00:26",
        question: "A dealer offers a discount of 10% on the marked price of an article and still makes a profit of 20%. If its marked price is Rs. 800, then the cost will be",
        options: {
          a: "Rs. 1000",
          b: "Rs. 500",
          c: "Rs. 800",
          d: "Rs. 600"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nDirect ratio between Cost Price (CP) and Marked Price (MP) is: CP : MP = (100 - D%) : (100 + P%)\n\nCP : MP = (100 - 10) : (100 + 20) = 90 : 120 = 3 : 4\nSince 4 parts = Rs. 800 (Given MP), then 1 part = Rs. 200.\nTherefore, CP = 3 parts = 3 \xD7 200 = Rs. 600.\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 600.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nMarked Price (MP) = Rs. 800\nDiscount = 10%\nProfit = 20%\n\nFormula Used:\nSP = MP - Discount\nCP = SP \xD7 [100 / (100 + Profit%)]\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Selling Price (SP) after 10% discount on MP:\n\u21D2 SP = 800 - (10 / 100) \xD7 800\n\u21D2 SP = 800 - 80 = Rs. 720\n\u21D2 Dealer still makes a profit of 20% on Cost Price (CP).\n\u21D2 CP \xD7 120 / 100 = 720\n\u21D2 CP = 720 \xD7 (100 / 120)\n\u21D2 CP = 720 \xD7 (5 / 6)\n\u21D2 CP = 120 \xD7 5 = Rs. 600\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 600.\n\nAdditional Information\nMarked Price and Discount\n\nDiscount is always calculated on the Marked Price (MP) unless specified otherwise. Formula: SP = MP \xD7 (100 - D%) \xF7 100.\n\nDirect CP and MP Relationship\n\nThere is a direct relationship between Cost Price and Marked Price when profit and discount percentages are given: CP / MP = (100 - D%) / (100 + P%).\n\nSuccessive Discounts\n\nIf two successive discounts of a% and b% are given, the equivalent single discount is calculated by the formula: (a + b - ab/100)%.",
        topic: "Profit, Loss & Discount",
        subtopic: "Profit & Loss - Marked Price and Discount",
        conceptTested: "Direct relationship between Cost Price and Marked Price: CP / MP = (100 - D%) / (100 + P%)",
