        chosenOption: "A",
        correctOption: "A",
        userTime: "00:34",
        avgTime: "00:24",
        question: "When the price of an article was reduced by 20%, its sale increased by 80%. What was the net effect on the sale?",
        options: {
          a: "44% increase",
          b: "44% decrease",
          c: "66% increase",
          d: "75% increase"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nUsing the successive percentage change formula: Net Change = a + b + (a \xD7 b) \xF7 100\nHere, price decrease a = -20% and sales quantity increase b = +80%\nNet Change = -20 + 80 + (-20 \xD7 80) \xF7 100\nNet Change = 60 - 16 = +44%\nSince the result is positive, there is a 44% increase in the net sale.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 44% increase.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nReduction in price = 20%\nIncrease in sales (quantity) = 80%\n\nFormula Used:\nTotal Revenue = Price \xD7 Quantity\nPercentage Change = (New Value - Original Value) \xF7 Original Value \xD7 100\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Let the initial price of the article be 100 and the initial sales (quantity) be 100 units.\n\u21D2 Initial Total Sale (Revenue) = 100 \xD7 100 = 10000\n\u21D2 New price after 20% reduction = 100 - 20 = 80\n\u21D2 New sales quantity after 80% increase = 100 + 80 = 180 units\n\u21D2 New Total Sale (Revenue) = 80 \xD7 180 = 14400\n\u21D2 Increase in sale = 14400 - 10000 = 4400\n\u21D2 Percentage increase = (4400 \xF7 10000) \xD7 100\n\u21D2 Percentage increase = 44%\n\u2234 The correct answer is 44% increase.\n\nAdditional Information\nSuccessive Percentage Change\n\nWhen two percentage changes are applied successively on a value, the net change is given by the formula: Net % = a + b + (a \xD7 b) \xF7 100. Use negative signs for reductions and positive signs for increases.\n\nRevenue and Expenditure Concepts\n\nSince Revenue = Price \xD7 Quantity (or Expenditure = Price \xD7 Consumption), a percentage change in both components causes a compounded effect on the total value, which can be easily evaluated using the successive percentage change formula.\n\nProduct Constancy Rule\n\nIf the product of two variables is kept constant (e.g., Price \xD7 Consumption = Constant Expenditure), an x% increase in one variable requires a percentage reduction in the other by (x \xF7 (100 + x)) \xD7 100%.",
        topic: "Percentage",
