        platform: "Testbook",
        status: "Correct (Slow)",
        chosenOption: "A",
        correctOption: "A",
        userTime: "01:19",
        avgTime: "01:00",
        question: "In a business, three friends Rina, Mina and Tina invest their capital in the ratio of \\(\\frac{1}{3}:\\frac{1}{4}:\\frac{1}{16}\\). If the difference in the profit earned by Rina and Tina is Rs. 10101, then find the profit earned by Mina. (in Rs.)",
        options: {
          a: "Rs. 9324",
          b: "Rs. 777",
          c: "Rs. 13324",
          d: "None of the above"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nMultiply the profit ratio^(1/3) : 1/4 : 1/16 by their LCM 48 to convert it to integers.\nSimplified profit ratio of Rina, Mina, and Tina = 16 : 12 : 3.\nDifference in ratio units between Rina and Tina = 16 - 3 = 13 units.\n13 units = 10101 \u21D2 1 unit = 777.\nMina's profit = 12 units = 12 \xD7 777 = 9324.\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 9324.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nInvestment ratio of Rina, Mina, and Tina = 1/3 : 1/4 : 1/16\nDifference in profit of Rina and Tina = Rs. 10101\n\nFormula Used:\nProfit Ratio = Investment Ratio (when time periods are equal)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 LCM of the denominators (3, 4, 16) = 48\n\u21D2 Multiplying the investment ratio by 48\n\u21D2 Rina : Mina : Tina = (1/3) \xD7 48 : (1/4) \xD7 48 : (1/16) \xD7 48\n\u21D2 Profit Ratio = 16 : 12 : 3\n\u21D2 Let the profits of Rina, Mina, and Tina be 16x, 12x, and 3x respectively.\n\u21D2 Difference between Rina's and Tina's profit = 16x - 3x\n\u21D2 13x = 10101\n\u21D2 x = 10101 \xF7 13\n\u21D2 x = 777\n\u21D2 Mina's profit = 12x\n\u21D2 Mina's profit = 12 \xD7 777 = 9324\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 9324.\n\nAdditional Information\nSimple Partnership\n\nWhen investments are made for the same time period, the profit is distributed entirely in the ratio of the capitals invested: Profit Ratio = C1 : C\xB2 : C\xB3.\n\nCompound Partnership\n\nWhen investments are made for different time periods, the profit is distributed based on the product of the capital and time: Profit Ratio = (C1 \xD7 T1) : (C\xB2 \xD7 T\xB2).\n\nWorking Partner vs Sleeping Partner\n\nA working partner receives a specific salary or fixed percentage from the total profit for actively managing the business. The remaining profit is then divided among all partners in their standard investment ratio.",
