        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nThe length of an arc is a direct fraction of the circle's total circumference.\n\nFraction of the circle = 150\xB0 \xF7 360\xB0 = 5/12\nTotal circumference = 2 \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 42 = 264 cm\nLength of the arc = (5/12) \xD7 264 = 110 cm\n\u2234 The correct answer is 110 cm.\n\nAlternate Method\n150\xB0\n\nr = 42 cm\nL = ?\n\nO\n\nGiven:\nRadius of the circle (r) = 42 cm\nAngle formed by the arc at the centre (\u03B8) = 150\xB0\n\nFormula Used:\nLength of arc = (\u03B8 \xF7 360\xB0) \xD7 2\u03C0r\n\nCalculation:\n\u21D2 Length of arc = (150\xB0 \xF7 360\xB0) \xD7 2 \xD7 (22 / 7) \xD7 42\n\u21D2 Length of arc = (5 / 12) \xD7 2 \xD7 22 \xD7 6\n\u21D2 Length of arc = (5 / 12) \xD7 264\n\u21D2 Length of arc = 5 \xD7 22\n\u21D2 Length of arc = 110 cm\n\u2234 The correct answer is 110 cm.\n\nAdditional Information\nArea of a Sector\n\nThe area enclosed by an arc and two radii is called a sector. It is calculated using the formula: Area = (\u03B8 \xF7 360\xB0) \xD7 \u03C0r\xB2.\n\nCircumference of a Circle\n\nThe total perimeter or boundary length of a complete circle is known as its circumference, given by the formula 2\u03C0r.\n\nArc vs Chord\n\nAn arc is a curved, continuous segment of the circle's outer edge, whereas a chord is a straight line drawn inside the circle connecting two points on its circumference.",
