        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nFor a right circular cone:\n$\\text{Volume} = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h$\n\nGiven ratio $r : h = 3 : 7$. Let $r = 3x$ and $h = 7x$:\n$\\text{Volume} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times (3x)^2 \\times (7x)$\n$\\Rightarrow \\text{Volume} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 22 \\times 9x^2 \\times x = 66x^3$\n\nWe are given the volume as $528\\text{ cm}^3$:\n$\\Rightarrow 66x^3 = 528$\n$\\Rightarrow x^3 = \\frac{528}{66} = 8$\n$\\Rightarrow x = \\sqrt[3]{8} = 2$\n\nHeight of the cone:\n$\\Rightarrow h = 7x = 7 \\times 2 = 14\\text{ cm}$\n\n\u2234 The height of the cone is $14.0\\text{ cm}$.",
