        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nThe inradius (r) of an equilateral triangle with side a is r = a / 2\u221A3.\nArea of incircle = \u03C0r\xB2 = \u03C0 \xD7 (a / 2\u221A3)2 = \u03C0a\xB2 / 12\nArea of equilateral triangle = (\u221A3 / 4)a\xB2\nRatio = (\u03C0a\xB2 / 12) : (\u221A3a\xB2 / 4) = \u03C0 : 3\u221A3\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u03C0 : 3\u221A3.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nSide of the equilateral triangle = a cm\n\nFormula Used:\nInradius of an equilateral triangle, r = a / 2\u221A3\nArea of circle = \u03C0r\xB2\nArea of equilateral triangle = (\u221A3 / 4)a\xB2\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Radius of the inscribed circle, r = a / 2\u221A3\n\u21D2 Area of the inscribed circle = \u03C0 \xD7 (a / 2\u221A3)2\n\u21D2 Area of the inscribed circle = \u03C0a\xB2 / 12\n\u21D2 Ratio = (Area of the circle) : (Area of the equilateral triangle)\n\u21D2 Ratio = (\u03C0a\xB2 / 12) : (\u221A3a\xB2 / 4)\n\u21D2 Ratio = (\u03C0 / 12) : (\u221A3 / 4)\n\u21D2 Ratio = \u03C0 : 3\u221A3\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u03C0 : 3\u221A3.\n\nAdditional Information\nCircumcircle of an Equilateral Triangle\n\nThe circumradius (R) of an equilateral triangle with side a is given by R = a / \u221A3. The ratio of circumradius to inradius for an equilateral triangle is always 2 : 1.\n\nIncenter of a Triangle\n\nThe incenter is the point of intersection of the internal angle bisectors. It is equidistant from all three sides of the triangle.\n\nRatio of Areas (Incircle vs Circumcircle)\n\nFor any regular equilateral triangle, the ratio of the area of its incircle to the area of its circumcircle is exactly 1 : 4.",
