        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nGiven, sin\u03B8 - cos\u03B8 = 0 \u21D2 sin\u03B8 = cos\u03B8\nSince the angle is in the 1st quadrant, \u03B8 = 45\xB0.\nAt \u03B8 = 45\xB0, sin\u03B8 = cos\u03B8 = 1/\u221A2.\nNow, substitute in sin3\u03B8 + 3cos3\u03B8:\n\u21D2 4 \xD7 cos3(45\xB0) = 4 \xD7 (1/\u221A2)3 = 4 / (2\u221A2) = \u221A2.\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u221A2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nsin\u03B8 - cos\u03B8 = 0\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 sin\u03B8 = cos\u03B8\n\nDivide both sides by cos\u03B8:\n\n\u21D2 tan\u03B8 = 1\nSince \u03B8 lies in the first quadrant (0\xB0 < \u03B8 < 90\xB0), we get:\n\u21D2 \u03B8 = 45\xB0\n\nWe need to find the value of sin3\u03B8 + 3cos3\u03B8\n\nSubstitute \u03B8 = 45\xB0 into the expression:\n\u21D2 sin3(45\xB0) + 3cos3(45\xB0)\n\u21D2 (1/\u221A2)3 + 3 \xD7 (1/\u221A2)3\n\u21D2 1/(2\u221A2) + 3/(2\u221A2)\n\u21D2 (1 + 3) / 2\u221A2\n\u21D2 4 / 2\u221A2\n\u21D2 2 / \u221A2\n\u21D2 \u221A2\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u221A2.\n\nAdditional Information\nTrigonometric Values at 45\xB0\n\nFor an angle of 45\xB0, both sine and cosine functions have the same value: sin(45\xB0) = 1/\u221A2 and cos(45\xB0) = 1/\u221A2.\n\nQuadrant Sign Convention (ASTC Rule)\n\nIn the 1st quadrant (0\xB0 to 90\xB0), all trigonometric ratios are positive. In the 2nd quadrant, Sine and Cosecant are positive.\n\nTrigonometric Identities\n\nThe fundamental Pythagorean identity is sin\xB2\u03B8 + cos\xB2\u03B8 = 1, which holds true for all real values of \u03B8.",
