        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nSide of the square = \u221A4900 = 70 m, which is also the radius of the circle.\nLength of the rectangle = 3/5 \xD7 radius = 3/5 \xD7 70 = 42 m.\nArea of the rectangle = Length \xD7 Breadth = 42 \xD7 20 = 840 m\xB2.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 840 m\xB2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nArea of the square = 4900 m\xB2\nRadius of circle = Side of the square\nLength of rectangle (L) = 3/5 \xD7 Radius of circle\nBreadth of rectangle (B) = 20 m\n\nFormula Used:\nArea of square = a\xB2 (where a is side length)\nArea of rectangle = L \xD7 B\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 a\xB2 = 4900\n\u21D2 a = \u221A4900 = 70 m\n\u21D2 Radius of the circle (r) = 70 m\n\u21D2 Length of the rectangle (L) = 3/5 \xD7 70 = 3 \xD7 14 = 42 m\n\u21D2 Area of the rectangle = L \xD7 B\n\u21D2 Area of the rectangle = 42 \xD7 20 = 840 m\xB2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 840 m\xB2.\n\nAdditional Information\nSquare Properties\n\nA square has all four equal sides. Its Area = a\xB2 and Perimeter = 4a (where a is side length).\n\nCircle Properties\n\nThe Area of a circle = \u03C0r\xB2 and its Circumference = 2\u03C0r (where r is the radius).\n\nRectangle Properties\n\nA rectangle has opposite equal sides. Its Area = Length \xD7 Breadth and Perimeter = 2 \xD7 (Length + Breadth).",
