        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\n13.5% of Bill Amount = Rs. 6075\n1% of Bill Amount = 6075 \xF7 13.5 = 450\n100% of Bill Amount = 450 \xD7 100 = 45000\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 45, 000.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nReduction percentage = 13.5%\nAmount of reduction = Rs. 6075\n\nFormula Used:\nPercentage Value = (Percentage \xF7 100) \xD7 Base Value\n\nCalculations:\nLet the total amount of the electricity bill be x.\n\u21D2 13.5% of x = 6075\n\u21D2 (13.5 \xF7 100) \xD7 x = 6075\n\u21D2 x = (6075 \xD7 100) \xF7 13.5\n\u21D2 x = 607500 \xF7 13.5\n\u21D2 x = 6075000 \xF7 135\n\u21D2 x = 45000\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 45, 000.\n\nAdditional Information\nBase and Percentage Relationship\n\nWhen a specific percentage of a base value is given, the complete base value can be found directly using the relation: Base = (Given Value \xD7 100) \xF7 Percentage Rate.\n\nPercentage Increase or Decrease\n\nNew Value = Original Value \xD7 (1 \xB1 r \xF7 100), where r is the percentage rate of change.\n\nSuccessive Percentage Change\n\nIf an amount is subjected to two successive percentage changes of a% and b%, the net effective change is calculated as: (a + b + ab \xF7 100)%.",
