        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nUsing the average deviation method to find the required runs directly: Runs required = Old average + (Total new innings \xD7 Increase in average)\n\nRuns required = 43 + (11 \xD7 3)\nRuns required = 43 + 33 = 76\n\u2234 The correct answer is 76 runs.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nAverage runs in the first 10 innings = 43\nRequired increase in average = 3\n\nFormula Used:\nAverage = Sum of all observations \xF7 Total number of observations\nTotal 11 Innings \u2192 New Average: 46\n10 Innings (Avg = 43)\n11th = ?\nDeviation: 10 innings need + 3 runs each\n11th Inning = 46 + (10 \xD7 3) = 76\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total runs scored in 10 innings = 10 \xD7 43 = 430 runs\n\u21D2 Target new average for 11 innings = 43 + 3 = 46 runs\n\u21D2 Total runs required in 11 innings = 11 \xD7 46 = 506 runs\n\u21D2 Runs required in the 11th inning = Total runs in 11 innings - Total runs in 10 innings\n\u21D2 Runs required = 506 - 430 = 76\n\u2234 The correct answer is 76 runs.\n\nAdditional Information\nBasic Average Concept\n\nThe average of any set of values is formulated as: Average = Sum of all values \xF7 Total count of values.\n\nDeviation Method for Included Items\n\nWhen a new item is added to a group, its value can be quickly found without large calculations using: Value of added item = Old Average + (Total new items \xD7 Change in Average).\n\nCombined Average\n\nWhen two groups of sizes n1 and n\xB2 with averages A1 and A\xB2 respectively are merged, the combined average is calculated as: (n1A1 + n2A\xB2) \xF7 (n1 + n\xB2).",
