        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nRelative speed of policeman = 10 - 8 = 2 km/h\nDistance gap to close = 100 m = 0.1 km\nTime required = Distance \xF7 Relative speed = 0.1 \xF7 2 = 1/20 hours\nTime in minutes = 1/20 \xD7 60 = 3 minutes\n\u2234 The correct answer is 3 minutes.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nSpeed of the policeman (Sp) = 10 km/h\nSpeed of the thief (St) = 8 km/h\nInitial distance ahead (D) = 100 m = 0.1 km\n\nFormula Used:\nRelative Speed = Sp - St (Since they move in the same direction)\nTime = Distance \xF7 Relative Speed\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Relative Speed = 10 - 8 = 2 km/h\n\u21D2 Time required to catch the thief = 0.1 km \xF7 2 km/h = 0.05 hours\n\u21D2 To convert hours into minutes, multiply by 60:\n\u21D2 Time required = 0.05 \xD7 60 = 3 minutes\n\u2234 The correct answer is 3 minutes.\n\nAdditional Information\nRelative Speed (Same Direction)\n\nWhen two bodies move in the same direction at speeds S1 and S\xB2 (where S1 > S\xB2), their relative speed is S1 - S\xB2.\n\nRelative Speed (Opposite Direction)\n\nWhen two bodies move towards each other at speeds S1 and S\xB2, their relative speed is S1 + S\xB2.\n\nSpeed Unit Conversion\n\nTo convert km/h to m/s, multiply the speed by 5 \xF7 18. To convert m/s to km/h, multiply by 18 \xF7 5.",
