        solution: "Solution\n\nGiven:\nA trader earns a profit of 30% by selling an article X and loses 16% by selling another article Y.\n\nThe ratio of the cost prices of X and Y is 3 \u2236 4.\n\nConcept used:\n\nProfit% =\nProfit\nCost Price\n\xD7100%\nP\nr\no\nf\ni\nt\ncos t\n\nP\nr\ni\nc\ne\n\xD7\n100\n%\n\nSelling Price = Cost Price - Cost Price \xD7 Loss%\nSelling Price = Cost Price + Cost Price \xD7 Gain%\n\nCalculation:\nLet the cost price of X and Y be Rs. 300 and Rs. 400.\nTotal cost price = 300 + 400 = Rs. 700\nSelling price of X = 300 + 300 \xD7 30% = Rs. 390\nSelling price of Y = 400 - 400 \xD7 16% = Rs. 336\nTotal selling price = 390 + 336 = Rs. 726\nGain made = 726 - 700 = Rs. 26\nNow, gain% in the entire transaction =\n26\n700\n\xD7100%\n26 / 700 \xD7 100\n%\n\u2248 3.7%\n\n\u2234 The gain in the entire transaction is 3.7%.",
