        solution: "Solution\n\nGiven:\nRam has \u20B930.\n\nShyam has \u20B940.\n\nGhanshyam has \u20B960.\n\nThey give equal amounts to their mother such that the remaining amounts are in continued proportion.\n\nFormula Used:\nFor continued proportion: a/b = b/c or b2 = a \u22C5 c\n\nCalculation:\nLet the amount given by each of them to their mother be x .\n\nThen, the remaining amounts are:\n\nRam: \u20B9(30 - x)\nShyam: \u20B9(40 - x)\nGhanshyam: \u20B9(60 - x)\n\nFor continued proportion:\n\n(30 - x)/(40 - x) = (40 - x)/(60 - x)\n\nBy cross-multiplication:\n\n(40 - x)\xB2 = (30 - x) \u22C5 (60 - x)\n\nExpanding both sides:\n\n\u21D2 1600 - 80x + x2 = 30 \xD7 60 - 30x - 60x + x2\n\u21D2 1600 - 80x + x2 = 1800 - 90x + x2\n\nCancel out x2 from both sides:\n\n\u21D2 1600 - 80x = 1800 - 90x\n\nSimplify:\n\n\u21D2 90x - 80x = 1800 - 1600\n\u21D2 10x = 200\n\u21D2 x = 20\n\nThe amount taken from each of them is \u20B920.",
