        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nLet the numbers be 8x and 8y, where x and y are co-prime.\nProduct of ratios (x \xD7 y) = LCM \xF7 HCF = 96 \xF7 8 = 12.\nSum of ratios (x + y) = Sum \xF7 HCF = 56 \xF7 8 = 7.\n\nFind two numbers that multiply to 12 and add to 7 \u2192 3 and 4.\n\nDifference between numbers = HCF \xD7 (x - y) = 8 \xD7 (4 - 3) = 8.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 8.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nLCM = 96, HCF = 8, Sum (a + b) = 56.\n\nFormula Used:\nProduct of two numbers (a \xD7 b) = LCM \xD7 HCF\nAlgebraic identity: (a - b)\xB2 = (a + b)\xB2 - 4ab\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Product (ab) = 96 \xD7 8 = 768\n\u21D2 Sum (a + b) = 56\n\u21D2 (a - b)\xB2 = (56)\xB2 - 4 \xD7 (768)\n\u21D2 (a - b)\xB2 = 3136 - 3072\n\u21D2 (a - b)\xB2 = 64\n\u21D2 (a - b) = \u221A64 = 8\n\u2234 The correct answer is 8.\n\nAdditional Information\nProduct Rule of HCF and LCM\n\nFor any two positive integers a and b, HCF(a, b) \xD7 LCM(a, b) = a \xD7 b.\n\nCo-prime Factors Property\n\nIf HCF of two numbers is h, the numbers can be written as hx and hy, where LCM = h \xD7 x \xD7 y and gcd(x, y) = 1.\n\nDifference and Sum Relationship\n\nThe relationship between sum and difference is given by the identity (a + b)\xB2 - (a - b)\xB2 = 4ab.",
