        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nLet the two numbers be 5a and 5b, where a and b are coprime.\nGiven LCM = 495 \u21D2 5 \xD7 a \xD7 b = 495 \u21D2 a \xD7 b = 99\nGiven Sum = 100 \u21D2 5a + 5b = 100 \u21D2 a + b = 20\nValues satisfying both conditions are a = 11 and b = 9.\nDifference = 5a - 5b = 5 \xD7 (11 - 9) = 10.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 10.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nLCM of the two numbers = 495\nHCF of the two numbers = 5\nSum of the numbers (a + b) = 100\n\nFormula Used:\nProduct of two numbers = HCF \xD7 LCM\n(a - b)\xB2 = (a + b)\xB2 - 4ab\nLarger Number = 55\nSmaller Number = 45\n10\nDifference\nSum = 100\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 a \xD7 b = 5 \xD7 495 = 2475\n\u21D2 We know that (a - b)\xB2 = (a + b)\xB2 - 4ab\n\u21D2 (a - b)\xB2 = (100)\xB2 - 4 \xD7 2475\n\u21D2 (a - b)\xB2 = 10000 - 9900\n\u21D2 (a - b)\xB2 = 100\n\u21D2 a - b = \u221A100\n\u21D2 a - b = 10\n\u2234 The correct answer is 10.\n\nAdditional Information\nProduct Rule for Two Numbers\n\nThe product of any two given numbers is always equal to the product of their HCF and LCM. Formula: a \xD7 b = HCF \xD7 LCM.\n\nCoprime Ratio Concept\n\nIf two numbers have an HCF of H, they can be expressed as Hx and Hy, where x and y are coprime. Their LCM is strictly H \xD7 x \xD7 y.\n\nHCF and LCM of Fractions\n\nHCF = (HCF of Numerators) \xF7 (LCM of Denominators) | LCM = (LCM of Numerators) \xF7 (HCF of Denominators).",
