        question: "A regular hexagon is inscribed in a circle. Find the ratio of area of circle to the area of that portion which is not covered by the hexagon?",
        options: {
          a: "2\u03C0/(2\u03C0 - 3\u221A3)",
          b: "\u03C0/(\u03C0 - 3\u221A3)",
          c: "2\u03C0/\u221A3",
          d: "\u03C0/\u221A3"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nRadius of circumcircle = side of inscribed regular hexagon = r\nArea of circle = \u03C0r2\nArea of regular hexagon = (3\u221A3/2)r2\nUncovered Area = \u03C0r2 - (3\u221A3/2)r2 = r2(2\u03C0 - 3\u221A3) / 2\nRatio = Area of circle \xF7 Uncovered Area = 2\u03C0 / (2\u03C0 - 3\u221A3)\n\u2234 The correct answer is 2\u03C0/(2\u03C0 - 3\u221A3).\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nA regular hexagon is inscribed in a circle.\n\nFormula Used:\nArea of a circle = \u03C0r2\nArea of a regular hexagon = 6 \xD7 (\u221A3 / 4)a2 (where a is the side length)\n\nFor a regular hexagon inscribed in a circle, the side length (a) equals the radius (r).\n\nO\nRs. haded blue region = Area not covered by hexagon\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Let the radius of the circle be r.\n\u21D2 Side of the inscribed regular hexagon = r\n\u21D2 Area of the circle = \u03C0r2\n\u21D2 Area of the hexagon = 6 \xD7 (\u221A3 / 4)r2 = (3\u221A3 / 2)r2\n\u21D2 Area not covered by hexagon = Area of circle - Area of hexagon\n\u21D2 Area not covered = \u03C0r2 - (3\u221A3 / 2)r2\n\u21D2 Area not covered = r2(2\u03C0 - 3\u221A3) / 2\n\u21D2 Required Ratio = (Area of circle) \xF7 (Area not covered)\n\u21D2 Ratio = \u03C0r2 \xF7 [r2(2\u03C0 - 3\u221A3) / 2]\n\u21D2 Ratio = 2\u03C0 / (2\u03C0 - 3\u221A3)\n\u2234 The correct answer is 2\u03C0/(2\u03C0 - 3\u221A3).\n\nAdditional Information\nCircumcircle of a Regular Hexagon\n\nThe circumcenter and incenter of a regular hexagon coincide. The radius of the circumscribed circle is exactly equal to the side length of the hexagon (R = a).\n\nIncircle of a Regular Hexagon\n\nThe radius of a circle inscribed inside a regular hexagon is given by r = (a\u221A3)/2. The ratio of the area of the circumcircle to the incircle is 4:3.\n\nArea of an Equilateral Triangle\n\nA regular hexagon is composed of exactly 6 identical equilateral triangles. The area of one such triangle with side a is (\u221A3 / 4)a2.",
