        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal Lateral Surface Area = Total Surface Area - Base Area\n\u21D2 Total Lateral Area = 260 - 120 = 140 cm2\nNumber of Lateral Faces = Total Lateral Area \xF7 Area of each lateral face\n\u21D2 Number of faces = 140 \xF7 20 = 7\n\u2234 The correct answer is 7.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal surface area of the pyramid = 260 cm2\nArea of its base = 120 cm2\nArea of each lateral face = 20 cm2\n\nFormula Used:\nTotal Surface Area = Base Area + (Number of lateral faces \xD7 Area of each lateral face)\n\nCalculations:\nLet the number of lateral faces be n.\n\u21D2 260 = 120 + (n \xD7 20)\n\u21D2 n \xD7 20 = 260 - 120\n\u21D2 20n = 140\n\u21D2 n = 140 \xF7 20\n\u21D2 n = 7\n\u2234 The correct answer is 7.\n\nAdditional Information\nVolume of a Pyramid\n\nThe volume of a pyramid is one-third of the product of its base area and perpendicular height. Formula: V = (1 \xF7 3) \xD7 Base Area \xD7 Height.\n\nLateral Surface Area (Regular Pyramid)\n\nIt is the total area of all its lateral faces. For a regular pyramid: LSA = (1 \xF7 2) \xD7 Perimeter of Base \xD7 Slant Height.\n\nEuler's Formula for Polyhedra\n\nFor any convex polyhedron, the number of faces (F), vertices (V), and edges (E) are related by the formula: F + V - E = 2.",
