        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nWhen the time taken by both moving objects is constant, the ratio of the distance covered is equal to the ratio of their speeds.\n\nSpeed ratio (Thief : Policeman) = 11 : 13\nDistance ratio (Thief : Policeman) = 11 : 13\nDifference in distance covered = 13 parts - 11 parts = 2 parts\nGiven the initial distance difference is 225 m \u21D2 2 parts = 225 m \u21D2 1 part = 112.5 m\nDistance run by the thief = 11 parts = 11 \xD7 112.5 = 1237.5 metres\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1237.5 metres.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nInitial distance between policeman and thief = 225 m\nSpeed of thief = 11 km/h\nSpeed of policeman = 13 km/h\n\nFormula Used:\nRelative speed (same direction) = Speed1 - Speed2\nTime = Distance \xF7 Relative Speed\nDistance = Speed \xD7 Time\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Relative speed = 13 - 11 = 2 km/h\n\u21D2 Relative speed in m/s = 2 \xD7 (5/18) = 5/9 m/s\n\u21D2 Time taken to catch the thief = Distance \xF7 Relative speed = 225 \xF7 (5/9)\n\u21D2 Time taken = 225 \xD7 (9/5) = 45 \xD7 9 = 405 seconds\n\u21D2 Speed of thief in m/s = 11 \xD7 (5/18) = 55/18 m/s\n\u21D2 Distance covered by thief before getting caught = Speed of thief \xD7 Time taken\n\u21D2 Distance = (55/18) \xD7 405 = 55 \xD7 22.5\n\u21D2 Distance = 1237.5 m\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1237.5 metres.\n\nAdditional Information\nRelative Speed (Same Direction)\n\nWhen two bodies are moving in the same direction, their relative speed is the difference between their individual speeds: S = S1 - S2.\n\nRelative Speed (Opposite Direction)\n\nWhen two bodies are moving in opposite directions towards each other, their relative speed is the sum of their individual speeds: S = S1 + S2.\n\nUnit Conversion\n\nTo convert speed from km/h to m/s, multiply the value by 5/18. To convert speed from m/s to km/h, multiply the value by 18/5.",
