        userTime: "00:30",
        avgTime: "00:15",
        question: "The ratio of the outer and the inner circumference of a circular path is 17 \u2236 15. If path is 40 metres wide, then what is the radius of the inner circle?",
        options: {
          a: "280 metres",
          b: "340 metres",
          c: "360 metres",
          d: "300 metres"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nThe ratio of circumferences of two circles is identical to the ratio of their radii.\n\nRatio of outer radius\n(R) to inner radius (r) = 17 \u2236 15\nWidth of the path in ratio units = 17 - 15 = 2 units.\nGiven width = 40 metres, so 2 units = 40 metres \u21D2 1 unit = 20 metres.\nInner radius = 15 units = 15 \xD7 20 = 300 metres.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 300 metres.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nRatio of outer and inner circumference = 17 \u2236 15\nWidth of the path = 40 metres\n\nFormula Used:\nCircumference of a circle = 2\xD7\u03C0\xD7r\nWidth of circular path = R - r\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Let the outer radius be R and the inner radius be r.\n\u21D2 Ratio of circumferences = (2\xD7\u03C0\xD7R) \xF7 (2\xD7\u03C0\xD7r)\n\u21D2 R / r = 17 / 15\n\u21D2 Let R = 17x and r = 15x\n\u21D2 Width of the circular path = Outer Radius - Inner Radius\n\u21D2 17x - 15x = 40\n\u21D2 2x = 40\n\u21D2 x = 20\n\u21D2 Inner radius (r) = 15x = 15 \xD7 20 = 300 metres\n\u2234 The correct answer is 300 metres.\n\nAdditional Information\nArea of a Circular Path\n\nThe total area located strictly between two concentric circles is given by Area = \u03C0\xD7(R2 - r2), where R and r are the respective outer and inner radii.\n\nLength of an Arc\n\nAn arc is a fraction of the full circumference. The length is determined by the central angle \u03B8: (\u03B8 \xF7 360) \xD7 2\u03C0r.\n\nArea of a Sector\n\nThe region bounded by two radii and an adjoining arc is called a sector. Its area is: (\u03B8 \xF7 360) \xD7 \u03C0r2.",
