        status: "Unattempted",
        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "A",
        userTime: "00:48",
        avgTime: "00:19",
        question: "Three friends A, B, C invested in a business in the ratio of 3 : 2 : 6. After 6 months C withdraw half his capital. If the total profit earned for the year is Rs. 53010, then profit made by A is (in Rs.):",
        options: {
          a: "16740",
          b: "19740",
          c: "17740",
          d: "18740"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nProfit ratio = (Capital \xD7 Time)\nA : B : C = (3 \xD7 12) : (2 \xD7 12) : (6 \xD7 6 + 3 \xD7 6)\n\u21D2 A : B : C = 36 : 24 : 54 = 6 : 4 : 9\nTotal profit = 19 parts = \u20B953010 \u21D2 1 part = \u20B92790\nA's profit = 6 parts = 6 \xD7 2790 = \u20B916740\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B916740.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nRatio of initial investments of A, B and C = 3 : 2 : 6\n\nC withdraws half of his capital after 6 months.\n\nTotal profit for the year = \u20B953010\n\nFormula Used:\nProfit Ratio = Product of Capital and Time Period\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Equivalent capital for A = 3 \xD7 12 = 36 units\n\u21D2 Equivalent capital for B = 2 \xD7 12 = 24 units\n\u21D2 Equivalent capital for C = (6 \xD7 6) + (3 \xD7 6) = 36 + 18 = 54 units\n\u21D2 Ratio of profits (A : B : C) = 36 : 24 : 54\n\u21D2 Simplified profit ratio = 6 : 4 : 9\n\u21D2 Total ratio parts = 6 + 4 + 9 = 19\n\u21D2 A's share = (6 \xF7 19) \xD7 Total Profit\n\u21D2 A's share = (6 \xF7 19) \xD7 53010\n\u21D2 A's share = 6 \xD7 2790 = 16740\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B916740.\n\nAdditional Information\nPartnership Profit Sharing\n\nProfit is distributed directly in proportion to the product of capital invested and the time duration of the investment. Ratio = C1T1 : C2T2.\n\nActive vs Sleeping Partner\n\nAn active partner manages the business and receives a fixed salary or percentage of the total profit. The remaining profit is divided among all partners based on their capital-time ratio.\n\nCapital Adjustments Mid-Year\n\nWhen capital is added or withdrawn midway, the effective capital is found by calculating (Capital \xD7 Time) for each phase independently and summing them up.",
