        userTime: "00:02",
        avgTime: "00:10",
        question: "The average salary of the entire staff in an office is Rs. 130 per month. The average salary of officers is Rs. 450 and that of non-officers is Rs. 120. If the number of officers is 15, then find the number of non-officers in the office?",
        options: {
          a: "450",
          b: "460",
          c: "470",
          d: "480"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nUsing the method of Alligation:\n\nRatio of Officers to Non-officers = (130 - 120) : (450 - 130)\nRatio = 10 : 320 = 1 : 32\nGiven 1 ratio unit = 15 officers, then 32 ratio units = 15 \xD7 32 = 480 non-officers.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 480 non-officers.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nAverage salary of overall staff = Rs. 130\nAverage salary of officers = Rs. 450\nAverage salary of non-officers = Rs. 120\nNumber of officers = 15\n\nFormula Used:\nOverall Average = (Total salary of all staff) \xF7 (Total number of staff)\nOfficers: 450\nNon-Off: 120\n130\n130 - 120 = 10\n450 - 130 = 320\nRatio \u2192 10 : 320 = 1 : 32\n\nCalculations:\nLet the number of non-officers be x.\n\u21D2 Total salary of officers = 450 \xD7 15 = 6750\n\u21D2 Total salary of non-officers = 120 \xD7 x = 120x\n\u21D2 Total staff members = 15 + x\n\u21D2 Overall Average = (6750 + 120x) \xF7 (15 + x)\n\u21D2 130 = (6750 + 120x) \xF7 (15 + x)\n\u21D2 130 \xD7 (15 + x) = 6750 + 120x\n\u21D2 1950 + 130x = 6750 + 120x\n\u21D2 130x - 120x = 6750 - 1950\n\u21D2 10x = 4800\n\u21D2 x = 480\n\u2234 The correct answer is 480 non-officers.\n\nAdditional Information\nWeighted Average\n\nUsed when calculating the combined average of groups with different sizes. Formula: Aw = (n1A1 + n2A2) \xF7 (n1 + n2).\n\nRule of Alligation\n\nA rapid visual method to find the ratio in which two groups with different averages are mixed to yield a desired overall combined average.\n\nAverage & Net Deviation\n\nThe sum of the net deviations of all individual values from their mean is always equal to zero, which is a useful property to solve unknown value problems quickly.",
