        testName: "SSC CGL Tier I: Full Test - 1",
        platform: "Testbook",
        status: "Unattempted",
        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "B",
        userTime: "00:05",
        avgTime: "00:11",
        question: "A cylindrical hole with the radius of its base given as 3.5 cm is made in a solid cube each of whose edge is 14 cm. Find the total surface area (in cm2) of the cube with the hole. [Use \u03C0 = 22/7]",
        options: {
          a: "1484",
          b: "1407",
          c: "791",
          d: "945"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nWhen a hole is drilled completely through a solid, the net Total Surface Area (TSA) is:\n\nNet TSA = (TSA of Cube) - (2 \xD7 Base Area of Hole) + (Curved Surface Area of Hole)\nNet TSA = 6a2 - 2\u03C0r2 + 2\u03C0rh\nNet TSA = 6 \xD7 142 - 2 \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 (3.5)\xB2 + 2 \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 3.5 \xD7 14\nNet TSA = 1176 - 77 + 308 = 1407 cm2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1407 cm2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\n\u21D2 Edge of the solid cube (a) = 14 cm\n\u21D2 Radius of the cylindrical hole (r) = 3.5 cm\n\u21D2 Height of the cylindrical hole (h) = Edge of cube = 14 cm\n\nFormula Used:\n\u21D2 Total Surface Area = (TSA of solid cube) - (2 \xD7 Area of circular bases of hole) + (CSA of cylindrical hole)\n\u21D2 TSA = 6a2 - 2\u03C0r2 + 2\u03C0rh\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 TSA of cube = 6 \xD7 14 \xD7 14 = 6 \xD7 196 = 1176 cm2\n\u21D2 Area of 2 circular bases = 2 \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 3.5 \xD7 3.5 = 77 cm2\n\u21D2 CSA of cylindrical hole = 2 \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 3.5 \xD7 14 = 308 cm2\n\u21D2 Total Surface Area = 1176 - 77 + 308 = 1407 cm2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1407 cm2.\n\nAdditional Information\nEffect of Drilling a Hole on Surface Area\n\nWhen a hole is drilled completely through a solid, the flat surface area corresponding to the base cuts is lost, but the newly created inner curved surface is exposed and must be added to the total area.\n\nImportant Formulas for a Cube\n\nVolume = a3 | Total Surface Area = 6a2 | Length of Body Diagonal = a\u221A3.\n\nImportant Formulas for a Cylinder\n\nVolume = \u03C0r2h | Curved Surface Area = 2\u03C0rh | Total Surface Area = 2\u03C0r(r + h).",
        topic: "Mensuration 3D",
