        avgTime: "00:24",
        question: "The radii of the two concentric circles are 27 cm and 18 cm. The area (in cm2) of the closed figure bounded by the boundaries of the circle is:",
        options: {
          a: "505\u03C0",
          b: "405\u03C0",
          c: "288\u03C0",
          d: "504\u03C0"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nArea of a circular ring = \u03C0 \xD7 (R - r) \xD7 (R + r)\nSubstitute R = 27 and r = 18 into the formula:\n\u21D2 Area = \u03C0 \xD7 (27 - 18) \xD7 (27 + 18)\n\u21D2 Area = \u03C0 \xD7 9 \xD7 45\n\u21D2 Area = 405\u03C0\n\u2234 The correct answer is 405\u03C0 cm2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\n\u21D2 Outer radius of the circle\n(R) = 27 cm\n\u21D2 Inner radius of the circle (r) = 18 cm\n\nFormula Used:\n\u21D2 Area of the bounded region (Ring) = Area of outer circle - Area of inner circle\n\u21D2 Area = \u03C0R2 - \u03C0r2 = \u03C0(R2 - r2)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Area = \u03C0 \xD7 (27)\xB2 - \u03C0 \xD7 (18)\xB2\n\u21D2 Area = \u03C0 \xD7 (729 - 324)\n\u21D2 Area = 405\u03C0\n\u2234 The correct answer is 405\u03C0 cm2.\n\nAdditional Information\nConcentric Circles\n\nConcentric circles are circles that share the exact same center point but have different radii. The region enclosed between two concentric circles is often referred to as an annulus or a circular ring.\n\nWidth of the Circular Ring\n\nThe thickness or width of the ring is uniformly distributed and can be calculated by subtracting the inner radius from the outer radius: Width = R - r.\n\nAlgebraic Identities\n\nWhen solving questions involving the difference of squares, applying the algebraic identity a2 - b2 = (a - b)(a + b) will severely reduce the calculation time and prevent squaring large values.",
