        correctOption: "B",
        userTime: "00:08",
        avgTime: "00:27",
        question: "The simple interest on a sum of money is 9/45 of the sum. If the number of years is numerically 5 times of rate per cent per annum, then find the rate per cent per annum.",
        options: {
          a: "7%",
          b: "2%",
          c: "5%",
          d: "3%"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nEffective Rate % over the entire period = (SI \xF7 P) \xD7 100\nRate \xD7 Time = (9 \xF7 45) \xD7 100\nGiven Time (T) = 5R, we substitute T directly:\nR \xD7 5R = (1 \xF7 5) \xD7 100\n5R2 = 20 \u21D2 R2 = 4 \u21D2 R = 2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 2%.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nSimple Interest (SI) = 9/45 of Principal\n(P) = P / 5\nTime (T) = 5 \xD7 Rate\n(R)\n\nFormula Used:\nSimple Interest (SI) = (P \xD7 R \xD7 T) \xF7 100\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 P / 5 = (P \xD7 R \xD7 5R) \xF7 100\n\nDividing both sides by P:\n\n\u21D2 1 / 5 = 5R2 / 100\n\u21D2 1 / 5 = R2 / 20\n\u21D2 R2 = 20 / 5\n\u21D2 R2 = 4\n\u21D2 R = \u221A4 = 2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 2%.\n\nAdditional Information\nSimple Interest (SI) Basics\n\nSimple interest is charged only on the initial principal for the entire duration. The formula is SI = (P \xD7 R \xD7 T) \xF7 100.\n\nImportant Variation Formulas\n\nPrincipal\n(P) = (SI \xD7 100) \xF7 (R \xD7 T) | Time (T) = (SI \xD7 100) \xF7 (P \xD7 R)\n\nSimple Interest vs Compound Interest\n\nSI grows linearly over time, whereas Compound Interest (CI) grows exponentially because interest is calculated on both the principal and the accumulated interest.",
