        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nWhen time intervals are equal, Average Speed = Arithmetic mean of all speeds.\n\nThe speeds for the 5 hours form a geometric sequence ending in 128: 8, 16, 32, 64, 128 km/h.\n\nSum of speeds = 8 + 16 + 32 + 64 + 128 = 248 km/h.\nAverage Speed = 248 \xF7 5 = 49.6 km/h.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 49.6 km/h.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal time taken for the journey = 5 hours\nSpeed in the 5th hour = 128 km/h\n\nThe speed doubles after every hour.\n\nFormula Used:\nDistance = Speed \xD7 Time\nAverage Speed = Total Distance \xF7 Total Time\n\nCalculations:\nLet the speed in the 1st hour be v km/h.\nSpeeds in consecutive hours follow the pattern: 2v, 4v, 8v, 16v.\n\u21D2 Speed in the 5th hour = 16v = 128\n\u21D2 v = 128 \xF7 16 = 8 km/h\n\nThe distance covered in each 1-hour interval is numerically equal to the speed:\n\n\u21D2 Distance in 1st hour = 8 \xD7 1 = 8 km\n\u21D2 Distance in 2nd hour = 16 \xD7 1 = 16 km\n\u21D2 Distance in 3rd hour = 32 \xD7 1 = 32 km\n\u21D2 Distance in 4th hour = 64 \xD7 1 = 64 km\n\u21D2 Distance in 5th hour = 128 \xD7 1 = 128 km\n\u21D2 Total Distance = 8 + 16 + 32 + 64 + 128 = 248 km\n\u21D2 Average Speed = 248 \xF7 5 = 49.6 km/h\n\u2234 The correct answer is 49.6 km/h.\n\nAdditional Information\nAverage Speed\n\nAverage speed is defined as the total distance traveled divided by the total time taken. It is not the simple average of individual speeds unless the time intervals for each speed are strictly equal.\n\nEqual Time Intervals Rule\n\nIf an object travels at different speeds v1, v2, ..., vn for equal durations of time, the average speed is simply the arithmetic mean of all the speeds: (v1 + v2 + ... + vn) \xF7 n.\n\nGeometric Progression (GP)\n\nA sequence of numbers where each term after the first is found by multiplying the previous one by a fixed, non-zero number (common ratio). The sum of a GP is computed as Sn = a(rn - 1) \xF7 (r - 1) for r > 1.",
