        question: "A distributor purchases electric heaters at a price 60% above the factory's basic cost C. He gives a 25% trade discount to a shopkeeper. The shopkeeper then adds a 30% markup to his purchase price and offers customers a 10% discount on the marked price. If a customer pays \u20B921,060 for one heater, what was its basic cost at the factory?",
