        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nUsing the combined volume formula for a cone on a hemisphere: V = (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2 \xD7 (2r + h)\nCone height h = Total height - radius = 11.6 - 5.6 = 6 cm.\nV = (1/3) \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 5.6 \xD7 5.6 \xD7 (2 \xD7 5.6 + 6)\nV = (1/3) \xD7 22 \xD7 0.8 \xD7 5.6 \xD7 17.2 \u2248 565.07 cm3\n\nRounding off to the closest integer gives 565 cm3.\n\n\u2234 The correct answer is 565 cm3.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal height of the toy = 11.6 cm\nRadius of hemisphere (r) = 5.6 cm\n\nFormula Used:\nVolume of a Cone = (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2 \xD7 h\nVolume of a Hemisphere = (2/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r3\nTotal Volume = (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2 \xD7 (2r + h)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Height of cone (h) = Total height - Radius of hemisphere\n\u21D2 h = 11.6 - 5.6 = 6 cm\n\u21D2 Total Volume = (1/3) \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 (5.6)\xB2 \xD7 (2 \xD7 5.6 + 6)\n\u21D2 Total Volume = (1/3) \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 31.36 \xD7 (11.2 + 6)\n\u21D2 Total Volume = (1/3) \xD7 22 \xD7 4.48 \xD7 17.2\n\u21D2 Total Volume = (1/3) \xD7 98.56 \xD7 17.2\n\u21D2 Total Volume = 1695.232 \xF7 3 \u2248 565.07 cm3\n\u21D2 Rounding to the closest integral value, the volume is 565 cm3.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 565 cm3.\n\nAdditional Information\nVolume of a Hemisphere\n\nV = (2/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r3, where r is the radius of the circular base.\n\nVolume of a Right Circular Cone\n\nV = (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2 \xD7 h, where r is the radius of the base and h is the height.\n\nSurface Areas\n\nCurved Surface Area (CSA) of a Cone = \u03C0 \xD7 r \xD7 l, where slant height l = \u221A(r2 + h2). CSA of a Hemisphere = 2 \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2.",
