        userTime: "00:03",
        avgTime: "00:16",
        question: "Aman's average score in a series of tests was \u2018y\u2019. He appeared in one more test and obtained score \u2018z\u2019. If Aman appeared in total \u2018n\u2019 tests, then which one of the following expression shows his average score for all the tests?",
        options: {
          a: "y(n-1)+zn",
          b: "y(n-1)+zn",
          c: "y(n-1)+1n",
          d: "y(n-1)n"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal number of tests taken by Aman = n.\nNumber of initial tests before the last one = n - 1.\nSum of scores in the first (n - 1) tests = Average \xD7 Count = y(n - 1).\nTotal sum of all n tests = Initial sum + Score of last test = y(n - 1) + z.\nNew Average = Total Sum \xF7 Total Tests = [y(n - 1) + z] / n.\n\u2234 The correct answer is [y(n - 1) + z] / n.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal number of tests appeared = n\nAverage score in the series before the last test = y\nScore obtained in the last test = z\n\nFormula Used:\nAverage = Sum of Observations \xF7 Number of Observations\nSum of Observations = Average \xD7 Number of Observations\n\nFirst (n - 1) tests\nSum = y(n - 1)\nLast 1 test\nScore = z\nTotal n tests\nTotal Sum = y(n - 1) + z\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Number of tests taken before the final test = Total tests - 1 = n - 1\n\u21D2 Sum of scores in the initial (n - 1) tests = y \xD7 (n - 1)\n\u21D2 Total score for all n tests = Sum of (n - 1) tests + Score in the last test\n\u21D2 Total score = y(n - 1) + z\n\u21D2 Required Average = Total score \xF7 Total number of tests\n\u21D2 Required Average = [y(n - 1) + z] / n\n\u2234 The correct answer is [y(n - 1) + z] / n.\n\nAdditional Information\nAverage (Arithmetic Mean)\n\nAverage is defined as the sum of all values divided by the total number of values. Formula: Average = Sum of all terms \xF7 Number of terms.\n\nCombined Average\n\nIf group 1 has n1 items with average A1 and group 2 has n2 items with average A2, then the combined average is (n1A1 + n2A2) \xF7 (n1 + n2).\n\nNet Change in Average\n\nWhen a new observation is added, the new average can also be calculated as: Old Average + (Difference between new value and old average \xF7 Total new number of items).",
        topic: "Average",
