        testName: "SSC CGL Tier I: Full Test - 6",
        platform: "Testbook",
        status: "Unattempted",
        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "B",
        userTime: "00:03",
        avgTime: "00:36",
        question: "A hemispherical bowl of diameter 16 cm is full of ice cream. Each student in a class is served exactly 6 scoops of ice cream. If the hemispherical scoop is having a radius of 2 cm, then ice cream is served to approximately how many students?",
        options: {
          a: "13 students",
          b: "10 students",
          c: "12 students",
          d: "8 students"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal number of scoops in the bowl = (Radius of bowl \xF7 Radius of scoop)3\n\u21D2 Total scoops = (8 \xF7 2)3 = 43 = 64 scoops\nSince each student is served exactly 6 scoops:\n\u21D2 Number of students served = 64 \xF7 6 = 10.66\n\nIce cream can be fully served to a maximum of 10 students with exactly 6 scoops each.\n\n\u2234 The correct answer is 10 students.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nDiameter of the hemispherical bowl = 16 cm \u21D2 Radius\n(R) = 16 \xF7 2 = 8 cm\nRadius of the hemispherical scoop (r) = 2 cm\nScoops served per student = 6\n\nFormula Used:\nVolume of a hemisphere = (2 \xF7 3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 radius3\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Volume of the ice cream in the bowl = (2 \xF7 3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 83 = (2 \xF7 3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 512\n\u21D2 Volume of a single scoop = (2 \xF7 3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 23 = (2 \xF7 3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 8\n\u21D2 Total number of scoops = Volume of bowl \xF7 Volume of single scoop\n\u21D2 Total number of scoops = [(2 \xF7 3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 512] \xF7 [(2 \xF7 3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 8] = 512 \xF7 8 = 64 scoops\n\u21D2 Since each student receives exactly 6 scoops, the number of students = 64 \xF7 6 = 10.66\n\u21D2 Thus, ice cream is fully served to 10 students, leaving exactly 4 scoops remaining in the bowl.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 10 students.\n\nAdditional Information\nVolume of a Hemisphere\n\nA hemisphere is exactly half of a complete sphere. Its volume formula is V = (2 \xF7 3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r3.\n\nTotal Surface Area (TSA) of a Hemisphere\n\nThe TSA encompasses the curved surface along with the flat circular base. The formula is TSA = 3 \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2.\n\nVolume Proportionality Rule\n\nFor any pair of 3D shapes featuring identical proportions (like two spheres or hemispheres), the ratio of their total volumes equals the cube of the ratio of their corresponding linear dimensions.",
