        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nLet the number of \u20B92 coins be 5y. Then \u20B95 coins (20% less) = 4y, and \u20B910 coins = 4y - 8.\n\nTotal value = 2(5y) + 5(4y) + 10(4y - 8) = 270.\n10y + 20y + 40y - 80 = 270 \u21D2 70y = 350 \u21D2 y = 5.\nNumber of \u20B95 coins = 4 \xD7 5 = 20.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 20.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nNumber of \u20B95 coins is 8 more than the number of \u20B910 coins.\n\nNumber of \u20B95 coins is 20% less than the number of \u20B92 coins.\n\nTotal amount in the bag = \u20B9270.\n\nFormula Used:\nTotal Value = (Value of \u20B92 coins) + (Value of \u20B95 coins) + (Value of \u20B910 coins)\n\nCalculation:\n\u21D2 Let the number of \u20B92 coins be 5y.\n\u21D2 Number of \u20B95 coins is 20% less = 5y \xD7 (80 \xF7 100) = 4y\n\u21D2 Number of \u20B910 coins is 8 less than \u20B95 coins = 4y - 8\n\u21D2 Total value = (2 \xD7 5y) + (5 \xD7 4y) + 10 \xD7 (4y - 8) = 270\n\u21D2 10y + 20y + 40y - 80 = 270\n\u21D2 70y = 350\n\u21D2 y = 350 \xF7 70 = 5\n\u21D2 Number of \u20B95 coins = 4 \xD7 5 = 20\n\u2234 The correct answer is 20.\n\nAdditional Information\nCoins and Denominations\n\nThe total value of any denomination is calculated by multiplying the face value of the coin with the number of coins (Value = Denomination \xD7 Count).\n\nPercentage Relationships\n\nIf quantity A is R% less than quantity B, then A = B \xD7 (100 - R) \xF7 100. This relationship is often used to find the ratio between multiple quantities quickly.\n\nLinear Equations\n\nWord problems often translate into linear equations format ax + b = c, where solving for the common ratio variable 'y' or 'x' gives the exact values for each parameter.",
