        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nWhen tangents from an external point P intersect a circle, and the chord of contact is at a distance d from the centre:\n\nDistance of P from centre OP = (Radius)\xB2 \xF7 d\n\u21D2 OP = 6.52 \xF7 2.5\n\u21D2 OP = 42.25 \xF7 2.5 = 16.9 cm\n\u2234 The correct answer is 16.9 cm.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nRadius of the circle, OA = 6.5 cm\nDistance of chord from the centre, OM = 2.5 cm\n\nFormula Used:\nHypotenuse2 = Perpendicular2 + Base2\n\nCalculations:\nO\nA\nB\nP\nM\n6.5 / 2.5\nOP = 16.9 cm\n\u21D2 In right \u0394OMA, by Pythagoras theorem:\n\u21D2 AM = \u221A(OA2 - OM2)\n\u21D2 AM = \u221A(6.52 - 2.52) = \u221A(42.25 - 6.25) = \u221A36 = 6 cm\n\u21D2 Tangent PA is perpendicular to radius OA, so \u2220OAP = 90\xB0.\n\u21D2 In right \u0394OAP, AM is the altitude from the right angle to hypotenuse OP.\n\u21D2 By the geometric mean property of right triangles: OA2 = OM \xD7 OP\n\u21D2 6.52 = 2.5 \xD7 OP\n\u21D2 42.25 = 2.5 \xD7 OP\n\u21D2 OP = 42.25 \xF7 2.5 = 16.9 cm\n\u2234 The correct answer is 16.9 cm.\n\nAdditional Information\nTangent to a Circle\n\nA tangent at any point of a circle is perpendicular to the radius through the point of contact.\n\nChord of Contact\n\nThe line joining the points of contact of two tangents drawn from an external point to a circle is called the chord of contact.\n\nRight-Angled Triangle Properties\n\nIn a right \u0394ABC right angled at A, if AD \u22A5 BC, then AB2 = BD \xD7 BC and AC2 = CD \xD7 BC.",
        topic: "Geometry",
        subtopic: "Circles - Tangents & Secants",
