        status: "Unattempted",
        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "C",
        userTime: "00:06",
        avgTime: "00:28",
        question: "A girl cycles from A to B, a distance of 25 km in 2 hours 20 minutes. The road from A is a levelled road for 15 km and then it slopes down to B. The average speed of the girl on the levelled road is 10 km/h. Her average downhill speed (in km/h) is:",
        options: {
          a: "10",
          b: "15",
          c: "12",
          d: "18"
        },
        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal time = 2 hr 20 min = 7/3 hours\nTime spent on levelled road = 15 \xF7 10 = 3/2 hours\nRemaining time for downhill = 7/3 - 3/2 = 5/6 hours\nDownhill distance = 25 - 15 = 10 km\nDownhill speed = 10 \xF7 (5/6) = 12 km/h\n\u2234 The correct answer is 12 km/h.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal distance = 25 km\nTotal time = 2 hours 20 minutes = 2 + 20/60 = 7/3 hours\nDistance of levelled road = 15 km\nSpeed on levelled road = 10 km/h\n\nFormula Used:\nTime = Distance \xF7 Speed\nSpeed = Distance \xF7 Time\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Time taken to cover the levelled road = 15 \xF7 10 = 1.5 hours = 3/2 hours\n\u21D2 Remaining distance (downhill) = Total distance - Distance of levelled road\n\u21D2 Remaining distance = 25 - 15 = 10 km\n\u21D2 Remaining time = Total time - Time on levelled road\n\u21D2 Remaining time = 7/3 - 3/2 = (14 - 9) / 6 = 5/6 hours\n\u21D2 Average downhill speed = Remaining distance \xF7 Remaining time\n\u21D2 Average downhill speed = 10 \xF7 (5/6) = (10 \xD7 6) / 5 = 12 km/h\n\u2234 The correct answer is 12 km/h.\n\nAdditional Information\nAverage Speed\n\nAverage speed is the total distance covered divided by the total time taken. Formula: Average Speed = Total Distance \xF7 Total Time.\n\nAverage Speed (Equal Distances)\n\nIf two equal distances are covered at speeds x and y, the average speed for the whole journey is given by 2xy \xF7 (x + y).\n\nRelative Speed\n\nWhen two bodies move in the same direction, relative speed = |S1 - S2|. When moving in opposite directions, relative speed = S1 + S2.",
