        userTime: "00:01",
        avgTime: "00:21",
        question: "There are 12 men on a Basketball team and in a game 5 of them play at any one time. If the game is 1 hour long and if each man plays exactly the same amount of time, how many minutes does each man play?",
        options: {
          a: "20",
          b: "25",
          c: "15",
          d: "30"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal active playing time on the court = Number of active players \xD7 Game duration.\nTotal playing time = 5 \xD7 60 = 300 minutes.\n\nSince this playing time is exactly equally distributed among all 12 players, we divide the total time by 12.\n\nTime per player = 300 \xF7 12 = 25 minutes.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 25 minutes.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal players on the basketball team = 12\nNumber of players active on the court at any one time = 5\nDuration of the game = 1 hour = 60 minutes\n\nFormula Used:\nTotal player-minutes = Number of active players \xD7 Game duration\nTime per player = Total player-minutes \xF7 Total number of players\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total player-minutes = 5 \xD7 60\n\u21D2 Total player-minutes = 300 minutes\n\u21D2 As the total court time is shared equally among 12 players, we divide the total minutes by 12.\n\u21D2 Time per player = 300 \xF7 12\n\u21D2 Time per player = 25 minutes\n\u2234 The correct answer is 25 minutes.\n\nAdditional Information\nMan-Hours Concept\n\nWhen an activity requires a constant number of individuals active at all times, the total accumulated effort is the product of the active individuals and the duration: Total Time = Active Members \xD7 Duration.\n\nEqual Distribution (Average)\n\nIf a total continuous resource must be shared exactly equally among a group, the amount received per individual is calculated as Average = Total Quantity \xF7 Total Number of Individuals.",
