        avgTime: "00:33",
        question: "Three solid iron cubes of edges 8 cm, 10 cm and 12 cm are melted together to make a new cube. It is observed that 496 cm3 of the melted material is lost due to improper handling. The area (in cm2) of the whole surface of the newly formed cube is:",
        options: {
          a: "1331",
          b: "1176",
          c: "2197",
          d: "3375"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal volume of given cubes = 83 + 103 + 123 = 512 + 1000 + 1728 = 3240 cm3\nVolume of the new cube = 3240 - 496 = 2744 cm3\nSide of the new cube (a) = 3\u221A2744 = 14 cm\nTotal Surface Area = 6a2 = 6 \xD7 142 = 6 \xD7 196 = 1176 cm2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1176 cm2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nEdges of the three solid iron cubes = 8 cm, 10 cm, and 12 cm\nMelted material lost due to improper handling = 496 cm3\n\nFormula Used:\nVolume of a cube = a3\nTotal surface area of a cube = 6a2\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total volume of the three smaller cubes = (83 + 103 + 123) cm3\n\u21D2 Total volume = 512 + 1000 + 1728 = 3240 cm3\n\u21D2 Volume of the newly formed cube = Total Initial Volume - Material Lost\n\u21D2 Volume of the new cube = 3240 - 496 = 2744 cm3\n\u21D2 Let the edge length of the new cube be 'a' cm.\n\u21D2 a3 = 2744\n\u21D2 a = 3\u221A2744 = 14 cm\n\u21D2 Area of the whole surface of the new cube = 6a2\n\u21D2 Surface Area = 6 \xD7 (14)\xB2\n\u21D2 Surface Area = 6 \xD7 196 = 1176 cm2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1176 cm2.\n\nAdditional Information\nTotal Surface Area of a Cube\n\nThe total surface area of a cube is the combined area of its 6 identical square faces. Formula: TSA = 6a2.\n\nLateral Surface Area of a Cube\n\nThe lateral surface area includes only the 4 vertical faces, excluding the top and bottom faces. Formula: LSA = 4a2.\n\nVolume of a Cube\n\nThe volume of a cube represents the 3D space occupied by it. Formula: Volume = a3.\n\nDiagonal of a Cube\n\nThe length of the longest line segment connecting two opposite interior corners of a cube. Formula: Diagonal = a\u221A3.",
