        userTime: "00:01",
        avgTime: "00:37",
        question: "In a company, there are only two types of employees, workers, and officers. 35% of the employees are officers and the average monthly salary of an officer is \u20B939,000 more than the combined average monthly salary of all employees. What is the difference between the average monthly salaries of an officer and a worker?",
        options: {
          a: "\u20B952,650",
          b: "\u20B950,700",
          c: "\u20B964,350",
          d: "\u20B960,000"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nRatio of Officers : Workers = 35% : 65% = 7 : 13.\nDeviation of Officer's salary from the combined average = +\u20B939,000.\nApplying the net deviation rule: Sum of deviations = 0.\n7 \xD7 (+39,000) + 13 \xD7 (Worker's deviation) = 0.\nWorker's deviation = -(7 \xD7 39,000) \xF7 13 = -\u20B921,000.\nTotal difference = Officer's surplus + Worker's deficit = 39,000 + 21,000 = \u20B960,000.\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B960,000.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nPercentage of Officers = 35%\nPercentage of Workers = 100% - 35% = 65%\nAvgOfficer - AvgTotal = \u20B939,000\n\nFormula Used:\nWeighted Average: n1(A1 - Aavg) = n2(Aavg - A2)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Ratio of Officers (nO) to Workers (nW) = 35 : 65 = 7 : 13\n\u21D2 Let AvgTotal be A, then AvgOfficer = A + 39,000\n\u21D2 Let AvgWorker be AW\n\u21D2 7 \xD7 (AvgOfficer - A) = 13 \xD7 (A - AvgWorker)\n\u21D2 7 \xD7 (39,000) = 13 \xD7 (A - AvgWorker)\n\u21D2 A - AvgWorker = (7 \xD7 39,000) \xF7 13\n\u21D2 A - AvgWorker = 7 \xD7 3,000 = 21,000\n\u21D2 Difference = AvgOfficer - AvgWorker\n\u21D2 Difference = (AvgOfficer - A) + (A - AvgWorker)\n\u21D2 Difference = 39,000 + 21,000 = 60,000\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B960,000.\n\nAdditional Information\nAlligation Rule for Averages\n\nThe ratio of the quantities of two groups is the inverse ratio of the differences of their individual averages from the combined average: n1/n2 = (A2 - Aavg) / (Aavg - A1).\n\nNet Deviation Method\n\nIn any distribution, the sum of the products of the frequency and the deviation of each value from the mean is always zero: \u2211 fi(xi - x\u0304) = 0.\n\nWeighted Average Formula\n\nThe combined average of two groups is given by Aavg = (n1A1 + n2A2) / (n1 + n2), where n represents the number of items and A represents the average.",
