        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nRatio of Radius (r) to Height (h) = 33.33% = 1 : 3.\nLet r = x and h = 3x.\nVolume of Cone = (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 x2 \xD7 3x = \u03C0x3.\nGiven: \u03C0x3 = 27\u03C0 \u21D2 x3 = 27 \u21D2 x = 3.\nRadius = 3 cm, Height = 3 \xD7 3 = 9 cm.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 3 cm and 9 cm.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nVolume (V) = 27\u03C0 cm3\nRadius (r) = 33.33% of Height (h)\n\nFormula Used:\nVolume of a Right Circular Cone = (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2 \xD7 h\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 r = 33.33/100 \xD7 h \u21D2 r = (1/3)h\n\u21D2 h = 3r\n\u21D2 Volume = (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2 \xD7 (3r)\n\u21D2 27\u03C0 = (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r2 \xD7 3r\n\u21D2 27\u03C0 = \u03C0r3\n\u21D2 r3 = 27\n\u21D2 r = \u221A327 = 3 cm\n\u21D2 h = 3 \xD7 3 = 9 cm\n\u2234 The correct answer is 3 cm and 9 cm.\n\nAdditional Information\nCurved Surface Area (CSA) of Cone\n\nThe formula for CSA of a cone is \u03C0rl, where l is the slant height.\n\nSlant Height Formula\n\nThe slant height (l) of a cone is given by l = \u221A(r2 + h2).\nTotal Surface Area (TSA) of Cone\nThe TSA of a cone is given by the sum of CSA and base area: TSA = \u03C0rl + \u03C0r2 = \u03C0r(l + r).\n\nVolume Relation\n\nThe volume of a cone is exactly 1/3rd of the volume of a cylinder with the same radius and height (\u03C0r2h).",
