        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nRatio of Capitals: 70,000 : 1,05,000 : 1,40,000 = 2 : 3 : 4\nRatio of Time: 36 months : 30 months : 24 months = 6 : 5 : 4\nProfit Ratio = (Capital \xD7 Time) Ratio\nProfit Ratio = (2 \xD7 6) : (3 \xD7 5) : (4 \xD7 4) = 12 : 15 : 16\n\u2234 The correct answer is 12 : 15 : 16.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nAman investment = \u20B970,000 | Rakhi investment = \u20B91,05,000 | Sagar investment = \u20B91,40,000\nAman time = 3 years = 36 months\nRakhi time = 36 - 6 = 30 months\nSagar time = 30 - 6 = 24 months\nFormula: Profit Ratio = (Investment1 \xD7 Time1) : (Investment2 \xD7 Time2) : (Investment3 \xD7 Time3)\n\u21D2 Profit Ratio = (70000 \xD7 36) : (105000 \xD7 30) : (140000 \xD7 24)\n\u21D2 Simplifying by 1000: (70 \xD7 36) : (105 \xD7 30) : (140 \xD7 24)\n\u21D2 Dividing by 35: (2 \xD7 36) : (3 \xD7 30) : (4 \xD7 24)\n\u21D2 Dividing by 6: (2 \xD7 6) : (3 \xD7 5) : (4 \xD7 4)\n\u21D2 Profit Ratio = 12 : 15 : 16\n\u2234 The correct answer is 12 : 15 : 16.\n\nAdditional Information\nBasic Partnership Rule\n\nProfit is always distributed in the ratio of the product of Capital and Time Period (P = C \xD7 T).\n\nWorking vs. Sleeping Partner\n\nA working partner manages the business and may receive a salary or commission before the remaining profit is shared among all partners.\n\nVariable Investment\n\nIf a partner changes their investment amount during the year, total profit share is calculated as \u03A3(Capitaln \xD7 Timen).",
