        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nTime taken by A = (Distance \xF7 Speed) = 100 \xF7 (6 \xD7 5/18) = 60 seconds.\n\nB takes 12 seconds more to cover 4m less distance.\n\nTime taken by B = 60 + 12 = 72 seconds.\nDistance covered by B = 100 - 4 = 96 m.\nSpeed of B = (96 \xF7 72) \xD7 (18/5) = 4.8 km/hr.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 4.8 km/hr.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal Race Distance = 100 m\nSpeed of A = 6 km/hRs. tart given to B = 4 m\nTime lag (A beats B) = 12 seconds\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Speed of A in m/s = 6 \xD7 (5/18) = 5/3 m/s\n\u21D2 Time taken by A to finish 100m = 100 \xF7 (5/3) = 60 seconds\n\u21D2 Since A beats B by 12 seconds, B takes (60 + 12) = 72 seconds\n\u21D2 Distance covered by B = Total Distance - Start = 100 - 4 = 96 m\n\u21D2 Speed of B = Distance \xF7 Time = 96 \xF7 72 = 4/3 m/s\n\u21D2 Speed of B in km/hr = (4/3) \xD7 (18/5)\n\u21D2 Speed of B = 24/5 = 4.8 km/hr\n\u2234 The correct answer is 4.8 km/hr.\n\nAdditional Information\nRace Terminology\n\n'A gives B a start of x meters' means B starts x meters ahead of A. 'A beats B by t seconds' means A finishes the race t seconds before B.\n\nUnit Conversion\n\nTo convert km/hr to m/s, multiply by 5/18. To convert m/s to km/hr, multiply by 18/5.\n\nDead Heat\n\nA dead heat occurs when all participants finish the race at the exact same time, meaning the time taken by each is equal.",
