        solution: "Solution\n\nGiven:\n\\(1 \\frac{3}{4} + 5 \\frac{1}{3} + 3 \\frac{2}{x} = 10 \\frac{29}{60}\\)\n\nFormula used:\n\\(A \\frac{b}{c} = A + \\frac{b}{c}\\)\n\nCalculation:\n\\(1 \\frac{3}{4} + 5 \\frac{1}{3} + 3 \\frac{2}{x} = 10 \\frac{29}{60}\\)\n\n\u21D2 \\((1 + 5 + 3) + (\\frac{3}{4} + \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{2}{x}) = 10 + \\frac{29}{60}\\)\n\u21D2 \\(9 + \\frac{9 + 4}{12} + \\frac{2}{x} = 10 + \\frac{29}{60}\\)\n\u21D2 \\(9 + \\frac{13}{12} + \\frac{2}{x} = 10 + \\frac{29}{60}\\)\n\u21D2 \\(9 + 1 + \\frac{1}{12} + \\frac{2}{x} = 10 + \\frac{29}{60}\\)\n\u21D2 \\(10 + \\frac{1}{12} + \\frac{2}{x} = 10 + \\frac{29}{60}\\)\n\u21D2 \\(\\frac{1}{12} + \\frac{2}{x} = \\frac{29}{60}\\)\n\u21D2 \\(\\frac{2}{x} = \\frac{29}{60} - \\frac{5}{60}\\)\n\u21D2 \\(\\frac{2}{x} = \\frac{24}{60}\\)\n\u21D2 \\(\\frac{2}{x} = \\frac{2}{5}\\)\n\u21D2 x = 5\n\u2234 The correct answer is option (2).",
