        correctOption: "A",
        userTime: "00:08",
        avgTime: "00:44",
        question: "If the radii of two circular ends of a bucket are 15 cm and 7 cm and the curved surface area of the bucket is 374\u03C0 cm^2, find the volume of the bucket.",
        options: {
          a: "1895\u03C0",
          b: "6788\u03C0",
          c: "1564\u03C0",
          d: "1687\u03C0"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nSlant height l = CSA \xF7 [\u03C0 \xD7 (R + r)] = 374\u03C0 \xF7 (22\u03C0) = 17 cm.\nHeight h = \u221A(l2 - (R - r)\xB2) = \u221A(172 - 82) = \u221A(289 - 64) = 15 cm.\nVolume = (\u03C0 \xD7 h \xF7 3) \xD7 (R2 + r2 + R \xD7 r) = 5\u03C0 \xD7 (225 + 49 + 105).\nVolume = 5\u03C0 \xD7 379 = 1895\u03C0 cm3.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1895\u03C0 cm3.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nRadius of larger end (R) = 15 cm\nRadius of smaller end (r) = 7 cm\nCurved Surface Area (CSA) = 374\u03C0 cm2\n\nFormula Used:\nCSA of frustum = \u03C0(R + r)l\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 CSA = \u03C0(R + r)l\n\u21D2 374\u03C0 = \u03C0(15 + 7) \xD7 l\n\u21D2 374 = 22 \xD7 l\n\u21D2 l = 374 \xF7 22 = 17 cm\n\u21D2 l2 = h2 + (R - r)\xB2\n\u21D2 172 = h2 + (15 - 7)\xB2\n\u21D2 289 = h2 + 82\n\u21D2 289 = h2 + 64\n\u21D2 h2 = 225\n\u21D2 h = 15 cm\n\u21D2 Volume = (1 \xF7 3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 15 \xD7 (152 + 72 + 15 \xD7 7)\n\u21D2 Volume = 5\u03C0 \xD7 (225 + 49 + 105)\n\u21D2 Volume = 5\u03C0 \xD7 379\n\u21D2 Volume = 1895\u03C0 cm3\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1895\u03C0 cm3.\n\nAdditional Information\nTotal Surface Area of Frustum\n\nThe total surface area includes the curved area and the area of both circular bases: TSA = \u03C0l(R + r) + \u03C0R2 + \u03C0r2.\n\nSlant Height Relation\n\nThe slant height l of a frustum is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs h and (R - r), given by l = \u221A[h2 + (R - r)\xB2].\n\nVolume of a Cone\n\nThe volume of a full cone is a special case of a frustum where r = 0, expressed as V = (1/3)\u03C0R2h.",
