        userTime: "00:16",
        avgTime: "00:49",
        question: "A sum of Rs. 66,550 is taken on loan. This is to be paid back in two equal instalments. If the rate of interest is 20% compounded annually, find the value of each instalment.",
        options: {
          a: "Rs. 42,560",
          b: "Rs. 44,550",
          c: "Rs. 40,550",
          d: "Rs. 43,560"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nRate = 20% = 1/5 \u2192 (Principal : Amount) = 5 : 6\nFor 2 years, equate instalments: (5 \xD7 6 : 6 \xD7 6) and (52 : 62)\nYear 1: 30 : 36 | Year 2: 25 : 36\nTotal Principal = 30 + 25 = 55 units\n55 units = \u20B966,550 \u21D2 1 unit = \u20B91,210\nEach instalment = 36 units = 36 \xD7 1,210 = \u20B943,560\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B943,560.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nPrincipal (P) = \u20B966,550\nRate of Interest (R) = 20% p.a.\nNumber of instalments (n) = 2\n\nFormula Used:\nP = x / (1 + R/100)1 + x / (1 + R/100)\xB2 where x = instalment value.\n\nCalculation:\n\u21D2 66,550 = x / (1 + 20/100) + x / (1 + 20/100)\xB2\n\u21D2 66,550 = x / 1.2 + x / 1.44\n\u21D2 66,550 = (1.2x + x) / 1.44\n\u21D2 66,550 = 2.2x / 1.44\n\u21D2 x = (66,550 \xD7 1.44) / 2.2\n\u21D2 x = 30,250 \xD7 1.44\n\u21D2 x = 43,560\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B943,560.\n\nAdditional Information\nCompound Interest Instalment Formula\n\nFor n years, Principal P = x [1/k + 1/k2 + ... + 1/kn], where k = (1 + R/100) and x is the annual instalment.\n\nSimple Interest Instalment\n\nIn SI, the instalment x = (100 \xD7 A) / [100n + RTn(n-1)/2], where A is the total debt amount to be paid.\n\nEffective Rate of Interest\n\nFor CI, the effective rate for 2 years is R + R + (R \xD7 R)/100. For 20%, it is 20 + 20 + 4 = 44%.",
