        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nRate (R) = 5% = 1/20 \u2192 Installment Factor = 21/20.\nFor 2 installments: Principal (P) = x \xD7 [ (20/21) + (20/21)\xB2 ]\n30,000 = x \xD7 [ 20/21 + 400/441 ] = x \xD7 [ 820 / 441 ]\nx = (30,000 \xD7 441) \xF7 820 \u2248 16,134.14\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B916,134.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven: Principal (P) = \u20B930,000 | Rate (R) = 5% | Time (n) = 2 years | Equal Installments = x\nFormula: Principal = [ x \xF7 (1 + R/100)1 ] + [ x \xF7 (1 + R/100)\xB2 ]\n\u21D2 30,000 = x \xF7 (1.05) + x \xF7 (1.05)\xB2\n\u21D2 30,000 = x \xD7 (1 \xF7 1.05 + 1 \xF7 1.1025)\n\u21D2 30,000 = x \xD7 (0.95238 + 0.90703)\n\u21D2 30,000 = x \xD7 1.85941\n\u21D2 x = 30,000 \xF7 1.85941\n\u21D2 x \u2248 16134.14\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B916,134.\n\nAdditional Information\nCI Installment General Formula\n\nFor n installments, Principal P = x \xF7 k1 + x \xF7 k2 + ... + x \xF7 kn, where k = (1 + r/100).\n\nEffective Interest Rate\n\nThe effective compound rate for 2 years is Reff = 2R + R2/100. For 5%, Reff = 10.25%.\n\nPresent Value Concept\n\nEach installment paid in the future is discounted back to the present day using the compound interest rate to equate it with the initial borrowed principal.",
