        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nUse the value substitution method by picking a specific angle, let \u03B8 = 30\xB0.\n\nSubstitute values: tan 30\xB0 = 1/\u221A3, cot 30\xB0 = \u221A3, sec 30\xB0 = 2/\u221A3, sin 30\xB0 = 1/2.\nExpression = (1/\u221A3 + \u221A3) \xD7 (2/\u221A3 + 1/\u221A3) \xD7 (1 - 1/2) = (4/\u221A3) \xD7 (3/\u221A3) \xD7 (1/2).\nExpression = (4/\u221A3) \xD7 \u221A3 \xD7 1/2 = 2.\nCheck options for \u03B8 = 30\xB0: cosec 30\xB0 = 1/sin 30\xB0 = 1/(1/2) = 2.\n\u2234 The correct answer is cosec \u03B8.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven: The expression (tan \u03B8 + cot \u03B8) (sec \u03B8 + tan \u03B8) (1 - sin \u03B8) for 0\xB0 < \u03B8 < 90\xB0.\nFormula Used: tan \u03B8 = sin \u03B8/cos \u03B8; cot \u03B8 = cos \u03B8/sin \u03B8; sec \u03B8 = 1/cos \u03B8; sin\xB2\u03B8 + cos\xB2\u03B8 = 1.\n\u21D2 Simplifying (tan \u03B8 + cot \u03B8) = (sin \u03B8 / cos \u03B8 + cos \u03B8 / sin \u03B8) = (sin\xB2\u03B8 + cos\xB2\u03B8) / (sin \u03B8 cos \u03B8)\n\u21D2 (tan \u03B8 + cot \u03B8) = 1 / (sin \u03B8 cos \u03B8)\n\u21D2 Simplifying (sec \u03B8 + tan \u03B8)(1 - sin \u03B8) = (1/cos \u03B8 + sin \u03B8/cos \u03B8)(1 - sin \u03B8)\n\u21D2 ((1 + sin \u03B8) / cos \u03B8) \xD7 (1 - sin \u03B8) = (1 - sin\xB2\u03B8) / cos \u03B8\n\u21D2 cos\xB2\u03B8 / cos \u03B8 = cos \u03B8\n\u21D2 Multiplying both parts: [1 / (sin \u03B8 cos \u03B8)] \xD7 cos \u03B8 = 1 / sin \u03B8\n\u21D2 1 / sin \u03B8 = cosec \u03B8\n\u2234 The correct answer is cosec \u03B8.\n\nAdditional Information\nReciprocal Identities\n\nTrigonometric ratios are related by reciprocals: cosec \u03B8 = 1/sin \u03B8, sec \u03B8 = 1/cos \u03B8, and cot \u03B8 = 1/tan \u03B8.\n\nPythagorean Identities\n\nFundamental identities include sin\xB2\u03B8 + cos\xB2\u03B8 = 1, 1 + tan\xB2\u03B8 = sec\xB2\u03B8, and 1 + cot\xB2\u03B8 = cosec\xB2\u03B8.\n\nQuotient Identities\n\nThe tangent and cotangent functions can be expressed as ratios: tan \u03B8 = sin \u03B8/cos \u03B8 and cot \u03B8 = cos \u03B8/sin \u03B8.",
