        question: "A swimming pool is constructed in the shape of a right-angled triangle. One side is five-third of the length of the second side (leaving the longest side). If the management decides to increase the length of one side by 4 m and decrease the second side by 2 m such that the area of the swimming pool remains the same, then what was the length of one side before the alteration happened?",
        options: {
          a: "18 m",
          b: "20 m",
          c: "22 m",
          d: "16 m"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nRatio of sides (excluding hypotenuse) = 5 : 3.\nLet the sides be 5x and 3x. Area = (1/2) \xD7 5x \xD7 3x = 7.5x2.\nAccording to the condition: (5x + 4)(3x - 2) = 15x2 (since area is halved by 2).\n\u21D2 15x2 - 10x + 12x - 8 = 15x2.\n\u21D2 2x = 8 \u21D2 x = 4.\nSides are: 5 \xD7 4 = 20 m and 3 \xD7 4 = 12 m.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 20 m.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven: Side1 = (5/3) \xD7 Side2.\nFormula: Area of right - angled triangle = (1/2) \xD7 Base \xD7 Height.\nLet the second side be 3x and the first side be 5x.\n\u21D2 Initial Area = (1/2) \xD7 5x \xD7 3x = 7.5x2 m2.\n\u21D2 New sides after alteration = (5x + 4) and (3x - 2).\n\u21D2 New Area = (1/2) \xD7 (5x + 4) \xD7 (3x - 2).\n\u21D2 Since Area remains same: (1/2) \xD7 5x \xD7 3x = (1/2) \xD7 (5x + 4) \xD7 (3x - 2).\n\u21D2 15x2 = 15x2 - 10x + 12x - 8.\n\u21D2 2x = 8.\n\u21D2 x = 4.\n\u21D2 Length of Side 1 = 5 \xD7 4 = 20 m.\n\u21D2 Length of Side 2 = 3 \xD7 4 = 12 m.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 20 m.\n\nAdditional Information\nPythagoras Theorem\n\nIn a right - angled triangle, the square of the hypotenuse is equal to the sum of the squares of the other two sides: a2 + b2 = c2.\n\nHeron\u2019s Formula\n\nFor any triangle with sides a, b, and c, Area = \u221A[s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)], where s = (a + b + c)/2.\n\nTriangle Area Property\n\nIf the product of the base and height remains constant, the area of the triangle remains unchanged.",
