        userTime: "00:50",
        avgTime: "00:41",
        question: "Shyam is travelling on his cycle and has calculated to reach point 'A' at 2 PM If he travels at 10 kmph. he will reach there at 12 noon if he travels at 15 kmph. At what speed must he travel to reach 'A' at 1 PM:",
        options: {
          a: "12 kmph",
          b: "14 kmph",
          c: "8 kmph",
          d: "11 kmph"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nThe target time (1 PM) is the exact midpoint between 12 noon and 2 PM.\n\nWhen the distance is constant and the required time is the arithmetic mean of two given times, the required speed is the Harmonic Mean of the two speeds.\n\nRequired Speed = (2 \xD7 S1 \xD7 S2) \xF7 (S1 + S2)\nRequired Speed = (2 \xD7 10 \xD7 15) \xF7 (10 + 15) = 300 \xF7 25 = 12 kmph.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 12 kmph.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nSpeed 1 (S1) = 10 kmph (Reaches at 2 PM)\nSpeed 2 (S2) = 15 kmph (Reaches at 12 noon)\nTime difference (\u0394T) = 2 PM - 12 noon = 2 hours.\n\nFormula Used:\nDistance (D) = (S1 \xD7 S2 \xD7 \u0394T) \xF7 (S2 - S1)\nSpeed = Distance \xF7 Time\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 D = (10 \xD7 15 \xD7 2) \xF7 (15 - 10)\n\u21D2 D = 300 \xF7 5 = 60 km.\n\u21D2 Time taken at 10 kmph = 60 \xF7 10 = 6 hours.\n\u21D2 If he reaches at 2 PM after 6 hours, he started at = 2 PM - 6 hours = 8 AM.\n\u21D2 To reach at 1 PM, target duration = 1 PM - 8 AM = 5 hours.\n\u21D2 Required Speed = Total Distance \xF7 Target Duration\n\u21D2 Required Speed = 60 \xF7 5 = 12 kmph.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 12 kmph.\n\nAdditional Information\nDistance - Speed Inverse Relation\n\nWhen distance is constant, speed is inversely proportional to time (S1/S2 = T2/T1).\n\nAverage Speed (Equal Distances)\n\nIf a person covers equal distances at speeds x and y, the average speed is 2xy \xF7 (x + y).\n\nSpeed Units Conversion\n\nTo convert kmph to m/s, multiply by 5/18. To convert m/s to kmph, multiply by 18/5.",
