        question: "A vertical cross-section along the middle of a cylinder with a height of 15 cm and a base radius of 7 cm is cut out. Find the area of the cross-section portion in cm^2.",
        options: {
          a: "154",
          b: "186",
          c: "142",
          d: "210"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nVertical cross - section of a cylinder along the middle is a rectangle.\n\nDimensions of this rectangle: Width = Diameter (2r) and Length = Height (h).\nWidth = 2 \xD7 7 = 14 cm\nArea = Width \xD7 Height = 14 \xD7 15\nArea = 210 cm2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 210 cm2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nRadius of cylinder (r) = 7 cm\nHeight of cylinder (h) = 15 cm\nFormula: Area of vertical cross - section = 2 \xD7 r \xD7 h\n\u21D2 Diameter of the base (d) = 2 \xD7 Radius\n\u21D2 d = 2 \xD7 7 = 14 cm\n\u21D2 The vertical cross - section is a rectangle with length 15 cm and breadth 14 cm.\n\u21D2 Area of the rectangle = Length \xD7 Breadth\n\u21D2 Area = 15 \xD7 14\n\u21D2 Area = 210 cm2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 210 cm2.\n\nAdditional Information\nHorizontal Cross - section\n\nA horizontal cross - section (parallel to the base) of a cylinder is always a circle with area \u03C0r2.\n\nVolume of Cylinder\n\nThe volume of a cylinder is calculated as V = \u03C0r2h, representing the total capacity.\nTotal Surface Area (TSA)\n\nThe TSA of a cylinder includes the curved surface and two circular bases: TSA = 2\u03C0rh + 2\u03C0r2 = 2\u03C0r(h + r).\n\nDiagonal of Vertical Cross - section\n\nThe diagonal of the rectangular cross - section can be found using \u221A((2r)\xB2 + h2).",
        topic: "Mensuration 3D",
        subtopic: "Cylinder",
        conceptTested: "Cross-sectional area of a cylinder along its axis forming a rectangular shape with dimensions equal to diameter and height.",
        tags: {
          topic: "Mensuration 3D",
          subtopic: "Cylinder",
          conceptTested: "Cross-sectional area of a cylinder along its axis forming a rectangular shape with dimensions equal to diameter and height.",
          difficulty: "medium"
        }
