        userTime: "00:03",
        avgTime: "00:15",
        question: "What annual instalment will discharge a debt of Rs. 8,154 due in 3 years at 13.25% simple interest per annum? [Note: Instalments will be paid at the end of Year 1, Year 2 and Year 3.]",
        options: {
          a: "Rs. 2,400",
          b: "Rs. 2,368",
          c: "Rs. 2,468",
          d: "Rs. 2,718"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nLet the annual instalment be 100%.\n\nTotal amount paid to clear the debt includes the simple interest earned on each instalment up to the end of 3 years.\n\n\u21D2 Total Debt = 100% + (100% + 13.25%) + (100% + 2 \xD7 13.25%)\n\u21D2 Total Debt = 100% + 113.25% + 126.5% = 339.75%\n\u21D2 339.75% = Rs. 8154 \u21D2 100% = (8154 \xF7 339.75) \xD7 100 = Rs. 2400\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 2, 400.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nDebt (A) = Rs. 8, 154\nTime (T) = 3 years\nRate (R) = 13.25% p.a.\n\nFormula Used:\nAnnual Instalment = (100 \xD7 A) \xF7 [100 \xD7 T + (R \xD7 T \xD7 (T - 1)) \xF7 2]\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Annual Instalment = (100 \xD7 8154) \xF7 [100 \xD7 3 + (13.25 \xD7 3 \xD7 2) \xF7 2]\n\u21D2 Annual Instalment = 815400 \xF7 [300 + 39.75]\n\u21D2 Annual Instalment = 815400 \xF7 339.75\n\u21D2 Annual Instalment = 2400\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 2, 400.\n\nAdditional Information\nSimple Interest Instalment\n\nInstalments paid earlier earn interest until the end of the term. For a debt due in n years, the first instalment earns interest for (n - 1) years, while the last instalment earns none.\n\nCompound Interest Instalment\n\nWhen clearing a loan with compound interest, the present value of all instalments equals the principal borrowed: P = x \xF7 (1 + R \xF7 100) + x \xF7 (1 + R \xF7 100)2 + ...\n\nPresent Worth and True Discount\n\nPresent Worth (PW) is the actual borrowed amount. The Debt (A) is the sum of Present Worth and True Discount (TD), where TD = (PW \xD7 R \xD7 T) \xF7 100.",
        topic: "Simple Interest",
        subtopic: "Installments",
