        status: "Unattempted",
        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "A",
        userTime: "00:48",
        avgTime: "00:57",
        question: "A TV and an air conditioner were sold for \u20B99,600 each. The TV was sold at a loss of 20% and the AC was sold at a profit of 20%. What is the net result?",
        options: {
          a: "Loss of \u20B9800",
          b: "Gain of \u20B9800",
          c: "No loss or gain",
          d: "Gain of \u20B91,600"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nWhen two items are sold at the same price, one at a profit of x% and the other at a loss of x%, there is always a net loss.\n\nNet Loss % = (x \xF7 10)2 % = (20 \xF7 10)2 = 4%.\nTotal Selling Price (SP) = \u20B99, 600 + \u20B99, 600 = \u20B919, 200.\n\nSince the loss is 4%, the Total SP is equivalent to 96% of the Total Cost Price (CP).\n\nLoss value = Total SP \xD7 [4% \xF7 96%] = 19200 \xD7 (1 \xF7 24) = \u20B9800.\n\u2234 The correct answer is Loss of \u20B9800.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nSP of TV = \u20B99, 600 (Sold at a 20% loss)\nSP of Air Conditioner (AC) = \u20B99, 600 (Sold at a 20% profit)\n\nFormula Used:\nCost Price (CP) = (Selling Price \xD7 100) \xF7 (100 \xB1 Profit/Loss %)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total Selling Price = 9600 + 9600 = \u20B919, 200\n\u21D2 Cost Price of TV = (9600 \xD7 100) \xF7 (100 - 20)\n\u21D2 Cost Price of TV = 960000 \xF7 80 = \u20B912, 000\n\u21D2 Cost Price of AC = (9600 \xD7 100) \xF7 (100 + 20)\n\u21D2 Cost Price of AC = 960000 \xF7 120 = \u20B98, 000\n\u21D2 Total Cost Price = 12000 + 8000 = \u20B920, 000\n\u21D2 Since Total CP > Total SP, there is a net loss.\n\u21D2 Net Loss = Total CP - Total SP\n\u21D2 Net Loss = 20000 - 19200 = \u20B9800\n\u2234 The correct answer is Loss of \u20B9800.\n\nAdditional Information\nSame SP, Same Profit/Loss %\n\nIf two distinct items are sold at the same price, where one makes an x% profit and the other suffers an x% loss, the transaction always yields an overall net loss of (x \xF7 10)2 %.\n\nSame CP, Same Profit/Loss %\n\nIf a person buys two distinct items at the exact same cost price, and sells one at x% profit and the other at x% loss, the net result is neither profit nor loss (0% net change).\n\nSuccessive Percentage Rule\n\nWhenever a value is first increased by x% and then decreased by x% (or vice versa), the final value is always less than the initial value, resulting in a net decrement of (x\xB2 \xF7 100)%.",
        topic: "Profit, Loss & Discount",
