        testName: "Quantitative Aptitude Sectional Test - 10",
        platform: "Testbook",
        status: "Unattempted",
        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "B",
        userTime: "00:57",
        avgTime: "00:56",
        question: "The marked price of a car is Rs. 1900. Under a scheme successive discounts of 10% and 8% are offered on it. Find the total discount offered while selling the car under the given scheme.",
        options: {
          a: "316.8",
          b: "326.8",
          c: "226.8",
          d: "114.8"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nEquivalent discount % for successive discounts of a% and b% = a + b - (a \xD7 b) / 100\nNet discount % = 10 + 8 - (10 \xD7 8) / 100 = 18 - 0.8 = 17.2%\nTotal discount = 17.2% of Rs. 1900\nTotal discount = (17.2 / 100) \xD7 1900 = 17.2 \xD7 19 = 326.8\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 326.8.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nMarked Price (MP) = Rs. 1900\nSuccessive discounts = 10% and 8%\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 First discount = 10% of Rs. 1900\n\u21D2 First discount = (10 / 100) \xD7 1900 = Rs. 190\n\u21D2 Price after first discount = 1900 - 190 = Rs. 1710\n\u21D2 Second discount = 8% of Rs. 1710\n\u21D2 Second discount = (8 / 100) \xD7 1710 = Rs. 136.8\n\u21D2 Total discount offered = First discount + Second discount\n\u21D2 Total discount = 190 + 136.8 = 326.8\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 326.8.\n\nAdditional Information\nMarked Price (MP) and Discount\n\nMarked price is the price printed on an article. Discount is always calculated on the Marked Price. Selling Price (SP) = MP - Discount.\n\nSuccessive Discounts Formula\n\nWhen two successive discounts of a% and b% are given, the equivalent single discount is [a + b - (a \xD7 b) / 100]%.\n\nSelling Price after Successive Discounts\nFinal Selling Price (SP) = MP \xD7 (100 - a) / 100 \xD7 (100 - b) / 100.",
        topic: "Profit, Loss & Discount",
        subtopic: "Successive Discounts",
        conceptTested: "Equivalent single discount for successive discounts a% and b% is given by a + b - (ab)/100.",
