        userTime: "00:04",
        avgTime: "00:10",
        question: "Find the median of the following data. (Rounded off to 2 decimal places.) Class interval 0-5 5-10 10-15 15-20 20-25 25-30 30-35 Frequency 3 5 4 2 7 6 5",
        options: {
          a: "18.64",
          b: "20.53",
          c: "21.43",
          d: "23.40"
        },
        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal frequency N = 32 \u2192 N/2 = 16.\n\nCumulative frequency just > 16 is 21, so median class is 20 - 25.\n\nL = 20, CF = 14, f = 7, h = 5.\nMedian = 20 + [(16 - 14) \xF7 7] \xD7 5 = 20 + 10/7 \u2248 21.43.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 21.43.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal frequency (N) = 3 + 5 + 4 + 2 + 7 + 6 + 5 = 32\nCumulative frequencies (CF) for classes: 3, 8, 12, 14, 21, 27, 32\n\nFormula Used:\nMedian = L + [(N/2 - CF) \xF7 f] \xD7 h\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 N/2 = 32 \xF7 2 = 16\n\u21D2 The CF just greater than 16 is 21, which corresponds to the class interval 20 - 25.\n\u21D2 Lower limit of median class (L) = 20\n\u21D2 CF of preceding class (CF) = 14\n\u21D2 Frequency of median class (f) = 7\n\u21D2 Class size (h) = 5\n\u21D2 Median = 20 + [(16 - 14) \xF7 7] \xD7 5\n\u21D2 Median = 20 + (2 \xF7 7) \xD7 5\n\u21D2 Median = 20 + 10 \xF7 7\n\u21D2 Median = 20 + 1.428...\n\u21D2 Median \u2248 21.43\n\u2234 The correct answer is 21.43.\n\nAdditional Information\nMode of Grouped Data\n\nMode = L + [(f1 - f0) \xF7 (2f1 - f0 - f\xB2)] \xD7 h, where f1 is frequency of modal class, f0 and f\xB2 are frequencies of preceding and succeeding classes.\n\nMean of Grouped Data\n\nDirect method formula: Mean = \u03A3fixi \xF7 \u03A3fi, where xi represents the class mark (midpoint) of each class interval.\n\nEmpirical Relationship\n\nThe empirical relationship between Mean, Median, and Mode is given by: Mode = 3 \xD7 Median - 2 \xD7 Mean.",
        topic: "Statistics",
