        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal Distance = Length of Train + Length of Tunnel = 735 + 225 = 960 m\nSpeed = Distance \xF7 Time = 960 \xF7 48 = 20 m/s\nConvert speed from m/s to km/h by multiplying by (18 \xF7 5): Speed = 20 \xD7 (18 \xF7 5) = 72 km/h\n\u2234 The correct answer is 72 km/h.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nLength of the train = 735 m\nLength of the tunnel = 225 m\nTime taken to pass the tunnel = 48 sec\n\nFormula Used:\nSpeed = Total Distance \xF7 Time\nTotal Distance = Length of Train + Length of Object Passed\nSpeed in km/h = Speed in m/s \xD7 (18 \xF7 5)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total Distance = 735 + 225 = 960 m\n\u21D2 Speed in m/s = 960 \xF7 48 = 20 m/s\n\u21D2 To convert speed from m/s to km/h, multiply by (18 \xF7 5)\n\u21D2 Speed in km/h = 20 \xD7 (18 \xF7 5)\n\u21D2 Speed = 4 \xD7 18 = 72 km/h\n\u2234 The correct answer is 72 km/h.\n\nAdditional Information\nCrossing a Point Object\n\nWhen a train crosses a stationary point object like a man, a pole, or a tree, the distance covered is equal to the length of the train alone.\n\nCrossing an Extended Object\n\nWhen a train crosses an extended stationary object like a platform, bridge, or tunnel, the total distance covered is the sum of the train's length and the object's length.\n\nRelative Speed\n\nFor two moving bodies, Relative Speed = V1 - V\xB2 when traveling in the same direction, and Relative Speed = V1 + V\xB2 when traveling in opposite directions.\n\nUnit Conversions\n\nTo convert speed from km/h to m/s, multiply the value by (5 \xF7 18). To convert speed from m/s to km/h, multiply the value by (18 \xF7 5).",
