        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTSA is 50% more than CSA \u21D2 TSA = 1.5 \xD7 CSA\n\u21D2 2\u03C0r(r + h) = 1.5 \xD7 2\u03C0rh \u21D2 r + h = 1.5h \u21D2 h = 2r\nVolume = \u03C0r2h = \u03C0r2(2r) = 2\u03C0r\xB3\n\u21D2 2\u03C0r\xB3 = 5488\u03C0 \u21D2 r\xB3 = 2744 \u21D2 r = 14 m\nCSA = 2\u03C0rh = 2\u03C0r(2r) = 4\u03C0r\xB2 = 4\u03C0(14)\xB2 = 784\u03C0 m\xB2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 784\u03C0 m\xB2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal Surface Area (TSA) = Curved Surface Area (CSA) + 50% of CSA = 1.5 \xD7 CSA\nVolume (V) = 5488\u03C0 m\xB3\n\nFormula Used:\nTSA = 2\u03C0r(r + h), CSA = 2\u03C0rh, Volume = \u03C0r2h\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 2\u03C0r(r + h) = 1.5 \xD7 2\u03C0rh\n\u21D2 r + h = 1.5h\n\u21D2 r = 0.5h \u21D2 h = 2Rs. ubstitute h = 2r into the volume formula:\n\u21D2 \u03C0r2(2r) = 5488\u03C0\n\u21D2 2\u03C0r\xB3 = 5488\u03C0\n\u21D2 r\xB3 = 2744\n\u21D2 r = 14 m\nNow find height (h) and CSA:\n\u21D2 h = 2 \xD7 14 = 28 m\n\u21D2 CSA = 2\u03C0rh = 2 \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 14 \xD7 28\n\u21D2 CSA = 784\u03C0 m\xB2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 784\u03C0 m\xB2.\n\nAdditional Information\nRight Circular Cylinder Geometry\n\nTotal Surface Area (TSA) is the sum of the Curved Surface Area (CSA) and the two circular bases: TSA = 2\u03C0r\xB2 + 2\u03C0rh.\n\nRatio of Areas\n\nThe relationship between TSA and CSA directly gives the ratio of radius to height since TSA \xF7 CSA = (r + h) \xF7 h = 1 + (r \xF7 h).\n\nVolume of Cylinder\n\nThe volume represents the total 3D space enclosed within the cylinder, given by the product of the base area and the height: V = \u03C0r2h.",
