        userTime: "00:02",
        avgTime: "00:19",
        question: "The speed of a train is 3 times that of a car and 1.5 times of a steamer. A person travelled x km by steamer, 3.75x km by train and x/2 km by car. If the speed of the car is 40 km/h and total time taken by him is $4\\frac{1}{2}$ hours, then the total distance travelled by him in three modes is:",
        options: {
          a: "450 km",
          b: "520 km",
          c: "480 km",
          d: "420 km"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nSpeeds \u2192 Car: 40 km/h | Train: 40 \xD7 3 = 120 km/h | Steamer: 120 \xF7 1.5 = 80 km/h\nTime = Distance \xF7 Speed \u21D2 x/80 + 3.75x/120 + 0.5x/40 = 4.5\n\u21D2 x(1/80 + 1/32 + 1/80) = 4.5\n\u21D2 9x/160 = 4.5 \u21D2 x = 80\nTotal Distance = x + 3.75x + 0.5x = 5.25x = 5.25 \xD7 80 = 420 km.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 420 km.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nSpeed of car = 40 km/h\nTotal time taken = 4.5 hours\n\nFormula Used:\nTime = Distance \xF7 Speed\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Speed of train = 3 \xD7 40 = 120 km/h\n\u21D2 Speed of steamer = 120 \xF7 1.5 = 80 km/h\n\u21D2 Time taken by steamer = x \xF7 80 hours\n\u21D2 Time taken by train = 3.75x \xF7 120 = x \xF7 32 hours\n\u21D2 Time taken by car = (x/2) \xF7 40 = x \xF7 80 hours\n\u21D2 Total time = x/80 + x/32 + x/80 = 4.5\n\u21D2 2x/80 + x/32 = 4.5\n\u21D2 x/40 + x/32 = 4.5\n\u21D2 (4x + 5x) \xF7 160 = 4.5\n\u21D2 9x \xF7 160 = 4.5\n\u21D2 x = (4.5 \xD7 160) \xF7 9 = 80\n\u21D2 Total Distance = x + 3.75x + 0.5x = 5.25x\n\u21D2 Total Distance = 5.25 \xD7 80 = 420 km\n\u2234 The correct answer is 420 km.\n\nAdditional Information\nAverage Speed\n\nWhen an object covers multiple distances at different speeds, Average Speed = Total Distance \xF7 Total Time.\n\nRelative Speed\n\nIf two bodies move in the same direction, relative speed is |S1 - S2|. If they move in opposite directions, relative speed is S1 + S\xB2.\n\nUnit Conversion\n\nTo convert a speed from km/h to m/s, multiply the value by 5/18. To convert m/s back to km/h, multiply the value by 18/5.",
