        userTime: "00:40",
        avgTime: "00:39",
        question: "Let sin A + cos B = 0 and sin B + cos A = 2. What is the value of sin (A + B)?",
        options: {
          a: "1",
          b: "2",
          c: "-1",
          d: "0"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nGiven sin B + cos A = 2. Since the maximum value of both sine and cosine is 1, this equation is only possible if sin B = 1 and cos A = 1.\n\u21D2 B = 90\xB0 and A = 0\xB0\nCheck with the first given equation: sin A + cos B = sin 0\xB0 + cos 90\xB0 = 0 + 0 = 0 (Condition satisfied)\n\u21D2 sin(A + B) = sin(0\xB0 + 90\xB0) = sin 90\xB0 = 1\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nsin A + cos B = 0 . . . (1)\nsin B + cos A = 2 . . . (2)\n\nFormula Used:\nsin\xB2\u03B8 + cos\xB2\u03B8 = 1\nsin(A + B) = sin A cos B + cos A sin B\n\nCalculations:\nSquaring and adding equations (1) and (2):\n\n\u21D2 (sin A + cos B)\xB2 + (sin B + cos A)\xB2 = 0\xB2 + 2\xB2\n\u21D2 (sin\xB2A + cos\xB2B + 2 sin A cos B) + (sin\xB2B + cos\xB2A + 2 sin B cos A) = 4\n\nRearranging the terms:\n\n\u21D2 (sin\xB2A + cos\xB2A) + (sin\xB2B + cos\xB2B) + 2(sin A cos B + cos A sin B) = 4\n\u21D2 1 + 1 + 2 sin(A + B) = 4\n\u21D2 2 + 2 sin(A + B) = 4\n\u21D2 2 sin(A + B) = 2\n\u21D2 sin(A + B) = 1\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1.\n\nAdditional Information\nTrigonometric Identities\n\nsin\xB2\u03B8 + cos\xB2\u03B8 = 1 | sec\xB2\u03B8 - tan\xB2\u03B8 = 1 | cosec\xB2\u03B8 - cot\xB2\u03B8 = 1\n\nCompound Angle Formulas\n\nsin(A - B) = sin A cos B - cos A sin B\ncos(A + B) = cos A cos B - sin A sin B\ncos(A - B) = cos A cos B + sin A sin B",
