        correctOption: "B",
        userTime: "00:05",
        avgTime: "00:56",
        question: "X and Y can complete a certain work in 18 days and 30 days respectively. Z is 50% more efficient than Y. Z and Y started the work but both had to leave after 4 days. The remaining work was completed by X with the assistance of P in the next 4 days. P alone can complete the original work in",
        options: {
          a: "8 days",
          b: "9 days",
          c: "12 days",
          d: "10 days"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal work = LCM(18, 30) = 90 units.\nEfficiency of X = 5, Efficiency of Y = 3.\nZ is 50% more efficient than Y \u21D2 Z's efficiency = 3 + 1.5 = 4.5.\nWork by (Y + Z) in 4 days = 4 \xD7 (3 + 4.5) = 30 units.\nRemaining work (90 - 30 = 60 units) is done by (X + P) in 4 days \u21D2 Efficiency of P = (60 \xF7 4) - 5 = 10.\nTime taken by P alone = 90 \xF7 10 = 9 days.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 9 days.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTime taken by X = 18 days\nTime taken by Y = 30 days\n\nZ is 50% more efficient than Y.\n\nPerson Days Total Work Efficiency\n\nX 18 90 5\n\nY 30 3\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Efficiency of Z = Efficiency of Y + (50% of Efficiency of Y)\n\u21D2 Efficiency of Z = 3 + (0.5 \xD7 3) = 4.5 units/day\n\u21D2 Y and Z started the work and left after 4 days.\n\u21D2 Work completed by Y and Z = 4 \xD7 (Efficiency of Y + Efficiency of Z)\n\u21D2 Work completed by Y and Z = 4 \xD7 (3 + 4.5) = 4 \xD7 7.5 = 30 units\n\u21D2 Remaining work = Total Work - Work completed\n\u21D2 Remaining work = 90 - 30 = 60 units\n\u21D2 This remaining work is completed by X and P in 4 days.\n\u21D2 Combined efficiency of X and P = Remaining work \xF7 Time\n\u21D2 Combined efficiency of X and P = 60 \xF7 4 = 15 units/day\n\u21D2 Efficiency of P = Combined efficiency - Efficiency of X\n\u21D2 Efficiency of P = 15 - 5 = 10 units/day\n\u21D2 Time taken by P alone to complete the original work = Total Work \xF7 Efficiency of P\n\u21D2 Time taken by P = 90 \xF7 10 = 9 days\n\u2234 The correct answer is 9 days.\n\nAdditional Information\nEfficiency and Time\n\nThe time taken by a person to complete a piece of work is inversely proportional to their efficiency. Higher efficiency results in lesser time taken.\n\nTotal Work Concept\n\nTotal Work can be assumed as the Least Common Multiple (LCM) of the given individual times to simplify efficiency calculations. Total Work = Efficiency \xD7 Time.\n\nWork and Wages\n\nWages are distributed in direct proportion to the amount of total work completed by each individual, or their efficiency if they work for the same number of days.\n\nPipes & Cisterns\n\nFunctions identically to Time & Work problems, with the exception that outlet pipes or leaks are treated as negative efficiency.",
