        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nGiven:\n$(81^x \\div 27^3) \\times 3^2 = 3$\n\nFormula Used:\n$a^m \\div a^n = a^{m - n}$\n$a^m \\times a^n = a^{m + n}$\n$(a^m)^n = a^{mn}$\n\nCalculations:\nExpress all terms in base 3:\n$\\Rightarrow 81 = 3^4 \\Rightarrow 81^x = (3^4)^x = 3^{4x}$\n$\\Rightarrow 27 = 3^3 \\Rightarrow 27^3 = (3^3)^3 = 3^9$\n\nSubstitute into the equation:\n$\\Rightarrow (3^{4x} \\div 3^9) \\times 3^2 = 3^1$\n$\\Rightarrow 3^{4x - 9} \\times 3^2 = 3^1$\n$\\Rightarrow 3^{4x - 9 + 2} = 3^1$\n$\\Rightarrow 3^{4x - 7} = 3^1$\n\nEquating exponents on both sides:\n$\\Rightarrow 4x - 7 = 1$\n$\\Rightarrow 4x = 1 + 7 = 8$\n$\\Rightarrow x = \\frac{8}{4} = 2$\n\n\u2234 The value of $x$ is 2.",
