        testName: "Quantitative Aptitude Sectional Test - 9",
        platform: "Testbook",
        status: "Unattempted",
        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "C",
        userTime: "00:50",
        avgTime: "00:51",
        question: "The average weight of 17 men is 63 kg and the average weight of 36 women is 54 kg. What is the average weight (in kg) of all the men and women together? (Rounded off to the nearest integer)",
        options: {
          a: "59",
          b: "62",
          c: "57",
          d: "52"
        },
        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nUsing the assumed mean (deviation) method to simplify the calculation.\n\nAssume the base average = 54 kg.\nDeviation for 17 men = 17 \xD7 (63 - 54) = 17 \xD7 9 = +153 kg.\nAverage deviation per person = +153 \xF7 (17 + 36) = 153 \xF7 53 \u2248 +2.88 kg.\nCombined average = Base average + Average deviation = 54 + 2.88 = 56.88 kg.\n\nRounding off to the nearest integer gives 57.\n\n\u2234 The correct answer is 57 kg.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nNumber of men (n1) = 17, Average weight (A1) = 63 kg\nNumber of women (n\xB2) = 36, Average weight (A\xB2) = 54 kg\n\nWeighted Average Visualized as a Balance Scale\n\n36 W\n\n54 kg\n\n17 M\n\n63 kg\n\nAvg \u2248 57 kg\nRatio: 17 parts\nRatio: 36 parts\n\nFormula Used:\nWeighted Average = (n1 \xD7 A1 + n\xB2 \xD7 A\xB2) \xF7 (n1 + n\xB2)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total weight of men = 17 \xD7 63 = 1071 kg\n\u21D2 Total weight of women = 36 \xD7 54 = 1944 kg\n\u21D2 Total combined weight = 1071 + 1944 = 3015 kg\n\u21D2 Total number of people = 17 + 36 = 53\n\u21D2 Combined average weight = 3015 \xF7 53\n\u21D2 Combined average weight = 56.886... kg\n\u21D2 Rounding off to the nearest integer, we get 57 kg.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 57 kg.\n\nAdditional Information\nWeighted Average\n\nWhen two or more groups with different quantities are combined, their average is given by Aw = (n1A1 + n2A\xB2) \xF7 (n1 + n\xB2).\n\nDeviation Method\n\nInstead of calculating huge products, assume one value as base average. The true average is Base + (\u2211 Net Deviations \xF7 Total Quantity).\n\nAlligation Rule\n\nAlligation is the reverse visual concept of weighted average. It helps find the ratio in which two groups must be mixed to get a desired average: Ratio = (A\xB2 - Aw) : (Aw - A1).",
