        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nRelative speed in the same direction = 8 - 3 = 5 rounds per hour.\n\nThis means Priya gains 5 complete rounds over Seema in 60 minutes.\n\nThey will cross each other when Priya gains exactly 1 complete round.\n\nTime to gain 1 round = 60 \xF7 5 = 12 minutes.\nCrossing time = 11:54 p.m. + 12 minutes = 12:06 a.m.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 12:06 a.m.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\n\u21D2 Speed of Seema = 3 rounds/hr\n\u21D2 Speed of Priya = 8 rounds/hr\n\u21D2 Starting time = 11:54 p.m.\n\nFormula Used:\n\u21D2 Relative Speed (same direction) = Speed1 - Speed\xB2\n\u21D2 Time to cross for the first time = 1 round distance \xF7 Relative Speed\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Since they are moving in the same direction, relative speed = 8 - 3 = 5 rounds/hr\n\u21D2 They cross each other when the faster person (Priya) covers exactly 1 more round than the slower person (Seema).\n\u21D2 Time taken to gain 1 round = 1 \xF7 5 hours\n\u21D2 Time taken in minutes = (1/5) \xD7 60 = 12 minutes\n\u21D2 Crossing time = 11:54 p.m. + 12 minutes\n\u21D2 11:54 p.m. + 6 minutes = 12:00 a.m. (Midnight)\n\u21D2 12:00 a.m. + 6 minutes = 12:06 a.m.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 12:06 a.m.\n\nAdditional Information\nCircular Motion (Same Direction)\n\nWhen two bodies move in the same direction on a circular track, the time taken to meet for the first time anywhere on the track is calculated as Track Length \xF7 (Speed1 - Speed\xB2).\n\nCircular Motion (Opposite Direction)\n\nWhen two bodies move in opposite directions, their relative speed increases. The time taken to meet for the first time is Track Length \xF7 (Speed1 + Speed\xB2).\n\nMeeting at the Starting Point\n\nThe time taken for both runners to meet exactly at the starting point is the LCM (Least Common Multiple) of the individual times taken by each to complete one full round.\n\nNumber of Distinct Meeting Points\n\nIf the ratio of their speeds is a:b (in simplest form), they will meet at exactly (a - b) distinct points if running in the same direction, and at (a + b) distinct points if running in opposite directions.",
