        correctOption: "D",
        userTime: "00:26",
        avgTime: "00:20",
        question: "If the total surface area of a hemisphere is 1848 m2, then the diameter (in m) of the hemisphere is: (Use \\(\\pi = \\frac{22}{7}\\))",
        options: {
          a: "14",
          b: "7",
          c: "21",
          d: "28"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal surface area = 3\u03C0r\xB2 = 1848\n\u21D2 3 \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 r\xB2 = 1848\n\u21D2 r\xB2 = 1848 \xD7 (7/66) = 196\n\u21D2 r = \u221A196 = 14 m\n\u21D2 Diameter (d) = 2r = 2 \xD7 14 = 28 m\n\u2234 The correct answer is 28 m.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTotal surface area of the hemisphere = 1848 m\xB2\n\nFormula Used:\nTotal Surface Area (TSA) = 3\u03C0r\xB2\nDiameter = 2r\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 3 \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 r\xB2 = 1848\n\u21D2 (66/7) \xD7 r\xB2 = 1848\n\u21D2 r\xB2 = 1848 \xD7 (7/66)\n\u21D2 r\xB2 = 28 \xD7 7\n\u21D2 r\xB2 = 196\n\u21D2 r = \u221A196 = 14 m\n\u21D2 Diameter = 2 \xD7 14 = 28 m\n\u2234 The correct answer is 28 m.\n\nAdditional Information\nCurved Surface Area of Hemisphere\n\nThe curved surface area (CSA) includes only the upper dome portion and does not include the circular base. Formula: CSA = 2\u03C0r\xB2\n\nVolume of Hemisphere\n\nThe volume represents the total 3 - dimensional space contained within the hemisphere. Formula: V = (2/3)\u03C0r\xB3\n\nProperties of a Full Sphere\n\nFor a complete sphere of radius r, the Total Surface Area = 4\u03C0r\xB2 and its Volume = (4/3)\u03C0r\xB3",
        topic: "Mensuration 3D",
