        question: "When f(x) = 15x^3 - 14x^2 - 4x + 10 is divided by (3x + 2), then the remainder is:",
        options: {
          a: "-1",
          b: "1",
          c: "-2",
          d: "2"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nBy the Remainder Theorem, if a polynomial f(x) is divided by (ax + b), the remainder is f(-b/a).\n\nHere, dividing by (3x + 2) means we substitute x = -2/3 into f(x).\nf(-2/3) = 15(-8/27) - 14(4/9) - 4(-2/3) + 10\nf(-2/3) = -40/9 - 56/9 + 24/9 + 90/9 = 18/9 = 2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nPolynomial f(x) = 15x\xB3 - 14x\xB2 - 4x + 10\nDivisor = 3x + 2\n\nFormula Used:\nRemainder Theorem: If f(x) is divided by ax + b, the remainder is f(-b/a).\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Let 3x + 2 = 0\n\u21D2 3x = -2\n\u21D2 x = -2/3\n\u21D2 Substitute x = -2/3 in f(x) to find the remainder:\n\u21D2 Remainder = 15(-2/3)\xB3 - 14(-2/3)\xB2 - 4(-2/3) + 10\n\u21D2 Remainder = 15(-8/27) - 14(4/9) + 8/3 + 10\n\u21D2 Remainder = -40/9 - 56/9 + 24/9 + 90/9\n\u21D2 Remainder = (-40 - 56 + 24 + 90) / 9\n\u21D2 Remainder = 18 / 9\n\u21D2 Remainder = 2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 2.\n\nAdditional Information\nRemainder Theorem\n\nWhen a polynomial p(x) is divided by a linear polynomial (x - a), the remainder is equal to p(a).\n\nFactor Theorem\n\nA polynomial p(x) has a factor (x - a) if and only if p(a) = 0. This is a special case of the remainder theorem.\n\nPolynomial Division\n\nDividend = Divisor \xD7 Quotient + Remainder, where the degree of the Remainder is strictly less than the degree of the Divisor.",
