        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nArea of trapezium = 1\u20442 \xD7 Sum of parallel sides \xD7 height = 1\u20442 \xD7 75 \xD7 68 = 2550 cm\xB2.\nGiven, Area of trapezium = 6/17 \xD7 Area of square.\n\nWe know, Area of square can be written as 1\u20442 \xD7 (Diagonal)\xB2.\n\n\u21D2 2550 = 6/17 \xD7 (1\u20442 \xD7 d\xB2) = 3/17 \xD7 d\xB2\n\u21D2 d\xB2 = (2550 \xD7 17) \xF7 3 = 850 \xD7 17 = 14450\n\u21D2 d = \u221A14450 = 85\u221A2 = 85 \xD7 1.41 = 119.85 cm.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 119.85 cm.\n\nAlternate Method\n68 cm\n\na + b = 75 cm\n\nTrapezium\n\nd = ?\nArea = d\xB2 \xF7 2\n\nSquare\n\nGiven:\nHeight of the trapezium (h) = 68 cm\nSum of parallel sides (a + b) = 75 cm\nValue of \u221A2 = 1.41\n\nFormula Used:\nArea of trapezium = 1\u20442 \xD7 (Sum of parallel sides) \xD7 Height\nArea of square = (Side)\xB2 = 1\u20442 \xD7 (Diagonal)\xB2\n\nCalculation:\n\u21D2 Area of trapezium = 1\u20442 \xD7 75 \xD7 68\n\u21D2 Area of trapezium = 75 \xD7 34 = 2550 cm\xB2\n\nAccording to the given condition:\n\n\u21D2 Area of trapezium = 6/17 \xD7 Area of square\n\u21D2 2550 = 6/17 \xD7 Area of square\n\u21D2 Area of square = (2550 \xD7 17) \xF7 6 = 425 \xD7 17 = 7225 cm\xB2\nLet the diagonal of the square be d.\n\u21D2 1\u20442 \xD7 d\xB2 = 7225\n\u21D2 d\xB2 = 7225 \xD7 2 = 14450\n\u21D2 d = \u221A14450 = \u221A(7225 \xD7 2) = 85\u221A2 cm\n\u21D2 d = 85 \xD7 1.41 = 119.85 cm\n\u2234 The correct answer is 119.85 cm.\n\nAdditional Information\nArea of a Trapezium\n\nThe area is defined by the average of its parallel bases multiplied by its perpendicular height: Area = 1\u20442 \xD7 (a + b) \xD7 h.\n\nArea of a Square\n\nIt can be calculated using its side lengths as Area = a\xB2 or using its diagonal as Area = d\xB2 \xF7 2.\n\nRelationship between Side and Diagonal\n\nIn a square, the diagonal forms the hypotenuse of an isosceles right - angled triangle. By Pythagoras theorem, Diagonal = Side \xD7 \u221A2.",
