        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nCombine Ritu and Smita's percentages to find their total marks in one quick step.\n\nTotal percentage for both = 56% + 92% = 148%.\nCombined marks = 148% of 875 = 1.48 \xD7 875 = 1295.\nAverage score = (Combined marks + Reena's marks) \xF7 3 = (1295 + 634) \xF7 3 = 1929 \xF7 3 = 643.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 643 marks.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nMaximum marks = 875\nRitu's score = 56%\nSmita's score = 92%\nReena's score = 634 marks\n\nFormula Used:\nMarks obtained = (Percentage \xF7 100) \xD7 Maximum marks\nAverage = Total sum of values \xF7 Number of values\n\n490 / Ritu\n\n(56%)\n\n805\n\nSmita\n\n(92%)\n\n634\n\nReena\n\n(Given)\n\nAvg: 643\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Ritu's marks = 56% of 875 = (56 \xF7 100) \xD7 875 = 490\n\u21D2 Smita's marks = 92% of 875 = (92 \xF7 100) \xD7 875 = 805\n\u21D2 Total marks = Ritu's marks + Smita's marks + Reena's marks\n\u21D2 Total marks = 490 + 805 + 634 = 1929\n\u21D2 Average score = 1929 \xF7 3 = 643\n\u2234 The correct answer is 643 marks.\n\nAdditional Information\nPercentage Value Calculation\n\nThe value of a specific percentage of a base quantity is found using the relation: Value = (Percentage \xF7 100) \xD7 Base.\n\nCombining Percentages\n\nWhen calculating multiple percentage amounts over the same identical base value, you can save significant calculation time by adding or subtracting the percentage values directly before taking the product with the base.\n\nArithmetic Mean\n\nThe fundamental average is simply the sum of all elements divided by the total count of elements. Formula: Average = Sum of elements \xF7 Number of elements.",
