        correctOption: "D",
        userTime: "00:00",
        avgTime: "00:09",
        question: "In a factory, three assembly lines, A, B and C are set to manufacture a new car. Assembly line A takes 40 days to produce 240 cars. Assembly line B can do the same job, but A is 50% as efficient as B. Assembly line A is 20% more efficient than C. They all start working simultaneously to produce the order. After 5 days, assembly line A breaks down. How many more days would it take to complete the order with the remaining lines?",
        options: {
          a: "13 9/17",
          b: "8 9/17",
          c: "12 6/17",
          d: "7 6/17"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nA's efficiency = 240 \xF7 40 = 6 cars/day.\nB's efficiency = 6 \xF7 50% = 12 cars/day.\nC's efficiency = 6 \xF7 120% = 5 cars/day.\nWork done by all three lines in 5 days = (6 + 12 + 5) \xD7 5 = 23 \xD7 5 = 115 cars.\nRemaining work = 240 - 115 = 125 cars.\nTime taken by remaining lines B and C = 125 \xF7 (12 + 5) = 125 \xF7 17 = 7 6/17 days.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 7 6/17 days.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\n\u21D2 Total work (Order size) = 240 units.\n\u21D2 Assembly line A completes 240 units in 40 days.\n\u21D2 A's efficiency = 240 \xF7 40 = 6 units/day.\n\u21D2 Assembly line A is 50% as efficient as B, hence B's efficiency = 6 \xF7 0.50 = 12 units/day. Days taken by B = 240 \xF7 12 = 20 days.\n\u21D2 Assembly line A is 20% more efficient than C (A = 120% of C), hence C's efficiency = 6 \xF7 1.20 = 5 units/day. Days taken by C = 240 \xF7 5 = 48 days.\n\nPerson Days Total Work Efficiency\n\nA 40 240 6\n\nB 20 12\n\nC 48 5\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Combined efficiency of A, B and C = 6 + 12 + 5 = 23 units/day.\n\u21D2 Work completed by all three lines in the first 5 days = 23 \xD7 5 = 115 units.\n\u21D2 Remaining work = 240 - 115 = 125 units.\n\u21D2 After A breaks down, the remaining work is done by lines B and C.\n\u21D2 Combined efficiency of B and C = 12 + 5 = 17 units/day.\n\u21D2 Time required for remaining lines to complete the order = 125 \xF7 17 = 7 6/17 days.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 7 6/17 days.\n\nAdditional Information\nEfficiency Concept\n\nEfficiency refers to the rate of doing work. It is inversely proportional to the time taken to complete the total work. Total Work = Efficiency \xD7 Time.\n\nCombined Work Concept\n\nWhen multiple lines work together simultaneously, their combined one - day work is simply the arithmetic sum of their individual one - day works (efficiencies).\n\nRemaining Work Concept\n\nIf an entity leaves or stops working mid - way, determine the work already completed, subtract it from total work, and divide the remaining work strictly by the combined efficiency of those who are currently active.",
