        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal Simple Interest percentage is the product of rate and time.\n\u21D2 Total SI% = 7% \xD7 6 = 42%\n\u21D2 Simple Interest = 42% of \u20B93500\n\u21D2 Simple Interest = (42 \xF7 100) \xD7 3500 = 1470\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B91470.\n\nAlternate Method\n\u20B93500\n\nPrincipal\nRate = 7% p.a.\nTime = 6 years\nSI = \u20B91470\n\nSimple Interest\n\nEffective SI% = 7% \xD7 6 = 42%\n\nGiven:\nPrincipal (P) = \u20B93500\nRate (R) = 7% per annum\nTime (T) = 6 years\n\nFormula Used:\nSimple Interest (SI) = (P \xD7 R \xD7 T) \xF7 100\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 SI = (3500 \xD7 7 \xD7 6) \xF7 100\n\u21D2 SI = 3500 \xD7 42 \xF7 100\n\u21D2 SI = 35 \xD7 42\n\u21D2 SI = 1470\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B91470.\n\nAdditional Information\nTotal Amount in Simple Interest\n\nThe total amount paid or received is the sum of Principal and Simple Interest: Amount = P [1 + (R \xD7 T) \xF7 100].\n\nCompound Interest (CI)\n\nUnlike SI, CI is calculated on the principal and the accumulated interest of previous periods. Formula: CI = P[(1 + R \xF7 100)T - 1].\n\nDifference between CI and SI for 2 years\n\nFor the same principal and rate of interest, the difference between CI and SI for exactly 2 years is directly calculated as: D = P(R \xF7 100)2.",
