        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nSubstitute x = -1 in the equation: (3 - 1) \xD7 (1 + 1/3 + 13/3) + (19/3 + 1/3) = A - B + C + D\n\u21D2 2 \xD7 (17/3) + 20/3 = 54/3 = 18 \u21D2 A - B + C + D = 18\nSubstitute x = 0 in the equation: (-1) \xD7 (13/3) + 19/3 = D \u21D2 D = 2\n\u21D2 Required value = (A - B + C - D) = (A - B + C + D) - 2D = 18 - 4 = 14\n\u2234 The correct answer is 14.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\n(3x\xB2 - 1)(x\xB2 - x/3 + 13/3) + (19/3 - x/3) = Ax4 + Bx\xB3 + Cx\xB2 + D\nMethod Used: Expand the Left Hand Side (LHS) and compare the coefficients of like powers of x with the Right Hand Side (RHS).\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 LHS = 3x2(x\xB2 - x/3 + 13/3) - 1(x\xB2 - x/3 + 13/3) + 19/3 - x/3\n\u21D2 LHS = 3x4 - x\xB3 + 13x\xB2 - x\xB2 + x/3 - 13/3 + 19/3 - x/3\n\u21D2 LHS = 3x4 - x\xB3 + 12x\xB2 + (x/3 - x/3) + (19/3 - 13/3)\n\u21D2 LHS = 3x4 - x\xB3 + 12x\xB2 + 6/3\n\u21D2 LHS = 3x4 - x\xB3 + 12x\xB2 + 2\n\nComparing this with the RHS (Ax4 + Bx\xB3 + Cx\xB2 + D), we get:\n\n\u21D2 A = 3, B = -1, C = 12, D = 2\n\nWe need to find the value of (A - B + C - D):\n\n\u21D2 A - B + C - D = 3 - (-1) + 12 - 2\n\u21D2 3 + 1 + 12 - 2 = 14\n\u2234 The correct answer is 14.\n\nAdditional Information\nPolynomial Identity\n\nIf two polynomials are identically equal for all values of x, then the coefficients of their corresponding terms are exactly equal.\n\nSubstitution Method\n\nBy substituting convenient values like x = 0, x = 1, or x = -1 into an identity, we can directly find the constant term, sum of coefficients, or alternating sum of coefficients without fully expanding the entire expression.",
