        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nArea of the annular road $= \\pi(R^2 - r^2)$\n$\\Rightarrow \\text{Area} = \\frac{22}{7} \\times \\left((\\sqrt{65})^2 - 4^2\\right) = \\frac{22}{7} \\times (65 - 16) = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 49 = 154\\text{ m}^2$\nTime taken $= \\frac{\\text{Total Area}}{\\text{Speed}} = \\frac{154}{4.4} = 35\\text{ hours}$\n\u2234 The correct answer is 35 hours.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nOuter radius of the park $(R) = \\sqrt{65}\\text{ m}$\nInner radius of the park $(r) = 4\\text{ m}$\nSpeed of construction $= 4.4\\text{ m}^2/\\text{hour}$\n\nFormula Used:\nArea of annular ring $= \\pi(R^2 - r^2)$\n\nCalculations:\n$\\Rightarrow \\text{Area} = \\pi(R^2 - r^2)$\n$\\Rightarrow \\text{Area} = \\frac{22}{7} \\times \\left((\\sqrt{65})^2 - 4^2\\right)$\n$\\Rightarrow \\text{Area} = \\frac{22}{7} \\times (65 - 16)$\n$\\Rightarrow \\text{Area} = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 49 = 154\\text{ m}^2$\n$\\Rightarrow \\text{Time taken} = \\frac{\\text{Total Area}}{\\text{Speed}}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\text{Time taken} = \\frac{154}{4.4} = \\frac{1540}{44} = 35\\text{ hours}$\n\u2234 The correct answer is 35 hours.\n\nAdditional Information\nArea of a Circle: The total region enclosed by a circle is $\\pi r^2$.\nArea of an Annulus (Circular Path): For a circular track or path with outer radius $R$ and inner radius $r$, the bounded area is $\\pi(R^2 - r^2)$.\nCircumference of a Circle: The total boundary length of a circle is equal to $2\\pi r$ or $\\pi d$.",
