        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nProfit is 22% more than Loss, so Ratio of Profit to Loss = 122 : 100 = 61 : 50\nTotal difference in Selling Price = SP1 - SP\xB2 = 11544 - 5772 = 5772\nTotal ratio parts = 61 + 50 = 111 parts\nSince 111 parts = 5772 \u21D2 1 part = 52\nLoss = 50 parts = 50 \xD7 52 = 2600 \u21D2 CP = SP\xB2 + Loss = 5772 + 2600 = 8372\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B98372.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nSelling Price with profit (SP1) = \u20B911544\nSelling Price with loss (SP\xB2) = \u20B95772\n\nFormula Used:\nProfit = SP - CP\nLoss = CP - SP\n\nCalculations:\nLet the Cost Price be CP.\n\u21D2 Profit = 11544 - CP\n\u21D2 Loss = CP - 5772\n\nAccording to the question, Profit is 22% more than Loss:\n\n\u21D2 Profit = Loss + 22% of Loss\n\u21D2 11544 - CP = 1.22 \xD7 (CP - 5772)\n\u21D2 11544 - CP = 122\u2044100 \xD7 (CP - 5772)\n\u21D2 11544 - CP = 61\u204450 \xD7 (CP - 5772)\n\u21D2 50 \xD7 (11544 - CP) = 61 \xD7 (CP - 5772)\n\u21D2 577200 - 50 CP = 61 CP - 352092\n\u21D2 61 CP + 50 CP = 577200 + 352092\n\u21D2 111 CP = 929292\n\u21D2 CP = 929292 \xF7 111 = 8372\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B98372.\n\nAdditional Information\nCost Price (CP) & Selling Price (SP)\n\nCost price is the price at which the article is purchased. Selling price is the price at which the article is sold.\n\nProfit & Loss Condition\nWhen SP > CP, there is a profit: Profit = SP - CP. When CP > SP, there is a loss: Loss = CP - SP.\nProfit & Loss Percentage\n\nProfit or loss percentage is always calculated on the base of Cost Price: Profit % = (Profit \xF7 CP) \xD7 100.",
