        userTime: "01:20",
        avgTime: "00:56",
        question: "A and B enter into a partnership with capital in the ratio \\(\\frac{4}{3}: \\frac{5}{6}\\). After 6 months, A reduces his capital by 25% and B increases his capital by 50%. What is the share of B (in lakhs) in the profit of Rs. 63.6 lakhs, at the end of a year?",
        options: {
          a: "32.5",
          b: "30",
          c: "32",
          d: "33.6"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nInitial capital ratio = 4/3 : 5/6 = 8 : 5\nProfit ratio = (8 \xD7 6 + 6 \xD7 6) : (5 \xD7 6 + 7.5 \xD7 6)\nProfit ratio = (48 + 36) : (30 + 45) = 84 : 75 = 28 : 25\nTotal parts = 28 + 25 = 53 parts = 63.6 lakhs \u21D2 1 part = 1.2 lakhs\nB's share = 25 \xD7 1.2 = 30 lakhs\n\u2234 The correct answer is 30 lakhs.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nInitial capital ratio of A and B = 4/3 : 5/6 = 8 : 5\nTotal profit at the end of the year = Rs. 63.6 lakhs\n\nFormula Used:\nProfit Ratio = (Capital of A \xD7 Time of A) : (Capital of B \xD7 Time of B)\n\nCalculation:\n\u21D2 Let the initial capital of A be 8x and B be 5x.\n\u21D2 For the first 6 months, A invests 8x and B invests 5x.\n\u21D2 After 6 months, A reduces his capital by 25%.\n\u21D2 A's new capital = 8x - (25% of 8x) = 8x - 2x = 6x\n\u21D2 After 6 months, B increases his capital by 50%.\n\u21D2 B's new capital = 5x + (50% of 5x) = 5x + 2.5x = 7.5x\n\u21D2 Total profit units for A = (8x \xD7 6) + (6x \xD7 6) = 48x + 36x = 84x\n\u21D2 Total profit units for B = (5x \xD7 6) + (7.5x \xD7 6) = 30x + 45x = 75x\n\u21D2 Profit Ratio of A and B = 84x : 75x = 28 : 25\n\u21D2 Total ratio parts = 28 + 25 = 53 parts\n\u21D2 53 parts = 63.6 lakhs\n\u21D2 1 part = 63.6 \xF7 53 = 1.2 lakhs\n\u21D2 B's share in profit = 25 parts = 25 \xD7 1.2 = 30 lakhs\n\u2234 The correct answer is 30 lakhs.\n\nAdditional Information\nCompound Partnership\n\nWhen partners invest different amounts for different periods of time, the profit is shared in the ratio of the product of capital and time (C1 \xD7 T1 : C\xB2 \xD7 T\xB2).\n\nActive and Sleeping Partners\n\nAn active partner manages the business and usually receives a specific percentage or fixed salary from the profit. The remaining profit is then distributed among all partners based on their capital investments.\n\nMid - way Addition or Withdrawal\n\nIf a partner adds or withdraws money during the year, their effective capital for each time segment is calculated separately and summed up to find the overall investment equivalent for the year.",
        topic: "Partnership",
