        status: "Unattempted",
        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "A",
        userTime: "01:15",
        avgTime: "00:14",
        question: "A scooter is being sold at \u20B965,000 cash or \u20B941,000 cash down payment followed by 5 equal monthly instalments. If the rate of interest charged is 25% per annum simple interest, the monthly instalment rounded to the nearest integer is:",
        options: {
          a: "\u20B95,088",
          b: "\u20B95,146",
          c: "\u20B95,201",
          d: "\u20B95,129"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nBalance Principal = 65000 - 41000 = \u20B924, 000\nDue amount after 5 months = 24000 + (24000 \xD7 25 \xD7 5) \xF7 1200 = \u20B926, 500\nSum of 5 instalments (\u20B9x) = 5x + [x \xD7 25 \xD7 (4 + 3 + 2 + 1)] \xF7 1200 = 125x/24\nEquating both values: 125x/24 = 26500 \u21D2 x = 5088\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B95, 088.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nCash price of the scooter = \u20B965, 000\nDown payment = \u20B941, 000\nRate of simple interest (R) = 25% p.a.\nNumber of monthly instalments (n) = 5\n\nInstalment Calculation Timeline\n\nMonth 0\n\n\u20B924000\n\nMonth 1\n\n\u20B9x\n\nMonth 2\n\n\u20B9x\n\nMonth 3\n\n\u20B9x\n\nMonth 4\n\n\u20B9x\n\nMonth 5\n\n\u20B9x\n\nDue = \u20B926, 500\nx = \u20B95, 088\n\nFormula Used:\nTotal Due Amount = Principal + Simple Interest\nSimple Interest = (P \xD7 R \xD7 T) \xF7 100\nSum of Instalments = x \xD7 n + Interest on instalments for the remaining months\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Balance Principal (P) = \u20B965, 000 - \u20B941, 000 = \u20B924, 000\n\u21D2 Time for the Due Amount = 5 months = 5/12 years\n\u21D2 Due Amount after 5 months = 24000 + (24000 \xD7 25 \xD7 5) \xF7 (100 \xD7 12)\n\u21D2 Due Amount = 24000 + 2500 = \u20B926, 500\n\u21D2 Let each monthly instalment be \u20B9x.\n\u21D2 Sum of 5 instalments along with interest accrued till the 5th month:\n\u21D2 First instalment earns interest for 4 months, second for 3 months, and so on.\n\u21D2 Total Amount = 5x + [x \xD7 25 \xD7 (4 + 3 + 2 + 1 + 0)] \xF7 (100 \xD7 12)\n\u21D2 Total Amount = 5x + [x \xD7 25 \xD7 10] \xF7 1200\n\u21D2 Total Amount = 5x + 250x \xF7 1200 = 5x + 5x/24 = 125x/24\n\u21D2 Equating Both Values: 125x/24 = 26500\n\u21D2 x = (26500 \xD7 24) \xF7 125\n\u21D2 x = 212 \xD7 24 = \u20B95, 088\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B95, 088.\n\nAdditional Information\nInstalments in Simple Interest\n\nWhen a debt D is to be paid in n equal annual instalments x at r% p.a., the formula is: D = n \xD7 x + [x \xD7 r \xD7 n(n - 1)] \xF7 200.\n\nPresent Worth and True Discount\n\nTrue Discount (TD) is the simple interest on the Present Worth (PW) of a debt due after a certain time. Due Amount = PW + TD. Also, PW = (Amount \xD7 100) \xF7 (100 + R \xD7 T).\n\nCompound Interest Instalments\n\nFor Compound Interest, if a Principal P is repaid in n equal annual instalments x at rate R%, P = x \xF7 (1 + R/100) + x \xF7 (1 + R/100)\xB2 + ... + x \xF7 (1 + R/100)n.",
