        correctOption: "A",
        userTime: "00:00",
        avgTime: "00:35",
        question: "A person bought a rectangular piece of land whose length and breadth are in the ratio 7 : 5. If the cost of fencing the land is \u20B92,880 at the rate of \u20B915/m, then what is the length of the land?",
        options: {
          a: "56 m",
          b: "40 m",
          c: "60 m",
          d: "84 m"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal perimeter = Total cost \xF7 Rate = 2880 \xF7 15 = 192 m\nRatio of Length to Breadth = 7 : 5 \u21D2 Perimeter in ratio parts = 2 \xD7 (7 + 5) = 24 parts\n24 parts = 192 m \u21D2 1 part = 8 m\nLength = 7 parts = 7 \xD7 8 = 56 m\n\u2234 The correct answer is 56 m.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nLength and Breadth ratio = 7 : 5\nTotal cost of fencing = \u20B92880\nRate of fencing = \u20B915/m\n\nFormula Used:\nPerimeter of Rectangle = 2 \xD7 (Length + Breadth)\nPerimeter = Total Cost \xF7 Rate\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Perimeter = 2880 \xF7 15 = 192 m\n\u21D2 Let the length be 7x and the breadth be 5x.\n\u21D2 2 \xD7 (7x + 5x) = 192\n\u21D2 2 \xD7 12x = 192\n\u21D2 24x = 192\n\u21D2 x = 192 \xF7 24\n\u21D2 x = 8\n\u21D2 Length = 7x = 7 \xD7 8 = 56 m\n\u2234 The correct answer is 56 m.\n\nAdditional Information\nPerimeter vs Area\n\nFencing is always done along the boundary, so it requires calculating the perimeter. Flooring or painting a surface requires calculating the area.\n\nArea of a Rectangle\n\nArea = Length \xD7 Breadth. The total cost of flooring is determined by multiplying the total area by the rate per square unit.\n\nDiagonal of a Rectangle\n\nThe length of the longest pole that can be placed inside a rectangular area is its diagonal. Formula: Diagonal = \u221A(L\xB2 + B\xB2).",
