        status: "Unattempted",
        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "B",
        userTime: "00:00",
        avgTime: "00:17",
        question: "A thief is spotted by a policeman from a distance of 249 m. When the policeman starts the chase, the thief also starts running. Assuming the speed of the thief is 4 m/s and that of the policeman is 7 m/s, how far the thief would have run before he is overtaken by the policeman?",
        options: {
          a: "521 m",
          b: "332 m",
          c: "747 m",
          d: "249 m"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nSince the time taken by both to reach the catch point is the same, distance is directly proportional to their speed.\n\nRatio of distances = Ratio of speeds = Policeman : Thief = 7 : 4\nDifference in distance ratio = 7 - 4 = 3 parts\nHere, 3 parts = 249 m \u21D2 1 part = 83 m\nDistance run by the thief = 4 parts = 4 \xD7 83 = 332 m\n\u2234 The correct answer is 332 m.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nInitial distance between policeman and thief = 249 m\nSpeed of policeman = 7 m/s\nSpeed of thief = 4 m/s\n\nFormula Used:\nDistance = Speed \xD7 Time\nRelative Speed (same direction) = S1 - S\xB2\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Relative speed = 7 - 4 = 3 m/s\n\u21D2 Time taken to catch the thief = Distance \xF7 Relative speed\n\u21D2 Time = 249 \xF7 3 = 83 seconds\n\u21D2 Distance run by the thief (d) = Speed of thief \xD7 Time\n\u21D2 Distance = 4 \xD7 83 = 332 m\n\u2234 The correct answer is 332 m.\n\nAdditional Information\nRelative Speed (Same Direction)\n\nWhen two bodies move in the same direction, their relative speed is the difference of their individual speeds: Srel = S1 - S\xB2.\n\nRelative Speed (Opposite Direction)\n\nWhen two bodies move towards each other, their relative speed is the sum of their individual speeds: Srel = S1 + S\xB2.\n\nTime to Catch/Meet\n\nThe time taken for a faster object to catch a slower one is calculated by dividing their initial distance gap by their relative speed.",
        topic: "Time, Speed & Distance",
        subtopic: "Relative Speed - Police and Thief Problems",
