        status: "Unattempted",
        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "D",
        userTime: "00:00",
        avgTime: "00:19",
        question: "If A and B are digits and A3 + 8B = 150, then the value of A - B is",
        options: {
          a: "1",
          b: "2",
          c: "-2",
          d: "-1"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nLook at the units column: 3 + B must give a sum ending in 0.\nSince B is a single digit, 3 + B = 10 \u21D2 B = 7.\n\nThis generates a carry of 1 to the tens column.\n\nLook at the tens column: A + 8 + 1 (carry) = 15 \u21D2 A = 6.\nTherefore, A - B = 6 - 7 = -1.\n\u2234 The correct answer is - 1.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nA\xB3 + 8B = 150, where A and B are single digits.\n\nFormula Used:\nA two - digit number XY can be written as 10X + Y.\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Expand the numbers A\xB3 and 8B using their place values.\n\u21D2 (10 \xD7 A + 3) + (10 \xD7 8 + B) = 150\n\u21D2 10A + 3 + 80 + B = 150\n\u21D2 10A + B + 83 = 150\n\u21D2 10A + B = 150 - 83\n\u21D2 10A + B = 67\nSince A and B are single digits, 10A + B represents the two - digit number AB.\n\u21D2 This implies the two - digit number AB is 67.\n\u21D2 By comparing the digits, A = 6 and B = 7.\n\u21D2 We need to find the value of A - B.\n\u21D2 A - B = 6 - 7 = -1.\n\u2234 The correct answer is - 1.\n\nAdditional Information\nPlace Value Expansion\n\nA general two - digit number XY is mathematically represented as 10X + Y, where X is the tens digit and Y is the units digit. For a three - digit number XYZ, the expansion is 100X + 10Y + Z.\n\nCryptarithm Puzzles\n\nThese are mathematical puzzles where digits are replaced by letters. The key is to analyze the units column first and account for carries to the next higher place value.\n\nDigit Reversal Rule\n\nWhen the digits of a two - digit number XY are reversed to form YX, the difference between the two numbers is always a multiple of 9: (10X + Y) - (10Y + X) = 9(X - Y).",
        topic: "Number System",
        subtopic: "Cryptarithms & Place Value Expansion",
        conceptTested: "Representing two-digit numbers using decimal place value expansion (10A + B) to solve digit puzzles.",
        tags: {
          topic: "Number System",
          subtopic: "Cryptarithms & Place Value Expansion",
          conceptTested: "Representing two-digit numbers using decimal place value expansion (10A + B) to solve digit puzzles.",
          difficulty: "medium"
        }
