        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "B",
        userTime: "00:11",
        avgTime: "00:27",
        question: "A cylinder of height 28 cm and radius 10 cm is melted and formed into 4 square base pyramids each has the same height H and the base length of each pyramid is equal. Find the height of the pyramid, if the length of its base is 20 cm.",
        options: {
          a: "8.25 cm",
          b: "16.5 cm",
          c: "33 cm",
          d: "5.5 cm"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nVolume of Cylinder = 4 \xD7 Volume of Square Pyramid\n\u21D2 \u03C0r2h = 4 \xD7 (1/3 \xD7 a\xB2 \xD7 H)\n\u21D2 22/7 \xD7 100 \xD7 28 = 4 \xD7 1/3 \xD7 400 \xD7 H\n\u21D2 8800 = (1600/3) \xD7 H \u21D2 H = (8800 \xD7 3) \xF7 1600 = 16.5 cm\n\u2234 The correct answer is 16.5 cm.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nRadius of cylinder (r) = 10 cm, Height of cylinder (h) = 28 cm\nBase side of square pyramid (a) = 20 cm, Number of pyramids = 4\nLet the height of each pyramid be H.\n\nFormula Used:\nVolume of Cylinder = \u03C0r2h\nVolume of a Pyramid = 1/3 \xD7 Base Area \xD7 Height\n\nCalculations:\nWhen a solid is melted and recast to form new objects, the total volume remains constant.\n\n\u21D2 Volume of Cylinder = 4 \xD7 Volume of Square Pyramid\n\u21D2 \u03C0r2h = 4 \xD7 (1/3 \xD7 a\xB2 \xD7 H)\n\u21D2 (22/7) \xD7 102 \xD7 28 = 4 \xD7 (1/3 \xD7 202 \xD7 H)\n\u21D2 (22/7) \xD7 100 \xD7 28 = 4/3 \xD7 400 \xD7 H\n\u21D2 22 \xD7 100 \xD7 4 = (1600/3) \xD7 H\n\u21D2 8800 = (1600/3) \xD7 H\n\u21D2 H = (8800 \xD7 3) \xF7 1600\n\u21D2 H = (88 \xD7 3) \xF7 16\n\u21D2 H = (11 \xD7 3) \xF7 2\n\u21D2 H = 33 \xF7 2 = 16.5 cm\n\u2234 The correct answer is 16.5 cm.\n\nAdditional Information\nMelting and Recasting\n\nWhen a 3D object is melted and recast into another shape, the total volume always remains constant regardless of the change in dimensions.\n\nVolume of a Cone\n\nV = 1/3 \xD7 \u03C0r2h, where r is the base radius and h is the vertical height. A cone is essentially a circular base pyramid.\n\nVolume of a Prism\n\nV = Base Area \xD7 Height. The volume formula of a cylinder is a special case of a prism with a circular base.",
        topic: "Mensuration 3D",
