        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nGiven:\n\\(\\dfrac{3}{5} \\times \\left[ {\\left( {\\dfrac{9}{{14}} + \\dfrac{3}{7}} \\right) \\times \\dfrac{7}{{15}}} \\right] - \\dfrac{3}{5}\\)\n\nFormula used:\nBODMAS Rule\n\nCalculation:\n\\(\\dfrac{3}{5} \\times \\left[ {\\left( {\\dfrac{9}{{14}} + \\dfrac{3}{7}} \\right) \\times \\dfrac{7}{{15}}} \\right] - \\dfrac{3}{5}\\)\n\n\u21D2 \\(\\dfrac{3}{5} \\times \\left[ {\\left( {\\dfrac{9 + 6}{14}} \\right) \\times \\dfrac{7}{{15}}} \\right] - \\dfrac{3}{5}\\)\n\u21D2 \\(\\dfrac{3}{5} \\times \\left[ {\\dfrac{15}{14} \\times \\dfrac{7}{15}} \\right] - \\dfrac{3}{5}\\)\n\u21D2 \\(\\dfrac{3}{5} \\times \\left[ \\dfrac{1}{2} - \\dfrac{3}{5} \\right]\\)\n\u21D2 \\(\\dfrac{3}{5} \\times \\left[ \\dfrac{5 - 6}{10} \\right]\\)\n\u21D2 \\(\\dfrac{3}{5} \\times \\dfrac{-1}{10}\\)\n\u21D2 \\(\\dfrac{-3}{50}\\)\n\u2234 The correct answer is option (2).",
