        userTime: "00:52",
        avgTime: "00:20",
        question: "A man\u2019s basic pay for a 40 hours\u2019 week is Rs. 200. Overtimes is paid at 25% above the basic rate. In a certain week, he worked overtime and his total was Rs. 300. He therefore, worked for a total of (in hours):",
        options: {
          a: "52",
          b: "56",
          c: "58",
          d: "62"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nBasic rate = 200 \xF7 40 = Rs. 5/hr.\nOvertime rate = 5 \xD7 1.25 = Rs. 6.25/hr.\nOvertime amount = 300 - 200 = Rs. 100.\nOvertime hours = 100 \xF7 6.25 = 16 hours.\nTotal hours worked = 40 + 16 = 56 hours.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 56 hours.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nBasic pay for 40 hours = Rs. 200\nTotal pay earned in a certain week = Rs. 300\n\nOvertime rate is 25% above the basic rate.\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Basic rate per hour = 200 \xF7 40 = Rs. 5\n\u21D2 Overtime rate per hour = 5 + (25% of 5) = 5 + 1.25 = Rs. 6.25\n\u21D2 Amount earned through overtime = Total pay - Basic pay = 300 - 200 = Rs. 100\n\u21D2 Overtime hours = Overtime pay \xF7 Overtime rate per hour = 100 \xF7 6.25 = 16 hours\n\u21D2 Total hours worked = Basic hours + Overtime hours = 40 + 16 = 56 hours\n\u2234 The correct answer is 56 hours.\n\nAdditional Information\nTime and Wages\n\nWages are directly proportional to the time spent working if the rate is uniform. Formula: Total Wages = Rate per hour \xD7 Total hours worked.\n\nPercentage Increase\n\nWhen a value is increased by R%, the new value is Base \xD7 (1 + R/100). Here, the overtime rate is 1.25 times the basic rate.\n\nWork and Efficiency\n\nIn cases of varied efficiency or piece - rate work, wages are divided in the ratio of the efficiency or the part of total work completed by each individual.",
