        userTime: "01:02",
        avgTime: "00:51",
        question: "P and Q enter into a partnership with investments of Rs. 1400 and Rs. 1800 respectively. They share half of the profit equally for running the business and the remaining profit in the ratio of their investments. If the difference in their shares of profits is Rs. 47, what is the total profit?",
        options: {
          a: "Rs. 954",
          b: "Rs. 504",
          c: "Rs. 804",
          d: "Rs. 752"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nRatio of investments of P and Q = 1400 : 1800 = 7 : 9.\n\nThe first half of the profit is shared equally, so it creates zero difference in their total shares.\n\nThe difference of Rs. 47 comes entirely from the remaining half of the profit.\n\nDifference in shares = (9 - 7) \xF7 (9 + 7) of Half Profit = 2/16 \xD7 (Total Profit / 2) = Total Profit / 16.\n\u21D2 Total Profit / 16 = 47 \u21D2 Total Profit = 47 \xD7 16 = 752.\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 752.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nInvestment of P = Rs. 1400\nInvestment of Q = Rs. 1800\nDifference in their profit shares = Rs. 47\n\nFormula Used:\nProfit Ratio = Investment of Partner 1 \xD7 Time : Investment of Partner 2 \xD7 Time\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Ratio of investments = 1400 : 1800 = 7 : 9\n\u21D2 Let the total profit be x.\n\u21D2 First half of the profit = x/2 (divided equally)\n\u21D2 P's share from first half = x/4, and Q's share from first half = x/4\n\u21D2 Second half of the profit = x/2 (divided in investment ratio 7 : 9)\n\u21D2 P's share from second half = (7/16) \xD7 (x/2) = 7x/32\n\u21D2 Q's share from second half = (9/16) \xD7 (x/2) = 9x/32\n\u21D2 Difference in their shares = Q's total share - P's total share\n\u21D2 Difference = (x/4 + 9x/32) - (x/4 + 7x/32)\n\u21D2 Difference = 9x/32 - 7x/32 = 2x/32 = x/16\n\u21D2 Given difference = 47\n\u21D2 x/16 = 47\n\u21D2 x = 47 \xD7 16 = 752\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 752.\n\nAdditional Information\nWorking and Sleeping Partners\n\nWhen one partner actively manages the business (working partner), they typically receive a fixed percentage of the total profit as a salary before the remaining profit is divided according to the investments.\n\nCompound Partnership\n\nWhen partners invest money for different durations, the profit is shared based on the product of the capital invested and the time period. Profit Ratio = (C1 \xD7 T1) : (C\xB2 \xD7 T\xB2).\n\nEqually Shared Profit Component\n\nAny portion of the total profit that is shared equally among partners does not affect the difference in their final profit shares. The net difference arises solely from the remaining profit distributed based on their investment ratios.",
