        question: "A cube of side 15 cm is cut into 27 small cubes. Then find the ratio of the lateral surface area of the large cube to the total surface area of one of the small cubes.",
        options: {
          a: "9 : 4",
          b: "4 : 3",
          c: "5 : 2",
          d: "6 : 1"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nNumber of small cubes = (A/a)\xB3 = 27 \u21D2 Ratio of sides (A/a) = 3.\nRatio of areas = (Lateral Surface Area of Large Cube) \xF7 (Total Surface Area of Small Cube)\n\u21D2 (4 \xD7 A\xB2) \xF7 (6 \xD7 a\xB2)\n\u21D2 (4/6) \xD7 (A/a)\xB2 = (2/3) \xD7 32 = 6\n\u2234 The correct answer is 6 : 1.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nSide of the large cube (A) = 15 cm\nNumber of small cubes formed = 27\n\nFormula Used:\nVolume of cube = (side)\xB3\nLateral Surface Area of cube = 4 \xD7 (side)\xB2\nTotal Surface Area of cube = 6 \xD7 (side)\xB2\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Volume of large cube = 27 \xD7 Volume of small cube\n\u21D2 153 = 27 \xD7 a\xB3\n\u21D2 3375 = 27 \xD7 a\xB3\n\u21D2 a\xB3 = 125 \u21D2 a = 5 cm\n\u21D2 Lateral Surface Area of large cube = 4 \xD7 152 = 4 \xD7 225 = 900 cm\xB2\n\u21D2 Total Surface Area of small cube = 6 \xD7 52 = 6 \xD7 25 = 150 cm\xB2\n\u21D2 Required Ratio = 900 / 150 = 6 / 1 = 6 : 1\n\u2234 The correct answer is 6 : 1.\n\nAdditional Information\nTotal Surface Area of a Cube\n\nIt is the sum of the areas of all 6 faces of the cube. Formula: TSA = 6 \xD7 (side)\xB2\n\nLateral Surface Area of a Cube\n\nIt is the sum of the areas of the 4 vertical side faces of the cube, excluding the top and bottom faces. Formula: LSA = 4 \xD7 (side)\xB2\n\nVolume of a Cube\n\nIt represents the total 3D space occupied by the cube. When a shape is cut or reshaped, the total volume remains conserved. Formula: Volume = (side)\xB3",
