        correctOption: "D",
        userTime: "00:01",
        avgTime: "00:18",
        question: "If \\(\\frac{1}{3}A = 3B = \\frac{3}{4}C\\), then what is the value of \\(A \\\u2236 B \\\u2236 C\\)?",
        options: {
          a: "9 \\\u2236 3 \\\u2236 9",
          b: "9 \\\u2236 2 \\\u2236 4",
          c: "9 \\\u2236 4 \\\u2236 4",
          d: "9 \\\u2236 1 \\\u2236 4"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nEquate the given expression to 1: (1/3)A = 3B = (3/4)C = 1\n\u21D2 A = 3, B = 1/3, C = 4/3\n\u21D2 A : B : C = 3 : 1/3 : 4/3\n\nMultiply by 3 to eliminate the denominators:\n\n\u21D2 A : B : C = 9 : 1 : 4\n\u2234 The correct answer is 9 : 1 : 4.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\n\u21D2 (1/3)A = 3B = (3/4)C\n\nFormula Used:\nIf xA = yB = zC = k, then A : B : C = (k/x) : (k/y) : (k/z)\n\nCalculations:\nLet (1/3)A = 3B = (3/4)C = k\n\u21D2 A = 3k\n\u21D2 B = k/3\n\u21D2 C = 4k/3\nNow, substitute the values of A, B, and C into the ratio form A : B : C:\n\u21D2 A : B : C = 3k : k/3 : 4k/3\n\nDivide the entire ratio by k:\n\n\u21D2 A : B : C = 3 : 1/3 : 4/3\n\nMultiply all terms by the least common multiple of the denominators (LCM of 3 is 3):\n\n\u21D2 A : B : C = (3 \xD7 3) : (1/3 \xD7 3) : (4/3 \xD7 3)\n\u21D2 A : B : C = 9 : 1 : 4\n\u2234 The correct answer is 9 : 1 : 4.\n\nAdditional Information\nCompound Ratio\n\nThe compound ratio of two or more ratios is obtained by multiplying their antecedent and consequent terms respectively. For a : b and c : d, it is (a \xD7 c) : (b \xD7 d).\n\nInverse Ratio\n\nThe inverse ratio of a : b is b : a. If aA = bB, then the ratio A : B is equal to b : a.\n\nDuplicate & Triplicate Ratios\n\nThe duplicate ratio of a : b is given as a\xB2 : b\xB2, and the triplicate ratio is a\xB3 : b\xB3.",
