        avgTime: "00:13",
        question: "The ratio of the efficiencies of A, B and C is 4 \\\u2236 5 \\\u2236 3. Working together, they can complete that work in 25 days. A and C together will complete 35% of that work in:",
        options: {
          a: "\\(\\frac{75}{4}\\) days",
          b: "15 days",
          c: "\\(\\frac{65}{4}\\) days",
          d: "\\(\\frac{45}{4}\\) days"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nEfficiency ratio A : B : C = 4 : 5 : 3\nTotal efficiency = 4 + 5 + 3 = 12 units/day\nTotal work = 12 \xD7 25 = 300 units\n35% of work = 300 \xD7 0.35 = 105 units\nEfficiency of (A + C) = 4 + 3 = 7 units/day\nTime taken = 105 \xF7 7 = 15 days\n\u2234 The correct option is B.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven: Efficiency ratio of A, B and C is 4 : 5 : 3. They complete work in 25 days.\nFormula Used: Total Work = (Combined Efficiency) \xD7 Time\n\nPersons Time Work Efficiency\n\nA - 300 / 4\n\nB - 5\n\nC - 3\n\nA + B+C 25 12\n\nCombined efficiency of A + B + C = 4 + 5 + 3 = 12 units/day\nTotal work = 12 \xD7 25 = 300 units\n\u21D2 Target work = 35% of 300\n\u21D2 Target work = (35 \xF7 100) \xD7 300 = 105 units\n\u21D2 Combined efficiency of A and C = 4 + 3 = 7 units/day\n\u21D2 Time taken by A and C = 105 \xF7 7 = 15 days\n\u2234 The correct option is B.\n\nAdditional Information\nRelationship between Efficiency and Time\n\nEfficiency is inversely proportional to the time taken to complete a specific task (Efficiency \u221D 1 \xF7 Time). If efficiency doubles, time taken is halved.\n\nTotal Work Calculation\n\nTotal work can be calculated by multiplying the combined efficiency of the group by the total number of days taken: Work = (\u03A3 Efficiencies) \xD7 Total Days.\n\nWork & Wages\n\nWages are generally distributed in the ratio of the work done by each individual, which is the product of their efficiency and the time for which they worked.",
