        status: "Unattempted",
        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "C",
        userTime: "00:00",
        avgTime: "00:11",
        question: "A sum of \u20B92,50,000 is invested for one and a half years at 12% per annum compound interest. What is the difference between the amounts received when the interest is compounded semi-annually and when it is compounded annually?",
        options: {
          a: "\u20B9900",
          b: "\u20B9970",
          c: "\u20B9954",
          d: "\u20B9950"
        },
        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nEffective CI rate (annually) for 1.5 years at 12% = 12% + 6% + (12 \xD7 6) \xF7 100 = 18.72%\n\nEffective CI rate (semi - annually) for 3 half - years at 6% = 3(6) + 3(6)\xB2 \xF7 100 + (6)\xB3 \xF7 10000 = 18 + 1.08 + 0.0216 = 19.1016%\nDifference in effective rate = 19.1016% - 18.72% = 0.3816%\nDifference in amount = 0.3816% of 2, 50, 000 = (0.3816 \xF7 100) \xD7 250000 = \u20B9954\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B9954.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nPrincipal (P) = \u20B92, 50, 000\nRate (R) = 12% per annum\nTime (T) = 1.5 years\n\nCompounded Annually (1.5 years): \u20B92, 50, 000 + 12% (1st yr)\n\n\u20B92, 80, 000 + 6% (1\u20442 yr)\n\n\u20B92, 96, 800\n\nCompounded Semi - Annually (3 half - years): \u20B92, 50, 000 + 6%\n\n\u20B92, 65, 000 + 6%\n\n\u20B92, 80, 900 + 6%\n\n\u20B92, 97, 754\n\nDifference = \u20B92, 97, 754 - \u20B92, 96, 800 = \u20B9954\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Amount compounded annually (A1) = P \xD7 (1 + R/100)1 \xD7 (1 + (R/2)/100)\n\u21D2 A1 = 250000 \xD7 (1 + 12/100) \xD7 (1 + 6/100)\n\u21D2 A1 = 250000 \xD7 1.12 \xD7 1.06 = 250000 \xD7 1.1872\n\u21D2 A1 = \u20B92, 96, 800\n\u21D2 Amount compounded semi - annually (A\xB2) = P \xD7 (1 + (R/2)/100)2T\n\u21D2 A\xB2 = 250000 \xD7 (1 + 6/100)\xB3\n\u21D2 A\xB2 = 250000 \xD7 (1.06)\xB3 = 250000 \xD7 1.191016\n\u21D2 A\xB2 = \u20B92, 97, 754\n\u21D2 Difference in amounts = A\xB2 - A1\n\u21D2 Difference = 297754 - 296800 = \u20B9954\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B9954.\n\nAdditional Information\nEffective Rate Method\n\nFor 3 equal periods at rate R%, the effective compound interest rate is calculated as: 3R + 3R\xB2/100 + R\xB3/10000.\n\nHalf - Yearly Compounding\n\nWhen interest is compounded semi - annually, the annual rate of interest is divided by 2 (R/2) and the number of years is multiplied by 2 (2T).\n\nFractional Year Compounding\n\nIf time is given in fractions like 1.5 years, the formula used for annual compounding is: A = P(1 + R/100)1 \xD7 (1 + (R/2)/100)1.",
