        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nGiven, 1/3 of Males = 76% of Females\n\u21D2 M / 3 = (76 / 100) \xD7 F\n\u21D2 M / 3 = (19 / 25) \xD7 F\n\u21D2 M / F = (19 \xD7 3) / 25 = 57 / 25\n\u2234 The correct answer is 57 : 25.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\n76% of the number of females is equal to^(1/3) of the number of males.\n\nFormula Used:\nPercentage value = (Rate \xF7 100) \xD7 Base value\n\nCalculations:\nLet the total number of males be M and the total number of females be F.\n\u21D2 76% of F = (1 / 3) \xD7 M\n\u21D2 (76 \xF7 100) \xD7 F = M \xF7 3\n\u21D2 (19 \xF7 25) \xD7 F = M \xF7 3\n\nRearranging the terms to find the ratio of M to F:\n\n\u21D2 M \xF7 F = (19 \xF7 25) \xD7 3\n\u21D2 M \xF7 F = 57 \xF7 25\n\u21D2 M : F = 57 : 25\n\u2234 The correct answer is 57 : 25.\n\nAdditional Information\nRatio & Proportion Basics\n\nA ratio compares two quantities of the same kind. The ratio of a to b is written as a : b or a \xF7 b. The first term is called the antecedent, and the second term is the consequent.\n\nPercentage to Fraction Conversion\n\nTo convert a percentage into a fraction, simply divide the percentage value by 100 and simplify. For example, 76% = 76 \xF7 100 = 19 \xF7 25.\n\nEquivalent Ratios\n\nMultiplying or dividing both terms of a ratio by the same non - zero number does not change the ratio. This property is highly useful to simplify complex fractional equations into simplest form.",
