        userTime: "00:46",
        avgTime: "00:33",
        question: "Find the value of $2 \\operatorname{cosec}^2 23^\\circ \\cot^2 67^\\circ - \\sin^2 23^\\circ - \\sin^2 67^\\circ - \\cot^2 67^\\circ$:",
        options: {
          a: "$\\sec^2 23^\\circ$",
          b: "1",
          c: "$\\tan^2 23^\\circ$",
          d: "0",
          A: "$\\sec^2 23^\\circ$",
          B: "1",
          C: "$\\tan^2 23^\\circ$",
          D: "0"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nConvert 67\xB0 angles to 23\xB0 using cot 67\xB0 = tan 23\xB0 and sin 67\xB0 = cos 23\xB0.\n\u21D2 2 cosec\xB2 23\xB0 tan\xB2 23\xB0 - (sin\xB2 23\xB0 + cos\xB2 23\xB0) - tan\xB2 23\xB0\n\u21D2 2(1 / sin\xB2 23\xB0) \xD7 (sin\xB2 23\xB0 / cos\xB2 23\xB0) - 1 - tan\xB2 23\xB0\n\u21D2 2 sec\xB2 23\xB0 - 1 - tan\xB2 23\xB0 = sec\xB2 23\xB0 + (sec\xB2 23\xB0 - tan\xB2 23\xB0) - 1\n\u21D2 sec\xB2 23\xB0 + 1 - 1 = sec\xB2 23\xB0\n\u2234 The correct answer is sec\xB2 23\xB0.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\n2 cosec\xB2 23\xB0 cot\xB2 67\xB0 - sin\xB2 23\xB0 - sin\xB2 67\xB0 - cot\xB2 67\xB0\n\nFormulas Used: sin(90\xB0 - \u03B8) = cos \u03B8\ncot(90\xB0 - \u03B8) = tan \u03B8\nsin\xB2\u03B8 + cos\xB2\u03B8 = 1\nsec\xB2\u03B8 - tan\xB2\u03B8 = 1\n\nCalculation:\n\u21D2 2 cosec\xB2 23\xB0 cot2(90\xB0 - 23\xB0) - sin\xB2 23\xB0 - sin2(90\xB0 - 23\xB0) - cot2(90\xB0 - 23\xB0)\n\u21D2 2 cosec\xB2 23\xB0 tan\xB2 23\xB0 - sin\xB2 23\xB0 - cos\xB2 23\xB0 - tan\xB2 23\xB0\n\u21D2 2(1 / sin\xB2 23\xB0) \xD7 (sin\xB2 23\xB0 / cos\xB2 23\xB0) - (sin\xB2 23\xB0 + cos\xB2 23\xB0) - tan\xB2 23\xB0\n\u21D2 2(1 / cos\xB2 23\xB0) - 1 - tan\xB2 23\xB0\n\u21D2 2 sec\xB2 23\xB0 - 1 - tan\xB2 23\xB0\n\u21D2 sec\xB2 23\xB0 + (sec\xB2 23\xB0 - tan\xB2 23\xB0) - 1\n\u21D2 sec\xB2 23\xB0 + 1 - 1\n\u21D2 sec\xB2 23\xB0\n\u2234 The correct answer is sec\xB2 23\xB0.\n\nAdditional Information\nTrigonometric Identities\n\nThe fundamental Pythagorean identities are sin\xB2\u03B8 + cos\xB2\u03B8 = 1, sec\xB2\u03B8 - tan\xB2\u03B8 = 1, and cosec\xB2\u03B8 - cot\xB2\u03B8 = 1.\n\nComplementary Angles\n\nTwo angles are complementary if their sum is 90\xB0. Key relations: sin(90\xB0 - \u03B8) = cos \u03B8, tan(90\xB0 - \u03B8) = cot \u03B8, and sec(90\xB0 - \u03B8) = cosec \u03B8.\n\nReciprocal Relations\n\nTrigonometric ratios are related by reciprocal identities: cosec \u03B8 = 1 / sin \u03B8, sec \u03B8 = 1 / cos \u03B8, and cot \u03B8 = 1 / tan \u03B8.",
