        platform: "Testbook",
        status: "Unattempted",
        chosenOption: "Unattempted",
        correctOption: "D",
        userTime: "00:06",
        avgTime: "00:34",
        question: "The system of equations: 2x + 3y = 7 and (a - b)x + (a + b)y = 3a + b - 2 have infinitely many solutions:",
        options: {
          a: "a = 5, b = 3",
          b: "a = 2, b = 3",
          c: "a = 2, b = 1",
          d: "a = 5, b = 1"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nFor infinitely many solutions, the ratio of coefficients must be equal: a1/a\xB2 = b1/b\xB2.\n\n\u21D2 2 / (a - b) = 3 / (a + b)\n\u21D2 2a + 2b = 3a - 3b \u21D2 a = 5b\nCheck options: Only Option 4 has a = 5 and b = 1, which perfectly satisfies a = 5b.\n\u2234 The correct answer is a = 5, b = 1.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\n2x + 3y = 7\n(a - b)x + (a + b)y = 3a + b - 2\n\nFormula Used:\nFor a system of equations to have infinitely many solutions, the ratio of their coefficients must be equal: a1 / a\xB2 = b1 / b\xB2 = c1 / c\xB2\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Here, a1 = 2, b1 = 3, c1 = 7\n\u21D2 a\xB2 = (a - b), b\xB2 = (a + b), c\xB2 = (3a + b - 2)\n\u21D2 2 / (a - b) = 3 / (a + b) = 7 / (3a + b - 2)\n\u21D2 Equating the first two parts:\n\u21D2 2 / (a - b) = 3 / (a + b)\n\u21D2 2(a + b) = 3(a - b)\n\u21D2 2a + 2b = 3a - 3b\n\u21D2 a = 5b --- (Equation 1)\n\u21D2 Equating the second and third parts:\n\u21D2 3 / (a + b) = 7 / (3a + b - 2)\n\u21D2 3(3a + b - 2) = 7(a + b)\n\u21D2 9a + 3b - 6 = 7a + 7b\n\u21D2 2a - 4b = 6\n\u21D2 a - 2b = 3 --- (Equation 2)\n\u21D2 Substituting a = 5b into Equation 2:\n\u21D2 5b - 2b = 3\n\u21D2 3b = 3 \u21D2 b = 1\n\u21D2 Substitute b = 1 back into Equation 1:\n\u21D2 a = 5 \xD7 1 = 5\n\u2234 The correct answer is a = 5, b = 1.\n\nAdditional Information\nUnique Solution\n\nA system of linear equations has a unique solution if the lines intersect at exactly one point. The condition is a1 / a\xB2 = \u0338 b1 / b\xB2.\n\nNo Solution\n\nA system of equations has no solution if the lines are parallel and never intersect. The condition is a1 / a\xB2 = b1 / b\xB2 = \u0338 c1 / c\xB2.\n\nInfinitely Many Solutions\n\nA system of equations has infinitely many solutions if the lines overlap entirely, meaning they represent the exact same line. The condition is a1 / a\xB2 = b1 / b\xB2 = c1 / c\xB2.",
