        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nUsing the proportional ratio: (Amount \xF7 Quantity) \xF7 (100 + Profit%) = Constant\n\u21D2 (18 \xF7 10) \xF7 124 = (1530 \xF7 N) \xF7 155\n\u21D2 1.8 \xF7 124 = 1530 \xF7 (155 \xD7 N)\n\u21D2 N = (1530 \xD7 124) \xF7 (1.8 \xD7 155)\n\u21D2 N = 680\n\u2234 The correct answer is 680 pens.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nSelling Price (SP1) of 10 pens = \u20B918\nInitial Profit = 24%\nTarget Profit = 55%\nTarget Amount = \u20B91530\n\nFormula Used:\nCP = SP \xD7 [100 \xF7 (100 + Profit%)]\nNew SP = CP \xD7 [(100 + New Profit%) \xF7 100]\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 SP1 of 1 pen = 18 \xF7 10 = \u20B91.80\n\u21D2 CP of 1 pen = 1.80 \xD7 (100 \xF7 124) = \u20B945/31\n\u21D2 Target SP\xB2 of 1 pen for 55% profit = CP \xD7 (155 \xF7 100)\n\u21D2 Target SP\xB2 = (45 \xF7 31) \xD7 (155 \xF7 100)\n\u21D2 Target SP\xB2 = 45 \xD7 (5 \xF7 100) = \u20B92.25\n\u21D2 Number of pens = Total Amount \xF7 Target SP\xB2\n\u21D2 Number of pens = 1530 \xF7 2.25\n\u21D2 Number of pens = 680\n\u2234 The correct answer is 680 pens.\n\nAdditional Information\nMarked Price and Discount\n\nDiscount is always calculated on the Marked Price (MP). Formula: SP = MP \xD7 [1 - (Discount% \xF7 100)].\n\nSuccessive Discounts\n\nIf two successive discounts of a% and b% are given, the effective single discount is (a + b - ab \xF7 100)%.\n\nDishonest Dealer\n\nWhen a dealer sells goods at cost price but uses a false weight, the actual Profit% = [Error \xF7 (True Value - Error)] \xD7 100.",
        topic: "Profit, Loss & Discount",
        subtopic: "Profit & Loss - Proportion of Quantity & Price",
