        userTime: "00:06",
        avgTime: "00:25",
        question: "The radius of a cylinder is 5 cm more than its height. If the curved surface area of the cylinder is 792 cm\xB2, then the volume of the cylinder (in cm\xB3), is ________. [Use \\(\\pi = \\frac{22}{7}\\) ]",
        options: {
          a: "5306",
          b: "5254",
          c: "5544",
          d: "5712"
        },
        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nCurved Surface Area (CSA) = 2 \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r \xD7 h = 792 \u21D2 \u03C0 \xD7 r \xD7 h = 396\nVolume of a cylinder is \u03C0 \xD7 r\xB2 \xD7 h = (\u03C0 \xD7 r \xD7 h) \xD7 r = 396 \xD7 Rs. ince 2 \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 r \xD7 (r - 5) = 792 \u21D2 r \xD7 (r - 5) = 126\nBy simple observation, 14 \xD7 (14 - 5) = 126, so the radius r = 14 cm\nVolume = 396 \xD7 14 = 5544 cm\xB3\n\u2234 The correct answer is 5544 cm\xB3.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nRadius of cylinder (r) = height (h) + 5\nCurved Surface Area (CSA) = 792 cm\xB2\n\nFormula Used:\nCurved Surface Area (CSA) = 2 \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r \xD7 h\nVolume of cylinder = \u03C0 \xD7 r\xB2 \xD7 h\n\nCalculation:\n\u21D2 2 \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 (h + 5) \xD7 h = 792\n\u21D2 (44/7) \xD7 (h\xB2 + 5h) = 792\n\u21D2 h\xB2 + 5h = 792 \xD7 7 \xF7 44\n\u21D2 h\xB2 + 5h = 18 \xD7 7\n\u21D2 h\xB2 + 5h - 126 = 0\n\u21D2 h\xB2 + 14h - 9h - 126 = 0\n\u21D2 h(h + 14) - 9(h + 14) = 0\n\u21D2 (h - 9)(h + 14) = 0\n\u21D2 h = 9 cm (since height cannot be negative)\n\u21D2 Radius (r) = 9 + 5 = 14 cm\n\u21D2 Volume = (22/7) \xD7 (14)\xB2 \xD7 9\n\u21D2 Volume = (22/7) \xD7 196 \xD7 9 = 22 \xD7 28 \xD7 9\n\u21D2 Volume = 616 \xD7 9 = 5544 cm\xB3\n\u2234 The correct answer is 5544 cm\xB3.\n\nAdditional Information\nProperties of a Cylinder\n\nA cylinder is a 3D solid with two parallel circular bases. Total Surface Area (TSA) = CSA + 2 \xD7 Base Area = 2 \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r \xD7 (r + h).\n\nVolume of Related Shapes\n\nThe volume of a cone with the same base radius and height as a cylinder is exactly one - third of the cylinder's volume. Cone Volume = (1/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r\xB2 \xD7 h.\n\nCircumference and Area of Base\n\nThe base of a cylinder is a circle. Base Area = \u03C0 \xD7 r\xB2 and Base Perimeter (Circumference) = 2 \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r. The CSA can directly be calculated as Base Perimeter \xD7 height.",
