        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nThe extra weight of the 14th person (39 kg) is distributed among the first 13 persons to equalize their average to the overall average.\n\nTotal Average = Average of 13 persons + (Extra weight \xF7 13)\nTotal Average = 78 + (39 \xF7 13) = 78 + 3 = 81 kg\nWeight of 14th person = Total Average + Extra = 81 + 39 = 120 kg\n\u2234 The correct answer is 120 kg.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nAverage weight of 13 persons = 78 kg\nWeight of 14th person = Average of 14 persons + 39 kg\n\nFormula Used:\nAverage = Sum of all observations \xF7 Number of observations\n\nCalculations:\nLet the average weight of all 14 persons be x kg.\n\u21D2 Total weight of 14 persons = 14 \xD7 x = 14x\n\u21D2 Weight of 14th person = x + 39\n\u21D2 Sum of weights of 13 persons = 13 \xD7 78 = 1014 kg\n\u21D2 Total Weight = Sum of 13 persons + Weight of 14th person\n\u21D2 14x = 1014 + (x + 39)\n\u21D2 14x - x = 1053\n\u21D2 13x = 1053\n\u21D2 x = 1053 \xF7 13\n\u21D2 x = 81 kg\n\u21D2 Weight of 14th person = 81 + 39 = 120 kg\n\u2234 The correct answer is 120 kg.\n\nAdditional Information\nAverage Concept\n\nAverage is the central value of a set of data. Formula: Average = Total Sum \xF7 Total Number.\n\nDeviation Method\n\nIf a new member joins and the average increases, the new member's value = Old Average + (Increase in Average \xD7 New Strength).\n\nSum of Observations\n\nSum = Average \xD7 Number of observations. Any change in sum directly impacts the average by Change \xF7 n.",
