        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nSide of the maximum possible square = HCF of length and width.\nSide = HCF(12, 8) = 4 m.\nNumber of square designs = (Length \xD7 Width) \xF7 (Side \xD7 Side).\nNumber of designs = (12 \xD7 8) \xF7 (4 \xD7 4) = 96 \xF7 16 = 6.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 6.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven: Length (L) = 12 m and Width (W) = 8 m.\n\nFormula Used:\n1. Area of rectangle = Length \xD7 Width\n2. Side of square (max area) = HCF(L, W)\xB3. Number of squares = (Total Area) \xF7 (Area of one square)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Total Area of the floor = 12 m \xD7 8 m = 96 m2\n\u21D2 To find the maximum possible area of square designs, find HCF of 12 and 8.\n\u21D2 12 = 2 \xD7 2 \xD7 3\n\u21D2 8 = 2 \xD7 2 \xD7 2\n\u21D2 HCF(12, 8) = 2 \xD7 2 = 4 m\n\u21D2 Area of one square design = 4 m \xD7 4 m = 16 m2\n\u21D2 Number of square designs required = 96 \xF7 16\n\u21D2 Number of square designs required = 6\n\u2234 The correct answer is 6.\n\nAdditional Information\nHighest Common Factor (HCF)\n\nThe HCF of two or more numbers is the largest positive integer that divides each of the numbers without leaving a remainder.\n\nMinimum Number of Tiles\n\nTo minimize the number of tiles needed to cover a rectangular area, the side of each square tile must be the HCF of the length and breadth of the rectangle.\n\nArea and Perimeter of a Square\n\nArea = side2 and Perimeter = 4 \xD7 side. All four sides of a square are equal and each angle is 90\xB0.",
