        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nFind the common difference (k) between divisors and remainders: 24 - 13 = 11, 40 - 29 = 11, 48 - 37 = 11.\n\nCalculate LCM of (24, 40, 48) = 240.\n\nThe required number is (LCM \xD7 n) - k. For n = 1, Number = 240 - 11 = 229.\n\nSum of digits of 229 = 2 + 2 + 9 = 13.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 13.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nDivisors: D1 = 24, D2 = 40, D3 = 48\nRemainders: R1 = 13, R2 = 29, R3 = 37\n\nFormula Used:\nWhen (D1 - R1) = (D2 - R2) = (D3 - R3) = k, the number is [LCM(D1, D2, D3) \xD7 n] - k.\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Difference (k) = 24 - 13 = 11\n\u21D2 Difference (k) = 40 - 29 = 11\n\u21D2 Difference (k) = 48 - 37 = 11\n\u21D2 LCM of 24, 40, and 48:\n\u21D2 24 = 23 \xD7 3\n\u21D2 40 = 23 \xD7 5\n\u21D2 48 = 24 \xD7 3\n\u21D2 LCM = 24 \xD7 3 \xD7 5 = 16 \xD7 15 = 240\n\u21D2 Smallest required number = 240 - 11 = 229\n\u21D2 Sum of digits = 2 + 2 + 9 = 13\n\u2234 The correct answer is 13.\n\nAdditional Information\nLCM Method with Constant Remainder\n\nIf a number leaves the same remainder 'r' when divided by x, y, and z, the number is LCM(x, y, z) \xD7 n + r.\n\nLCM Method with Constant Difference\n\nIf the difference between divisor and remainder is constant 'k', the number is LCM(divisors) \xD7 n - k.\n\nSum of Digits Property\n\nThe sum of digits of a number is often used in divisibility tests for 3 and 9, where the sum must be divisible by the divisor.",
