        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nArea of four walls is proportional to (Length + Breadth) \xD7 Height.\n\nIf all dimensions (L, B, H) are doubled, the new area becomes 2 \xD7 2 = 4 times the original area.\n\nCost is directly proportional to the area.\nNew Cost = 4 \xD7 Original Cost = 4 \xD7 25 = 100.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 100.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nOriginal cost of plastering = 25\nNew dimensions = 2 \xD7 Original dimensions\n\nFormula Used:\nArea of four walls = 2 \xD7 (Length + Breadth) \xD7 Height\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Let original dimensions be L, B, and H.\n\u21D2 Original Area (A1) = 2(L + B)H\n\u21D2 New dimensions: L' = 2L, B' = 2B, H' = 2H\n\u21D2 New Area (A2) = 2(2L + 2B) \xD7 2H\n\u21D2 A2 = 2 \xD7 2(L + B) \xD7 2H = 4 \xD7 [2(L + B)H]\n\u21D2 A2 = 4 \xD7 A1\n\u21D2 Since cost is proportional to area: New Cost = 4 \xD7 25 = 100\n\u2234 The correct answer is 100.\n\nAdditional Information\nLateral Surface Area\n\nThe area of the four walls of a cuboid is also known as the Lateral Surface Area (LSA), calculated as 2H(L + B).\n\nTotal Surface Area\n\nIf the floor and ceiling are included, the Total Surface Area (TSA) is 2(LB + BH + HL).\n\nScaling Effect on Volume\n\nIf all dimensions are doubled, the Volume increases by 23 = 8 times, whereas the Area increases by 22 = 4 times.",
