        question: "Out of two numbers, the first number is three-fourth of the second number. If the average of the reciprocal of the two numbers is 7/48, then the first number is",
        options: {
          a: "8",
          b: "4",
          c: "10",
          d: "6"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nRatio of the first number to the second number is 3 : 4. Let the numbers be 3x and 4x.\nSum of reciprocals = 2 \xD7 Average = 2 \xD7 (7/48) = 7/24.\nAccording to the ratio: (1/3x) + (1/4x) = 7/24 \u21D2 (4 + 3)/12x = 7/24.\n7/12x = 7/24 \u21D2 12x = 24 \u21D2 x = 2.\nFirst number = 3 \xD7 2 = 6.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 6.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nFirst number (n1) = 3/4 of Second number (n2)\nAverage of reciprocals = 7/48\n\nFormula:\n\nAverage of two values x and y = (x + y) \xF7 2\nLet the second number be x. Then the first number is (3/4)x.\n\nThe reciprocals are 1/x and 4/3x.\n\n\u21D2 [(1/x) + (4/3x)] \xF7 2 = 7/48\n\u21D2 (1/x) + (4/3x) = (7/48) \xD7 2\n\u21D2 (3 + 4) / 3x = 7/24\n\u21D2 7 / 3x = 7 / 24\n\u21D2 3x = 24\n\u21D2 x = 8 (This is the second number)\n\u21D2 First number = (3/4) \xD7 8 = 6\n\nThus, the first number is 6, which corresponds to Option (4).\n\n\u2234 The correct answer is 6.\n\nAdditional Information\nReciprocal Property\n\nThe product of a number and its reciprocal is always 1. If a number is x/y, its reciprocal is y/x.\n\nAverage of Fractions\n\nTo find the average of two fractions, add them using a common denominator and then divide the sum by 2.\n\nRatio and Proportion\n\nIf A is k times B, the ratio A:B is k:1. This helps in representing variables as multiples of a common factor (e.g., 3x and 4x).",
