        question: "If the average of a number, 50% of that number, and 25% of the same number is 280, then find the number.",
        options: {
          a: "280",
          b: "480",
          c: "360",
          d: "None of the above"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nLet the required number be 100%.\n\nThe three parts given are 100%, 50%, and 25%.\n\nSum of these parts = 100% + 50% + 25% = 175%\nAverage = 175% \xF7 3 = 280\n\u21D2 100% = (280 \xD7 3 \xD7 100) \xF7 175 = 480\n\u2234 The correct answer is 480.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nThe average of a number, 50% of that number, and 25% of the same number is 280.\n\nFormula Used:\nAverage = Sum of observations \xF7 Number of observations\n\nCalculation:\n\u21D2 Let the required number be x.\n\u21D2 The other two values are 0.50x and 0.25x.\n\u21D2 Sum of all three values = x + 0.50x + 0.25x = 1.75x\n\u21D2 Average = 1.75x \xF7 3\n\u21D2 1.75x \xF7 3 = 280\n\u21D2 1.75x = 280 \xD7 3\n\u21D2 1.75x = 840\n\u21D2 x = 840 \xF7 1.75\n\u21D2 x = 84000 \xF7 175 = 480\n\u2234 The correct answer is 480.\n\nAdditional Information\nAverage of Multiple Quantities\n\nThe average (or arithmetic mean) is defined as the sum of all observations divided by the total number of observations. Average = Sum \xF7 Count.\n\nPercentage to Fraction Conversion\n\nPercentages can be directly represented as fractions or decimals to simplify calculations: 50% = 1/2 = 0.5 and 25% = 1/4 = 0.25.\n\nSolving Linear Equations\n\nWhen solving an equation in the form ax = b, dividing both sides by the coefficient a gives the value of x. Using fractions like 1.75 = 7/4 can make division easier (x = 840 \xD7 4 \xF7 7 = 480).",
