        userTime: "01:36",
        avgTime: "00:50",
        question: "On a sum of money, the compound interest for 2 years is Rs. 832, while the simple interest for the same time period is Rs.800, then find out the difference amount for period of 3 years?",
        options: {
          a: "98.56",
          b: "96.43",
          c: "90",
          d: "None of these"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nSI for 1 year = 800 \xF7 2 = \u20B9400\nDifference for 2 years = CI - SI = 832 - 800 = \u20B932\nRate\n(R) = (Interest on 1st year SI \xF7 1st year SI) \xD7 100 = (32 \xF7 400) \xD7 100 = 8%\nFor 3 years, Difference = 3 \xD7 (2-year Diff) + (R% of 2-year Diff)\nDifference = 3 \xD7 32 + (8% of 32) = 96 + 2.56 = 98.56\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B998.56.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nCompound Interest (CI) for 2 years = \u20B9832\nSimple Interest (SI) for 2 years = \u20B9800\n\nFormula Used:\nDifference for 2 years (D2) = P \xD7 (R \xF7 100)2\nDifference for 3 years (D3) = 3 \xD7 D2 + (R% of D2)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 SI for 1 year = Total SI \xF7 2 = 800 \xF7 2 = \u20B9400\n\u21D2 Difference between CI and SI for 2 years (D2) = 832 - 800 = \u20B932\n\u21D2 The difference of \u20B932 is the interest earned exactly on the first year's SI (\u20B9400).\n\u21D2 Rate of Interest\n(R) = (32 \xF7 400) \xD7 100% = 8%\n\u21D2 Difference for 3 years (D3) = 3 \xD7 D2 + (R% of D2)\n\u21D2 D3 = 3 \xD7 32 + (8 \xF7 100) \xD7 32\n\u21D2 D3 = 96 + 2.56\n\u21D2 D3 = \u20B998.56\n\u2234 The correct answer is \u20B998.56.\n\nAdditional Information\nTree Method for Compound Interest\n\nIt breaks down CI into simple interest and interest-on-interest components. The 1st row is always the Simple Interest. The lower rows sum up to represent the exact difference between CI and SI over the years.\n\nCI vs SI Difference (2 Years)\n\nFormula: Diff2 = P \xD7 (R \xF7 100)2. It strictly represents the interest generated on the first year's simple interest.\n\nCI vs SI Difference (3 Years)\n\nFormula: Diff3 = P \xD7 (R \xF7 100)2 \xD7 (3 + R \xF7 100). For fast calculation, simply multiply the 2-year difference by 3 and add the rate percentage of the 2-year difference.",
