        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nReduce angle to first quadrant: $378^\\circ = 360^\\circ + 18^\\circ$.\n$\\Rightarrow \\operatorname{cosec} 378^\\circ = \\operatorname{cosec} 18^\\circ$ and $\\tan 378^\\circ = \\tan 18^\\circ$.\nUsing $1 + \\tan^2 \\theta = \\sec^2 \\theta$:\n$\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}^2 18^\\circ}{1 + \\tan^2 18^\\circ} = \\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}^2 18^\\circ}{\\sec^2 18^\\circ} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sin^2 18^\\circ}}{\\frac{1}{\\cos^2 18^\\circ}} = \\frac{\\cos^2 18^\\circ}{\\sin^2 18^\\circ} = \\cot^2 18^\\circ$.\nSince $\\cot 18^\\circ = \\frac{p}{q}$:\n$\\Rightarrow \\cot^2 18^\\circ = \\left(\\frac{p}{q}\\right)^2 = \\frac{p^2}{q^2}$.\n\u2234 The correct answer is $\\frac{p^2}{q^2}$.",
