        avgTime: "00:33",
        question: "A boat can go 54 km upstream in 6 hours. If the speed of the stream is 4.8 km/h, then how much time (in hours) will the boat take to cover a distance of 279 km downstream?",
        options: {
          a: "20",
          b: "15",
          c: "18",
          d: "16"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nUpstream speed (U) = 54 \xF7 6 = 9 km/h.\nDownstream speed (D) = U + 2 \xD7 Stream speed = 9 + 2 \xD7 4.8 = 18.6 km/h.\nTime downstream = Distance \xF7 D = 279 \xF7 18.6 = 15 hours.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 15 hours.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nDistance upstream = 54 km\nTime upstream = 6 hours\nSpeed of the stream\n(S) = 4.8 km/h\nDistance downstream = 279 km\n\nFormula Used:\nUpstream speed (U) = Boat speed (B) - Stream speed\n(S)\nDownstream speed (D) = Boat speed (B) + Stream speed\n(S)\nTime = Distance \xF7 Speed\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Upstream speed (U) = 54 \xF7 6 = 9 km/h\n\u21D2 U = B - S\n\u21D2 9 = B - 4.8\n\u21D2 B = 9 + 4.8 = 13.8 km/h\n\u21D2 Downstream speed (D) = B + S = 13.8 + 4.8 = 18.6 km/h\n\u21D2 Time downstream = Distance \xF7 Downstream speed\n\u21D2 Time downstream = 279 \xF7 18.6 = 15 hours\n\u2234 The correct answer is 15 hours.\n\nAdditional Information\nUpstream and Downstream Speeds\n\nWhen a boat travels against the flow of the river, it moves upstream (U = B - S). When it travels with the flow, it moves downstream (D = B + S).\n\nSpeed of Boat and Stream\nIf upstream speed (U) and downstream speed (D) are given: Speed of boat in still water (B) = (D + U) \xF7 2. Speed of stream\n(S) = (D - U) \xF7 2.\nDistance, Speed and Time\nThe fundamental relation is Distance = Speed \xD7 Time. For river problems, always determine the effective speed (downstream or upstream) first.",
