        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nWages are distributed in the inverse ratio of time taken when persons work together.\n\nTime ratio of A : B = 20 : 50 = 2 : 5\nEfficiency (wage) ratio of A : B = 5 : 2\nShare of B = (2 \xF7 7) \xD7 3500 = 1000\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 1000.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nTime taken by A = 20 days\nTime taken by B = 50 days\nTotal wages = Rs. 3500\n\nFormula Used:\nWages are distributed in the ratio of efficiencies when working together.\n\nTotal Work = LCM of days taken.\nEfficiency = Total Work \xF7 Days\n\nPerson	Days	Total Work	Efficiency\nA	20	100	5\nB	50	2\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Efficiency ratio of A : B = 5 : 2\n\u21D2 Total efficiency parts = 5 + 2 = 7\n\u21D2 Share of B = (Efficiency of B \xF7 Total efficiency) \xD7 Total wages\n\u21D2 Share of B = (2 \xF7 7) \xD7 3500\n\u21D2 Share of B = 2 \xD7 500 = 1000\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 1000.\n\nAdditional Information\nWork and Wages\n\nWages are always distributed in proportion to the total work done. If multiple people work together for the exact same duration, their total wages are directly divided in the ratio of their individual efficiencies.\n\nEfficiency vs Time\n\nEfficiency is inversely proportional to time. If the ratio of time taken by A and B to complete a piece of work is a : b, then the ratio of their individual efficiencies will be b : a.\n\nPipes & Cisterns\n\nConcepts of time and work apply identically to pipes and cisterns problems. The only key difference is that an outlet or emptying pipe is assigned a negative efficiency.",
