        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nSpeed of the car = 990 \xF7 15 = 66 km/h.\nSpeed of the train = 180% of 66 = 1.8 \xD7 66 = 118.8 km/h.\nTime taken by train = Distance \xF7 Speed = 891 \xF7 118.8 = 7.5 hours. 7.5 hours is equal to 71\u20442 hours.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 71\u20442 hours.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nDistance covered by car = 990 km\nTime taken by car = 15 hours\nAverage speed of train = 180% of average speed of car\nDistance to be covered by train = 891 km\n\nFormula Used:\nSpeed = Distance \xF7 Time\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Speed of the car = 990 \xF7 15\n\u21D2 Speed of the car = 66 km/h\n\u21D2 Speed of the train = 180% of 66\n\u21D2 Speed of the train = (180 \xF7 100) \xD7 66 = 1.8 \xD7 66 = 118.8 km/h\n\u21D2 Time taken by the train = 891 \xF7 118.8\n\u21D2 Time taken by the train = 8910 \xF7 1188\n\u21D2 Time taken by the train = 7.5 hours\n\u21D2 7.5 hours = 71\u20442 hours\n\u2234 The correct answer is 71\u20442 hours.\n\nAdditional Information\nAverage Speed\n\nAverage speed is the total distance traveled divided by the total time taken. Formula: Average Speed = Total Distance \xF7 Total Time.\n\nRelative Speed\n\nWhen two objects move in the same direction, their relative speed is the difference of their individual speeds (S1 - S2). In opposite directions, it is the sum (S1 + S2).\n\nConversion of Units\n\nTo convert speed from km/h to m/s, multiply by 5 \xF7 18. To convert from m/s to km/h, multiply by 18 \xF7 5.",
