        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nPut \u03B8 = 45\xB0 to evaluate the expression quickly without using complex trigonometric identities.\nGiven = [sin(225\xB0) \xD7 cos(135\xB0)] / [sin(315\xB0) \xD7 cos(405\xB0)] \xD7 [tan(225\xB0) \xD7 cot(315\xB0)] / [cosec(-45\xB0) \xD7 sin(315\xB0)]\n\u21D2 [(-1/\u221A2) \xD7 (-1/\u221A2)] / [(-1/\u221A2) \xD7 (1/\u221A2)] \xD7 [1 \xD7 (-1)] / [(-\u221A2) \xD7 (-1/\u221A2)]\n\u21D2 [(1/2) / (-1/2)] \xD7 [(-1) / 1]\n\u21D2 (-1) \xD7 (-1) = 1\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\n[sin(\u03C0 + \u03B8) \xD7 cos(\u03C0/2 + \u03B8)] / [sin(2\u03C0 - \u03B8) \xD7 cos(2\u03C0 + \u03B8)] \xD7 [tan(3\u03C0/2 - \u03B8) \xD7 cot(2\u03C0 - \u03B8)] / [cosec(-\u03B8) \xD7 sin(3\u03C0/2 + \u03B8)]\n\nFormula Used:\nTrigonometric conversions for allied angles:\n\n\u21D2 sin(\u03C0 + \u03B8) = -sin\u03B8 | cos(\u03C0/2 + \u03B8) = -sin\u03B8\n\u21D2 sin(2\u03C0 - \u03B8) = -sin\u03B8 | cos(2\u03C0 + \u03B8) = cos\u03B8\n\u21D2 tan(3\u03C0/2 - \u03B8) = cot\u03B8 | cot(2\u03C0 - \u03B8) = -cot\u03B8\n\u21D2 cosec(-\u03B8) = -cosec\u03B8 | sin(3\u03C0/2 + \u03B8) = -cos\u03B8\n\nCalculation:\n\u21D2 Substituting the conversions into the given expression:\n\u21D2 [(-sin\u03B8) \xD7 (-sin\u03B8)] / [(-sin\u03B8) \xD7 (cos\u03B8)] \xD7 [(cot\u03B8) \xD7 (-cot\u03B8)] / [(-cosec\u03B8) \xD7 (-cos\u03B8)]\n\u21D2 [sin\xB2\u03B8] / [-sin\u03B8 \xD7 cos\u03B8] \xD7 [-cot\xB2\u03B8] / [cosec\u03B8 \xD7 cos\u03B8]\n\u21D2 [-sin\u03B8 / cos\u03B8] \xD7 [-cot\xB2\u03B8] / [(1 / sin\u03B8) \xD7 cos\u03B8]\n\u21D2 [-tan\u03B8] \xD7 [-cot\xB2\u03B8 / cot\u03B8]\n\u21D2 (-tan\u03B8) \xD7 (-cot\u03B8)\n\u21D2 tan\u03B8 \xD7 cot\u03B8 = 1\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1.\n\nAdditional Information\nASTC Rule (Quadrants)\n\n1st Quadrant: All positive | 2nd Quadrant: sin & cosec positive | 3rd Quadrant: tan & cot positive | 4th Quadrant: cos & sec positive.\n\nComplementary & Supplementary Angles\n\nFor angles (90\xB0 \xB1 \u03B8) and (270\xB0 \xB1 \u03B8), trigonometric ratios change (sin \u2194 cos, tan \u2194 cot, sec \u2194 cosec). For angles (180\xB0 \xB1 \u03B8) and (360\xB0 \xB1 \u03B8), the trigonometric ratios remain unchanged.\n\nNegative Angle Identities\n\nsin(-\u03B8) = -sin\u03B8 | cos(-\u03B8) = cos\u03B8 | tan(-\u03B8) = -tan\u03B8 | cosec(-\u03B8) = -cosec\u03B8.",
        topic: "Trigonometry",
