        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nEffective rate for 6 months (half year) = 8.5% \xF7 2 = 4.25%\nSimple Interest = 4.25% of 14800\nSimple Interest = 4.25 \xD7 148 = 629\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 629.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nPrincipal (P) = Rs. 14800\nRate (R) = 8.5% per annum\nTime (T) = 6 months = 6 \xF7 12 = 1/2 year\n\nFormula Used:\nSimple Interest (SI) = (P \xD7 R \xD7 T) \xF7 100\nPrincipal\nRs. 14800\nSimple Interest\nRs. 629\nR = 8.5% p.a.\nT = 6 months\nI = (P \xD7 R \xD7 T) \xF7 100\n\nCalculation:\n\u21D2 SI = (14800 \xD7 8.5 \xD7 1/2) \xF7 100\n\u21D2 SI = (148 \xD7 8.5) \xF7 2\n\u21D2 SI = 74 \xD7 8.5\n\u21D2 SI = 629\n\u2234 The correct answer is Rs. 629.\n\nAdditional Information\nSimple Interest (SI)\n\nSimple interest is calculated on the original principal for the entire given period. Formula: SI = (P \xD7 R \xD7 T) \xF7 100.\n\nCompound Interest (CI)\n\nCompound interest is calculated on the principal as well as the accumulated interest of previous periods. Formula: Amount = P(1 + R/100)T.\n\nRule of 72\n\nA quick trick to estimate the number of years required to double the invested money at a given annual fixed interest rate. Time \u2248 72 \xF7 Rate.",
