        userTime: "00:44",
        avgTime: "00:29",
        question: "A started a work and left working after 9 days now B finished the remaining work in 24 days. Had A left the work after working for 13 days then B would have finished the remaining work in next 18 days. Then find in how many days A and B together can complete the work",
        options: {
          a: "12 days",
          b: "15 days",
          c: "16 days",
          d: "18 days"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nWork done by A in (13 - 9) = 4 days is finished by B in (24 - 18) = 6 days.\nEfficiency Ratio (A : B) = 6 : 4 = 3 : 2.\nTotal Work = (A \xD7 9 days) + (B \xD7 24 days) = (3 \xD7 9) + (2 \xD7 24) = 27 + 48 = 75 units.\nCombined Efficiency of A + B = 3 + 2 = 5 units/day.\nTime taken by A and B together = 75 \xF7 5 = 15 days.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 15 days.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nCase 1: A works for 9 days, then B works for 24 days.\nCase 2: A works for 13 days, then B works for 18 days.\n\nFormula Used:\nTotal Work = Efficiency \xD7 Time\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Let efficiency of A be 'a' and B be 'b'.\n\u21D2 Total Work (W) = 9a + 24b = 13a + 18b\n\u21D2 13a - 9a = 24b - 18b\n\u21D2 4a = 6b\n\u21D2 a/b = 6/4 = 3/2\n\u21D2 Total Work = 9(3) + 24(2) = 27 + 48 = 75 units\n\u21D2 Time taken by A alone = 75 \xF7 3 = 25 days\n\u21D2 Time taken by B alone = 75 \xF7 2 = 37.5 days\n\nPerson	Days	Total Work	Efficiency\nA	25	75	3\nB	37.5	2\n\n\u21D2 Combined Efficiency of (A + B) = 3 + 2 = 5 units/day\n\u21D2 Time taken together = Total Work \xF7 Combined Efficiency\n\u21D2 Time = 75 \xF7 5 = 15 days\n\u2234 The correct answer is 15 days.\n\nAdditional Information\nEfficiency and Time Relation\n\nEfficiency is inversely proportional to the time taken to complete a work. If the ratio of time is x:y, the ratio of efficiency is y:x.\n\nCombined Work Formula\n\nIf A takes 'x' days and B takes 'y' days, then together they take (x \xD7 y) \xF7 (x + y) days.\n\nWork and Wages\n\nWages are always distributed in the ratio of the work done, which is the product of efficiency and the number of days worked.",
