        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nRatio of corresponding sides = \u221A(Ratio of areas) = \u221A(25 / 144) = 5 / 12\nSince \u0394ABC \u223C \u0394PQR, the corresponding side to AC is PR.\nTherefore, AC / PR = 5 / 12\n9 / PR = 5 / 12 \u21D2 PR = (9 \xD7 12) \xF7 5\nPR = 108 \xF7 5 = 21.6\n\u2234 The correct answer is 21.6 cm.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\n\u0394ABC \u223C \u0394PQR\n\nArea(\u0394ABC) / Area(\u0394PQR) = 25 / 144\nAB = 12 cm, BC = 7 cm, AC = 9 cm\n\nFormula Used:\nWhen two triangles are similar, the ratio of their areas is equal to the square of the ratio of their corresponding sides:\n\nArea(\u0394ABC) / Area(\u0394PQR) = (AC / PR)\xB2\n\nA\nB\nC\n12 cm\n9 cm\n7 cm\nArea = 25\nP\nQ\nR\nPR = ?\nArea = 144\n~\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 (AC / PR)\xB2 = 25 / 144\n\u21D2 AC / PR = \u221A(25 / 144)\n\u21D2 AC / PR = 5 / 12\n\u21D2 Substitute the value of AC = 9 cm:\n\u21D2 9 / PR = 5 / 12\n\u21D2 5 \xD7 PR = 9 \xD7 12\n\u21D2 5 \xD7 PR = 108\n\u21D2 PR = 108 \xF7 5 = 21.6\n\u2234 The correct answer is 21.6 cm.\n\nAdditional Information\nSimilarity of Triangles\n\nTwo triangles are similar if their corresponding angles are equal and their corresponding sides are proportional. If \u0394ABC \u223C \u0394PQR, then the ratio pattern strictly follows AB/PQ = BC/QR = AC/PR.\n\nArea Ratio Theorem\n\nThe ratio of the areas of two similar triangles is equal to the square of the ratio of any pair of their corresponding sides, altitudes, or medians.\n\nPerimeter Ratio of Similar Triangles\n\nUnlike the area ratio, the ratio of the perimeters of two similar triangles is directly equal to the ratio of their corresponding sides without any squared values.",
