        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nAverage speed for two equal halves of a journey = (2 \xD7 S1 \xD7 S2) \xF7 (S1 + S2)\nAverage speed = (2 \xD7 21 \xD7 24) \xF7 (21 + 24) = 1008 \xF7 45 = 22.4 km/h\nTotal Distance = Average Speed \xD7 Total Time\nTotal Distance = 22.4 \xD7 12 = 268.8 km\n\u2234 The correct answer is 268.8 km.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nSpeed for first half (S1) = 21 km/h\nSpeed for second half (S2) = 24 km/h\nTotal time (T) = 12 hours\n\nFormula Used:\nTime = Distance \xF7 Speed\nLet the total distance be D km.\n\u21D2 Time for first half = (D \xF7 2) \xF7 21 = D \xF7 42 hours\n\u21D2 Time for second half = (D \xF7 2) \xF7 24 = D \xF7 48 hours\n\u21D2 Total Time = D \xF7 42 + D \xF7 48 = 12\n\u21D2 (8D + 7D) \xF7 336 = 12 [LCM of 42 and 48 is 336]\n\u21D2 15D \xF7 336 = 12\n\u21D2 15D = 12 \xD7 336\n\u21D2 15D = 4032\n\u21D2 D = 4032 \xF7 15\n\u21D2 D = 268.8 km\n\u2234 The correct answer is 268.8 km.\n\nAdditional Information\nAverage Speed\n\nIt is the total distance traveled divided by the total time taken. Average Speed = Total Distance \xF7 Total Time.\n\nConversion of Units\n\nTo convert km/h to m/s, multiply by 5/18. To convert m/s to km/h, multiply by 18/5.\n\nProportionality Rule\n\nIf distance is constant, speed is inversely proportional to time (S \u221D 1/T). If time is constant, distance is directly proportional to speed (D \u221D S).",
