        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\nShortcut Trick\nVolume of a hemisphere = (2/3) \xD7 \u03C0 \xD7 r3\nGiven: r = 5 cm\nVolume = (2/3) \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 5 \xD7 5 \xD7 5\nVolume = (2 \xD7 22 \xD7 125) \xF7 21 \u2248 261.9 cm3\n\u2234 The correct answer is 261.9 cm3.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nRadius of the hemisphere (r) = 5 cm\n\nFormula Used:\nVolume of Hemisphere (V) = (2/3) \xD7 \u03C0r3\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Volume = (2/3) \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 (5)\xB3\n\u21D2 Volume = (2/3) \xD7 (22/7) \xD7 125\n\u21D2 Volume = (44 \xD7 125) \xF7 21\n\u21D2 Volume = 5500 \xF7 21\n\u21D2 Volume \u2248 261.9047 cm3\n\u2234 The correct answer is 261.9 cm3.\n\nAdditional Information\nCurved Surface Area (CSA) of Hemisphere\n\nThe surface area of the curved part is 2\u03C0r2.\n\nTotal Surface Area (TSA) of Hemisphere\nIncludes the base circle area: TSA = 2\u03C0r2 + \u03C0r2 = 3\u03C0r2.\n\nVolume of a Full Sphere\n\nThe volume of a complete sphere is exactly double that of a hemisphere: V = (4/3)\u03C0r3.",
