        userTime: "00:58",
        avgTime: "00:40",
        question: "The price of an article is reduced by 35%. How much should be the new price increased to get the original price?",
        options: {
          a: "$66 \\frac{2}{13}$\\%",
          b: "$33 \\frac{1}{3}$\\%",
          c: "$53 \\frac{11}{13}$\\%",
          d: "$52 \\frac{1}{13}$\\%"
        },
        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTo restore a value after a reduction of r%, apply the recovery formula: Required Increase % = [Reduction / (100 - Reduction)] \xD7 100\n\n\u21D2 Required Increase % = [35 / (100 - 35)] \xD7 100\n\u21D2 (35 / 65) \xD7 100 = (7 / 13) \xD7 100 = 700 / 13 = 53 11/13 %\n\u2234 The correct answer is 53 11/13 %.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nReduction in price = 35%\n\nFormula Used:\nPercentage Increase = (Difference / Initial Value) \xD7 100\n\u21D2 Let the original price of the article be \u20B9100.\n\u21D2 Reduced Price = 100 - 35% of 100 = \u20B965.\n\u21D2 To get back to the original price, the increase needed = 100 - 65 = \u20B935.\n\u21D2 This increase of \u20B935 is required on the new price of \u20B965.\n\u21D2 Required Percentage Increase = (35 / 65) \xD7 100\n\u21D2 Required Percentage Increase = (7 / 13) \xD7 100 = 700 / 13 = 53 11/13 %\n\u2234 The correct answer is 53 11/13 %.\n\nAdditional Information\nBase Change Property\n\nIf a value is decreased by x%, to restore it to the original value, it must be increased by [x / (100 - x)] \xD7 100%.\n\nPrice - Consumption Relation\n\nIf the price of a commodity decreases by r%, the increase in consumption required to keep the expenditure same is [r / (100 - r)] \xD7 100%.\n\nSuccessive Percentage Change\n\nThe net percentage change for two successive changes of a% and b% is given by the formula: [a + b + (a \xD7 b) / 100]%.",
