        userTime: "00:22",
        avgTime: "00:58",
        question: "A policeman notices a thief from a distance of 300 m. The thief starts running and the policeman chases him. The thief and the policeman run at the speeds of 10 km/h and 12 km/h, respectively. What will be the distance between them (in m) after 6 minutes?",
        options: {
          a: "150",
          b: "200",
          c: "80",
          d: "100"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nRelative speed of policeman with respect to thief = 12 - 10 = 2 km/h.\nRelative speed in m/min = (2 \xD7 1000) \xF7 60 = 100/3 m/min.\nRelative distance covered in 6 minutes = (100/3) \xD7 6 = 200 m.\nRemaining distance between them = Initial distance - Distance covered = 300 - 200 = 100 m.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 100 m.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nDistance between Policeman and Thief = 300 m\nSpeed of Thief (Vt) = 10 km/h\nSpeed of Policeman (Vp) = 12 km/h\nTime (t) = 6 minutes\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Relative Speed = Vp - Vt = 12 - 10 = 2 km/h\n\u21D2 To convert km/h to m/s: 2 \xD7 (5/18) = 5/9 m/s\n\u21D2 Time in seconds = 6 \xD7 60 = 360 seconds\n\u21D2 Relative distance covered in 6 min = Relative Speed \xD7 Time\n\u21D2 Distance covered = (5/9) \xD7 360 = 5 \xD7 40 = 200 m\n\u21D2 Distance between them after 6 min = Initial Gap - Relative distance covered\n\u21D2 Remaining distance = 300 - 200 = 100 m\n\u2234 The correct answer is 100 m.\n\nAdditional Information\nRelative Speed Concept\n\nWhen two objects move in the same direction, relative speed = S1 - S2. If they move in opposite directions, relative speed = S1 + S2.\nSpeed Unit Conversion\n\nTo convert Speed from km/h to m/s, multiply by 5/18. To convert from m/s to km/h, multiply by 18/5.\n\nCatching Time Formula\n\nTime taken to catch the thief = (Initial distance between them) \xF7 (Relative Speed).",
