        userTime: "01:27",
        avgTime: "00:55",
        question: "The nearest number which is greater to 87501, and is completely divisible by 765 is :",
        options: {
          a: "88975",
          b: "87975",
          c: "87966",
          d: "87775"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nFind the remainder of 87501 when divided by 765.\n\nRemainder = 87501 (mod 765) = 291.\n\nTo find the next greater divisible number, add (Divisor - Remainder) to the number.\n\nRequired Number = 87501 + (765 - 291) = 87501 + 474 = 87975.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 87975.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nOriginal Number = 87501\nDivisor = 765\n\nFormula Used:\nSmallest number greater than N divisible by D = N + (D - (N mod D))\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Divide 87501 by 765 to find the remainder:\n\u21D2 87501 \xF7 765 = 114 with a remainder of 291\n\u21D2 765 \xD7 114 = 87210 (largest divisible number less than 87501)\n\u21D2 The next divisible number = 87210 + 765\n\u21D2 Required number = 87975\n\u21D2 Verification: 87975 \xF7 765 = 115 (exactly divisible)\n\u2234 The correct answer is 87975.\n\nAdditional Information\nDivisibility and Remainders\n\nWhen a number N is divided by D, the remainder R always satisfies 0 \u2264 R < D. To make N divisible by D, one can either subtract R from N or add (D - R) to N.\n\nDivisibility Rule for Composite Numbers\n\nFor a number to be divisible by 765, it must be divisible by its prime factors. Since 765 = 32 \xD7 5 \xD7 17, the number must be divisible by 5 (ends in 0 or 5) and 9 (sum of digits is a multiple of 9).",
        topic: "Number System",
