        question: "If the complement of an angle x is equal to the supplement of angle 4x and the supplement of an angle y is 4 times its complement, then what is the value of (x + y) ?",
        options: {
          a: "80\xB0",
          b: "90\xB0",
          c: "100\xB0",
          d: "120\xB0"
        },
        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nFrom the first condition: 90\xB0 - x = 180\xB0 - 4x \u2192 3x = 90\xB0 \u2192 x = 30\xB0\nFrom the second condition: 180\xB0 - y = 4 \xD7 (90\xB0 - y) \u2192 3y = 180\xB0 \u2192 y = 60\xB0\nRequired sum = x + y = 30\xB0 + 60\xB0 = 90\xB0\n\u2234 The correct answer is 90\xB0.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nComplement of an angle x = Supplement of angle 4x\nSupplement of an angle y = 4 \xD7 Complement of y\n\nFormula Used:\nComplement of angle \u03B8 = 90\xB0 - \u03B8\n\nCalculations:\nFor finding the angle x:\n\n\u21D2 90\xB0 - x = 180\xB0 - 4x\n\u21D2 4x - x = 180\xB0 - 90\xB0\n\u21D2 3x = 90\xB0\n\u21D2 x = 30\xB0\n\nFor finding the angle y:\n\n\u21D2 180\xB0 - y = 4 \xD7 (90\xB0 - y)\n\u21D2 180\xB0 - y = 360\xB0 - 4y\n\u21D2 4y - y = 360\xB0 - 180\xB0\n\u21D2 3y = 180\xB0\n\u21D2 y = 60\xB0\nNow, calculate the value of (x + y):\n\u21D2 x + y = 30\xB0 + 60\xB0 = 90\xB0\n\u2234 The correct answer is 90\xB0.\n\nAdditional Information\nComplementary Angles\n\nTwo angles are complementary if their sum is exactly 90\xB0. If one angle is \u03B8, its complement is (90\xB0 - \u03B8).\n\nSupplementary Angles\n\nTwo angles are supplementary if their sum is exactly 180\xB0. If one angle is \u03B8, its supplement is (180\xB0 - \u03B8).\n\nStraight Angle & Complete Angle\n\nA straight angle measures exactly 180\xB0 and forms a straight line, while a complete angle measures exactly 360\xB0 around a single central point.",
