        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nTotal possible outcomes for tossing 3 coins = 23 = 8.\nOutcomes with at least 2 heads = (Exactly 2 heads) + (Exactly 3 heads).\nFavorable ways = 3C\xB2 + 3C\xB3 = 3 + 1 = 4.\nProbability = Favorable outcomes \xF7 Total outcomes = 4 \xF7 8 = 1/2.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1/2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nNumber of coins tossed = 3\n\nFormula Used:\nProbability P(E) = Number of favorable outcomes n(E) \xF7 Total number of outcomes n(S)\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 When 3 coins are tossed once, the sample space (S) of all possible outcomes is given by:\n\u21D2 S = {HHH, HHT, HTH, THH, HTT, THT, TTH, TTT}\n\u21D2 Total number of possible outcomes, n(S) = 8\n\u21D2 Let E be the event of getting at least 2 heads.\n\u21D2 Favorable outcomes are those that contain either 2 heads or 3 heads.\n\u21D2 Favorable outcomes, E = {HHT, HTH, THH, HHH}\n\u21D2 Number of favorable outcomes, n(E) = 4\n\u21D2 Required Probability P(E) = 4 \xF7 8\n\u21D2 P(E) = 1/2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 1/2.\n\nAdditional Information\nTotal Outcomes for Coins\n\nWhen n coins are tossed simultaneously, the total number of possible outcomes is 2n.\n\nAt Least vs At Most\n\n'At least x' means x or more occurrences. 'At most x' means x or fewer occurrences, including zero.\n\nRange of Probability\n\nThe probability of any event E always lies between 0 and 1, inclusive: 0 \u2264 P(E) \u2264 1.\n\nComplementary Event\n\nThe probability of an event not occurring is given by P(E') = 1 - P(E).",
