        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nLet the numbers be their smallest positive multiples: a = 18 and b = 12.\n(a\xB2 - b\xB2) = 18\xB2 - 12\xB2 = 324 - 144 = 180.\n\nChecking the given options, 180 is divisible by both 30 and 36.\n\nNow, test for another multiple: let a = 18 and b = 24.\n(a\xB2 - b\xB2) = 18\xB2 - 24\xB2 = 324 - 576 = -252, which is divisible by 36 but not 30.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 36.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nNumber a is divisible by 18, and number b is divisible by 12.\n\nCalculations:\n\u21D2 Let a = 18x (where x is an integer)\n\u21D2 Let b = 12y (where y is an integer)\n\u21D2 a\xB2 = (18x)\xB2\n\u21D2 a\xB2 = 324x\xB2\n\u21D2 b\xB2 = (12y)\xB2\n\u21D2 b\xB2 = 144y\xB2\n\u21D2 a\xB2 - b\xB2 = 324x\xB2 - 144y\xB2\n\u21D2 Taking the highest common factor from both numerical coefficients:\n\u21D2 324 = 36 \xD7 9\n\u21D2 144 = 36 \xD7 4\n\u21D2 a\xB2 - b\xB2 = 36(9x\xB2 - 4y\xB2)\n\u21D2 Since x and y are integers, the term (9x\xB2 - 4y\xB2) will also evaluate to an integer.\n\u21D2 Hence, the entire expression is a direct multiple of 36 and will always be divisible by 36.\n\u2234 The correct answer is 36.\n\nAdditional Information\nDivisibility of an Expression\n\nIf an algebraic expression can be rewritten as a multiple of an integer k, i.e., N = k \xD7 m (where m is an integer), then N is always completely divisible by k and all the factors of k.\n\nDifference of Squares\nThe identity a\xB2 - b\xB2 = (a - b)(a + b) is highly useful for finding common factors of quadratic differences without manually calculating the large squares directly.\n\nProperties of Common Divisors\n\nThe highest constant value that divides an algebraic expression axn - byn for all integer values of variables x and y is simply the Highest Common Factor (HCF) of the coefficients a and b.",
