        answer: "c",
        solution: 'Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nWhen a number is added to itself 14 times, it becomes (1 + 14) = 15 times its original value.\n\n15 \xD7 Number = 75\nNumber = 75 \xF7 15 = 5\n\u2234 The correct answer is 5.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nA number when added to itself 14 times results in 75.\n\nMethod Used: Basic linear equation formulation.\n\nCalculation:\nLet the required number be x.\n\u21D2 Original number = x\n\u21D2 Adding x to itself 14 times = x + 14x\n\u21D2 Sum = x + 14x = 15x\n\u21D2 15x = 75\n\u21D2 x = 75 \xF7 15\n\u21D2 x = 5\n\u2234 The correct answer is 5.\n\nAdditional Information\nTranslating Words to Algebra\n\nIf a number x is added to itself n times, the resulting expression is x + nx, which simplifies to (n + 1)x.\n\nMultiplication vs Addition\n\nWhen a problem states "multiplied by n", the expression is simply nx. It is important not to confuse this with "added to itself n times".\n\nLinear Equations in One Variable\n\nAn equation of the form ax = b can be solved directly by isolating the variable through division: x = b \xF7 a.',
