        question: "Gold is 19 times heavier than water and copper is 9 times heavier than water. In which ratio gold and copper should be mixed so that mixed metal (alloy) is 15 times heavier than water?",
        options: {
          a: "19 \u2236 9",
          b: "9 \u2236 19",
          c: "2 \u2236 3",
          d: "3 \u2236 2"
        },
        answer: "d",
        solution: "Solution\n\nShortcut Trick\nBy applying the rule of alligation directly: Weight of Gold = 19, Weight of Copper = 9, Weight of Mixture = 15\nRatio of Gold to Copper = (Mixture - Copper) \u2236 (Gold - Mixture)\nRequired Ratio = (15 - 9) \u2236 (19 - 15)\n\u21D2 6 \u2236 4 = 3 \u2236 2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 3 \u2236 2.\n\nAlternate Method\nGiven:\nWeight of Gold = 19 times heavier than water\nWeight of Copper = 9 times heavier than water\nWeight of Alloy (mixture) = 15 times heavier than water\n\nCalculation:\nLet the quantity of Gold to be mixed be x units and the quantity of Copper be y units.\n\n\u21D2 Total weight of the alloy = 19x + 9y\n\u21D2 Total quantity of the alloy = x + y\n\u21D2 Mean weight of the alloy = (19x + 9y) \xF7 (x + y)\n\nAccording to the given condition, the alloy is 15 times heavier than water:\n\n\u21D2 (19x + 9y) \xF7 (x + y) = 15\n\u21D2 19x + 9y = 15(x + y)\n\u21D2 19x + 9y = 15x + 15y\n\u21D2 19x - 15x = 15y - 9y\n\u21D2 4x = 6y\n\u21D2 x/y = 6/4\n\u21D2 x/y = 3/2\n\u2234 The correct answer is 3 \u2236 2.\n\nAdditional Information\nRule of Alligation\n\nIt allows us to quickly find the ratio in which two ingredients at given values must be mixed to produce a mixture of a desired average value.\n\nWeighted Average Formula\n\nWhen two groups of quantities n1 and n\xB2 have individual averages A1 and A\xB2 respectively, the combined mixture average is determined by (n1 \xD7 A1 + n\xB2 \xD7 A\xB2) \xF7 (n1 + n\xB2).\n\nReplacement Method in Mixtures\n\nIf from a container full of pure liquid of quantity x, y quantity is drawn out and replaced by water n times, the remaining pure liquid quantity is x \xD7 (1 - y/x)n.",
