        solution: 'Solution\n\nThe correct answer is Chandresh Narayanan.\n\nKey Points\nChandresh Narayanan is the author of the book titled "75 Years of Indian Sports - Game, Guts, Glory".\nThe book provides a comprehensive overview of India\u2019s sports history, achievements, and challenges over 75 years since independence.\nIt covers various sports disciplines, iconic moments, and contributions of Indian athletes to the global sports arena.\nThe book highlights the evolution of sports in India, including milestones in cricket, hockey, badminton, athletics, and more.\nChandresh Narayanan is a seasoned sports journalist with extensive knowledge and experience covering Indian and international sports.\n\nAdditional Information\nSanjay Baru\nSanjay Baru is an Indian political commentator, policy analyst, and writer.\nHe is known for his book "The Accidental Prime Minister", which was a memoir about his tenure as media adviser to former Prime Minister Dr. Manmohan Singh.\nHe has expertise in economics and public policy but is not associated with sports literature.\nRonojoy Sen\nRonojoy Sen is a historian and author specializing in Indian politics, history, and culture.\nHe authored "Nation at Play: A History of Sport in India", which explores the history of sports in India but is not linked to the book "75 Years of Indian Sports - Game, Guts, Glory".\nHis work focuses on the socio-cultural impact of sports in India rather than a celebratory account.\nDr. Jagdish Pillai\nDr. Jagdish Pillai is not a widely recognized author in the domain of sports literature.\nThere is limited information available about his contributions to the field, and he is not associated with the book "75 Years of Indian Sports - Game, Guts, Glory".',
