        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is Sikkimese New Year day.\n\nKey Points\nThe Kali Topi dance is a traditional folk dance performed during the Sikkimese New Year celebrations, also known as Losoong or Namsoong.\nThis dance is a part of the Bhutia community\u2019s cultural heritage in the Indian state of Sikkim.\nIt is performed to mark the harvest season and to welcome the new year with blessings for prosperity and well-being.\nThe dance features performers in traditional attire, including the characteristic black hats (Kali Topi), symbolizing their distinct identity.\nLosoong is celebrated in the 10th month of the Tibetan lunar calendar, corresponding to December or January in the Gregorian calendar.\n\nAdditional Information\nLosoong Festival:\nLosoong is a major festival celebrated by the Bhutia, Lepcha, and other communities of Sikkim.\nIt marks the end of the harvest season and the beginning of the Sikkimese New Year.\nTraditional rituals, prayers, and cultural performances like the Black Hat dance and Chaam dances are highlights of the celebrations.\nNamsoong Festival:\nNamsoong is the Lepcha community\u2019s version of the New Year celebration, coinciding with Losoong.\nIt emphasizes harmony with nature and involves rituals to express gratitude for the harvest.\nChaam Dance:\nChaam dances are ritualistic masked dances performed in monasteries during Losoong.\nThey depict tales of good triumphing over evil and are a significant spiritual aspect of the festival.\nSikkim\u2019s Cultural Diversity:\nSikkim is home to diverse ethnic groups, including Bhutias, Lepchas, and Nepalis, each contributing to the state\u2019s vibrant cultural fabric.\nThe state celebrates a wide range of festivals reflecting its rich heritage and traditions.",
