        question: "Which Article, under the Constitution of India, empowers the Government of India to levy and collect Goods and Services Tax?",
        options: {
          a: "Article 266",
          b: "Article 268 A",
          c: "Article 269 A",
          d: "Article 271 A"
        },
        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is Article 269 A.\n\nKey Points\nArticle 269A was introduced under the Constitution of India by the 101st Constitutional Amendment Act, 2016 to implement the Goods and Services Tax (GST) regime.\nThis article allows both the Central Government and the State Governments to levy and collect GST on inter-state trade or commerce.\nThe revenues collected under GST on inter-state trade are shared between the Centre and the states based on a formula prescribed by the Goods and Services Tax Council.\nIt provides the framework for Integrated GST (IGST), which is levied on inter-state transactions and imports.\n\nAdditional Information\nArticle 266\nDeals with Consolidated Fund of India and allocation of receipts and expenditures.\nForms the basis for government accounting and financial management.\nArticle 268A\nRelated to levy and collection of duties of excise on certain goods levied by the Union but collected by the states.\nArticle 271A\nDoes not exist; sometimes confused with Articles 271 and 271A, which deal with taxation of certain goods and cess but not directly GST.",
