        solution: "Solution\n\nThe Correct answer is Only (1).\n\nKey Points\nCalling Attention Motion is an Indian parliamentary innovation. It is not found in parliamentary systems of other countries and is unique to India.\nThis motion allows members of the Parliament to call the attention of a minister to a matter of public importance which requires immediate intervention and explanation.\nThe motion combines elements of both a question and a debate, making it an effective tool for ensuring accountability in governance.\nIt is an important parliamentary procedure for drawing attention to pressing matters such as policy issues, crises, or administrative lapses.\nCalling Attention Motion is explicitly mentioned in the Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in Lok Sabha, signifying its official recognition in parliamentary proceedings.\nThis procedure reflects the democratic principle of ensuring transparency and keeping the government accountable to its people.",
