        answer: "b",
        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is 2) 1, 3, and 4 only.\n\nKey Points\nUnderstanding the statements about the Ruhr industrial region in Germany\n\nCoal and Steel Production\nThe Ruhr region has historically been known for its extensive coal mines and steel production facilities.\nThis industrial base has been a cornerstone of Germany\u2019s economy. Hence\nstatement 1 is correct.\nLargest Industrial Region\nWhile the Ruhr region is a major industrial hub in Germany, it is not the largest industrial region in the world.\nThere are other industrial regions globally, such as in China and the United States, that are larger in terms of production and economic scale. Hence\nstatement 2 is incorrect.\nLocation\nThe Ruhr industrial region is located in the state of North Rhine-Westphalia in western Germany.\nThis region has been central to Germany\u2019s industrial development. Hence\nstatement 3 is correct.\nEnvironmental Challenges\nThe heavy industrialization in the Ruhr region has led to significant environmental challenges, including air and water pollution.\nEfforts have been made to address these issues, but they remain a concern. Hence\nstatement 4 is correct.\n\nAdditional Information\nHistorical Significance\nThe Ruhr region emerged as an industrial powerhouse during the 19th and 20th centuries, particularly driven by its abundant coal resources.\nIts development has played a crucial role in the industrialization of Germany.\nEconomic Transformation\nIn recent years, the Ruhr region has undergone significant economic transformation, shifting from traditional heavy industry to high-tech and service-oriented industries.\nThis diversification is part of broader efforts to ensure sustainable economic growth and development in the region.\nEnvironmental Remediation\nVarious initiatives have been undertaken to mitigate the environmental impact of historic industrial activities, including brownfield redevelopment and pollution control measures.\nThese efforts are aimed at improving the quality of life for residents and ensuring a cleaner environment.",
