        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is Shri Bibek Debroy.\n\nKey Points\nShri Bibek Debroy received the Padma Bhushan award posthumously in the field of Literature and Education in 2025. This recognition is one of India\u2019s highest civilian awards, acknowledging exceptional contributions to the nation.\nThe Padma Awards are categorized into three levels: Padma Vibhushan, Padma Bhushan, and Padma Shri. The Padma Bhushan is the third-highest civilian award in India.\nShri Bibek Debroy is renowned for his extensive contributions to Indian literature, particularly in ancient Sanskrit texts, and his work in the field of economic research. Hence, the correct answer is Shri Bibek Debroy.\nThe award is often given posthumously to recognize individuals who have left a lasting impact on their respective fields, even after their demise.\nShri Bibek Debroy\u2019s scholarly contributions include translations of ancient Indian texts like the Mahabharata and Ramayana, which have been highly acclaimed for their authenticity and accessibility.\n\nAdditional Information\nAbout Padma Awards:\nPadma Bhushan is India\u2019s third-highest civilian award. It is given for distinguished service of a high order in any field, including literature, education, arts, science, and public affairs.\nThe awards are announced annually on the eve of Republic Day and presented by the President of India at ceremonial functions held at Rashtrapati Bhavan.\nAbout Shri Bibek Debroy:\nShri Bibek Debroy was an eminent economist, translator, and author who contributed significantly to Indian literature, Sanskrit studies, and economic policy.\nHe is best known for translating the unabridged Mahabharata, a monumental work that made this ancient text accessible to a global audience.\nHe also played a vital role as the Chairman of the Economic Advisory Council to the Prime Minister (EAC-PM), where he contributed to India\u2019s economic policymaking.\nOther Key Recipients in Literature and Education:\nShri S. L. Bhyrappa: A celebrated Kannada novelist known for his profound exploration of Indian culture, history, and philosophy in his works.\nShri Amitav Ghosh: An internationally acclaimed author, especially known for his works on climate change and historical fiction.\nShri Gulzar: A renowned poet, lyricist, and author, widely respected for his contributions to Indian cinema and literature.\n\nImportant Points\n\nSignificance of Padma Awards:\nThe Padma Awards are a recognition of exceptional contributions to various fields, including arts, education, literature, science, social work, and public affairs.\nThey aim to celebrate and honor individuals who have significantly contributed to nation-building.\nPosthumous Awards:\nThe awards can be given posthumously to acknowledge the lasting impact of a person\u2019s contributions. This reflects the nation\u2019s gratitude towards their service.\nShri Bibek Debroy is a notable example of a posthumous recipient in recent years.",
