        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is Both 1 and 2.\n\nKey Points\nStatement 1 is Correct: In Judo, the red-and-white belt (Ko\u0304haku obi) is worn by judokas holding the ranks of Sixth Dan (6th), Seventh Dan (7th), and Eighth Dan (8th).\nStatement 2 is Correct: According to the International Judo Federation (IJF) competition rules, when two competition areas are adjacent, a shared safety zone of at least 3 metres must be maintained between them to ensure the safety of the competitors.\nThe safety zone provides adequate space for athletes who may move beyond the contest area during a bout, reducing the risk of injuries.\nHence, both statements are correct.\n\nAdditional Information\nThe competition area (contest area) in Judo is generally square and is surrounded by a designated safety zone.\nJudokas holding the Ninth Dan (9th) and Tenth Dan (10th) traditionally wear a solid red belt.\nThe belt system in Judo reflects a practitioner's technical skill, experience, and contribution to the sport.\n\nImportant Points\n\nRed-and-White Belt: 6th Dan to 8th Dan.\nRed Belt: 9th Dan and 10th Dan.\nShared Safety Zone: Minimum 3 metres between adjoining competition areas.\nGoverning Body: International Judo Federation (IJF).\nExam Tip: Remember that the red-and-white belt is awarded to 6th-8th Dan judokas, while a 3-metre shared safety zone is mandatory between adjoining competition areas.\nCorrect Answer: Both 1 and 2.",
