        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is Eastern Imperial Eagle\n\nIn News\nA rare Eastern Imperial Eagle was sighted at Mudumalai Tiger Reserve in Tamil Nadu during the 2025-26 winter season, confirming the reserve\u2019s importance as a winter refuge for long-distance migratory raptors.\n\nKey Points\nScientific Name: Aquila heliaca; Family: Accipitridae; Subfamily: Aquilinae.\nBreeds in southeastern Europe, West and Central Asia; migrates south to northeastern Africa, Middle East, and South & East Asia during winter.\nSecond largest eagle in Europe; wingspan up to 2.14 m; shows reverse sexual dimorphism.\nDiet: Predatory bird controlling rodent and small mammal populations; presence indicates a healthy ecosystem.\nConservation Status: Vulnerable on the IUCN Red List.\n\nAdditional Information\nMudumalai Tiger Reserve is located in Nilgiris district, Tamil Nadu, covering 321 sq. km, and is part of the Nilgiris Biosphere Reserve.\nThe reserve features open grasslands, forest edges, tall nesting trees, and abundant prey, attracting migratory raptors.\nRecent sightings also included the endangered Egyptian vulture alongside the Eastern Imperial Eagle, highlighting ecological significance.\nConservationists warn that increasing tourism could disturb sensitive habitats; sustainable tourism practices are needed to protect wildlife.",
