        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is Chakri - Jammu and Kashmir.\n\nKey Points\nChakri is one of the most popular traditional music forms of Jammu and Kashmir.\nIt is characterized by its unique style of storytelling through music, often depicting folk tales and events.\nInstruments commonly used in Chakri include the harmonium, rubab, nout, and sarangi.\nChakri is often performed during festivals, weddings, and cultural events, making it an integral part of the region's heritage.\nThe music form has been passed down through generations, maintaining its cultural significance in Jammu and Kashmir.\n\nAdditional Information\nThumri\nA genre of semi-classical Indian music originating from Uttar Pradesh.\nKnown for its romantic and devotional themes.\nOften associated with Kathak dance.\nNotable exponents include Begum Akhtar and Girija Devi.\nSorathi\nA traditional folk dance and music form from Gujarat.\nPerformed primarily by the Saurashtra community.\nInvolves storytelling through songs and dance.\nSohar\nA traditional folk song from Bihar and Uttar Pradesh.\nSung during childbirth and other auspicious occasions.\nReflects the cultural practices and traditions of the region.",
