        solution: "The fixed premium rate to be paid by farmers for all Kharif crops under the PMFBY is 2.0%.\n\nUnder the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY), the premium rates are capped at a very low level to reduce the financial burden on farmers.\n\nFor all Kharif crops (summer/monsoon crops), the premium to be paid by the farmer is fixed at 2.0% of the sum insured or the actuarial rate, whichever is less.\n\nFurther Insights:\nGovernment Subsidy: The difference between the actuarial premium rate (the actual market cost of the insurance) and the rate paid by the farmers is shared equally by the Central and State Governments as a subsidy.\nObjective: Launched in 2016, PMFBY aims to provide a comprehensive insurance cover against the failure of the crop, thus helping in stabilizing the income of the farmers and encouraging them to adopt innovative practices.\nCoverage: The scheme covers all stages of the crop cycle, including pre-sowing to post-harvest losses due to non-preventable natural risks such as drought, floods, landslides, pests, and diseases.\n\nRevamped PMFBY (2.0): In 2020, the scheme was made voluntary for all farmers (earlier it was mandatory for loanee farmers). It also increased the flexibility for states to customize the scheme according to their local climatic risks.",
