        solution: "Solution\nThe correct answer is A straight line inclined to the time axis.\n\nKey Points\nUniform speed is defined as a type of motion where an object covers equal distances in equal intervals of time.\nIn a distance-time graph, the distance is plotted on the Y-axis and the time is plotted on the X-axis.\nThe slope of a distance-time graph represents the speed of the object.\nSince the speed is constant (uniform), the slope of the graph must also be constant.\nA graph with a constant slope is represented by a straight line.\nFor uniform speed, this straight line must be inclined to the time axis, indicating that distance increases steadily as time progresses.\n\nAdditional Information\nIf the distance-time graph is a straight line parallel to the time axis, the speed is zero (the object is at rest).\nIf the graph is a curved line, it represents non-uniform motion, where the speed is changing over time.\nThe steeper the slope of the straight line, the higher the uniform speed of the object.\nMathematical relation: Speed = Distance / Time. In a linear graph, this is expressed as y = mx, where m is the constant speed.",
