        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is option 3.\n\nKey Points\nElections (whether direct or indirect) alone do not guarantee democratic government. Hence option 1 is incorrect.\nSometimes autocratic leaders like Hitler also get elected through ballot voting.\nElections should be based on a universal adult franchise as it is based on equality which is a basic principle of democracy.\nElections should be free and fair which should provide equal opportunity to contest and get elected.\nA Republic is where the head of state is elected by the people. Hence option 2 is incorrect.\nIt is not necessarily to be democratic.\nFor ex-China is a republic but not democratic whereas the United Kingdom is a monarch but still democratic.\nA democratic government must be responsible and answerable to the people.\nIt should necessarily explain the policies, provide information to the public and give freedom to criticize the actions through free speech.\nThis best describes the democratic government. Hence option 3 is correct.\nA democratic government need not necessarily have a written set of rules. Hence option 4 is incorrect.\nCountries like New Zealand and Britain have an unwritten constitution, but they qualify to be democratic countries due to features like freedom of speech and expression whereas Countries like Myanmar have a written constitution but not democracy.\n\nAdditional Information\nDemocracy is a form of government in which: Rulers elected by the people take all the major decisions.\nElections offer a choice and fair opportunity to the people to change the current rulers\nThis choice and opportunity are available to all the people on an equal basis, and the exercise of this choice leads to a government limited by basic rules of the constitution and citizens\u2019 rights.\nA democratic government rules within limits set by constitutional law and citizens\u2019 rights.",
