        solution: 'Solution\n\nThe correct answer is "south-west".\nKey Points\nA seasonal shift in wind direction is called a monsoon.\nMonsoons are reasons for heavy rainfall.\nThe Indian monsoon is the most prominent monsoon in the world.\nThe direction in which the monsoon blows is from land towards the Sea in the winters and from Sea towards land in the summers.\nThe winds of monsoon blow from cold to warm climates.\nThe motive in the back of this phenomenon is that bloodless air fills a greater area than heated air.\nThe low-stress place draws southeast change winds.\n\nAdditional Information\nDue to the Coriolis force, these trade winds turn right towards the low-pressure regions in India after crossing the equator and begin blowing withinside the southwestern direction.\nThereafter those exchange winds input the peninsular part of India because of the southwest monsoon.\nWinters in India are dry and hot.\nThe monsoon winds carry moisture from the northeast.\nMost of India lies between the equator and the tropic of cancer, so the Indian land receives direct get right of entry to the sun\u2019s rays.\nThe monsoon in summer enters the Indian subcontinent from the southwest direction.\nThese winds convey moisture from the Indian Ocean.\nThis brings heavy rainfall between the months of June to September.\nThe southeast exchange winds emerge as the southwest monsoon due to the fact those exchange winds go the equator and start blowing in the southwest direction under the influence of the Coriolis force.',
