        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nThe Correct answer is three.\n\nKey Points\nIn Indian classical music, ragas can be classified into three main categories, also known as Jatis, based on the number of notes used.\nThese categories are Audava (pentatonic, using 5 notes), Shadava (hexatonic, using 6 notes), and Sampurna (heptatonic, using 7 notes).\nThis classification helps in identifying the basic structure of ragas and their melodic patterns.\nAudava ragas are simpler and often associated with folk music or devotional songs.\nShadava ragas offer slightly more complexity and are used in various classical compositions.\nSampurna ragas are the most complex, utilizing all seven notes, and are commonly used in more elaborate classical music.\nThe classification into Jatis is an essential aspect of Indian music theory, aiding musicians and learners in understanding and performing ragas.\nThis system showcases the richness and diversity of Indian classical music, reflecting its ability to adapt to different moods and themes.",
