        userTime: "00:14",
        avgTime: "00:27",
        question: "With reference to the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA), consider the following statements:\n\nAssertion (A): The International Atomic Energy Agency promotes the peaceful use of nuclear energy.\nReason\n(R): The Agency conducts safeguards inspections to prevent diversion of nuclear material for military purposes.",
        options: {
          a: "Both A and R are correct and R explains A",
          b: "Both A and R are correct but R does not explain A",
          c: "A is correct but R is incorrect",
          d: "A is incorrect but R is correct"
        },
        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is Option A.\n\nKey Points\nThe IAEA was established to encourage and assist research, development, and practical application of nuclear energy for peaceful purposes.\nA core function of the IAEA is the implementation of safeguards, which involve inspections and verification measures.\nThese safeguards ensure that nuclear materials and facilities are not diverted to nuclear weapons or other military uses.\nAssertion (A): Correct - Promoting peaceful use of nuclear energy is a foundational objective of the IAEA.\nReason\n(R): Correct - Safeguards inspections are a principal mechanism through which the IAEA ensures peaceful use.\nThe safeguards system directly supports and explains how the IAEA promotes peaceful nuclear energy.\n\nHow Reason\n(R) explains Assertion (A):\n\nAssertion (A) states that the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) promotes the peaceful use of nuclear energy.\nReason\n(R) explains the mechanism through which this objective is achieved:\nBy conducting safeguards inspections, the IAEA verifies that nuclear materials, facilities, and technologies meant for civilian purposes are not diverted for military or weapons use.\nThis assurance builds international trust and confidence, enabling countries to cooperate in nuclear energy for power generation, medicine, agriculture, and research.\nWithout such safeguards, civilian nuclear programs could mask weapons development, undermining peaceful use.\n\nTherefore, R explains A because safeguarding nuclear material against military diversion is the practical tool that ensures nuclear energy remains strictly peaceful, directly fulfilling the IAEA\u2019s core mandate.\n\nThus, both A and R are correct, and R explains A \u2192 Option A.\n\nAdditional Information\nThe IAEA was established in 1957 as an autonomous organization under the UN system.\nIts functions rest on three pillars: Safeguards and Verification, Safety and Security, and Science and Technology.\nThe safeguards system operates primarily under the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty (NPT) framework.",
