        answer: "a",
        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is Hydroelectricity.\n\nKey Points\nThe Salal Dam, also known as Salal Hydroelectric Power Station, is primarily used for generating hydroelectric power.\nIt is located on the Chenab River in the Reasi district of Jammu and Kashmir, India.\nThe dam has an installed capacity of 690 megawatts, providing significant power to the region.\nThe construction of the Salal Dam was completed in two stages, with Stage I completed in 1987 and Stage II in 1995.\n\nAdditional Information\nChenab River:\nThe Chenab River is one of the major rivers in the Indian subcontinent, flowing through India and Pakistan.\nIt originates from the confluence of the Chandra and Bhaga rivers in the Lahaul and Spiti districts of Himachal Pradesh, India.\nThe river is a key source of irrigation and hydroelectric power in the region.\nHydroelectric Power:\nHydroelectric power is generated by using the energy of flowing water to turn turbines connected to generators.\nIt is a renewable and clean source of energy, contributing significantly to reducing carbon emissions.\nHydroelectric power plants can provide reliable and consistent power supply, especially in regions with abundant water resources.\nReasi District:\nReasi is a district in the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir, known for its scenic beauty and religious significance.\nThe district is home to several important hydropower projects, including the Salal Dam.\nReasi is also a popular tourist destination, attracting visitors to places like Vaishno Devi and Shiv Khori.\nEnergy Infrastructure in Jammu and Kashmir:\nJammu and Kashmir have several hydroelectric projects, contributing significantly to the region's power supply.\nThese projects are crucial for meeting the energy demands of the area and for economic development.\nThe region's topography and water resources make it an ideal location for hydroelectric power generation.",
