        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is Pir Panjal Range.\n\nKey Points\nThe Pir Panjal Range is part of the Inner Himalayan region and runs from northwest to southeast, forming a natural boundary between the Kashmir Valley and the outer plains.\nThis range separates the Kashmir Valley from the lesser Himalayan regions and lies south of the main Himalayan range.\nIt is known for its significant mountain passes like the Pir Panjal Pass, Banihal Pass, and Rohtang Pass, which have been crucial for trade and travel.\nThe range is home to dense forests and is rich in biodiversity, contributing significantly to the ecology of the region.\nThe Pir Panjal Range is also known for its beautiful landscapes and is a popular destination for trekking and tourism in India.\n\nAdditional Information\nKarakoram Range\nThe Karakoram Range lies to the north of the Himalayan Range and forms the border between India, Pakistan, and China.\nIt is home to some of the world\u2019s highest peaks, including K2 (Mount Godwin-Austen), the second-highest peak in the world.\nThe Siachen Glacier, the largest glacier in India, is located in the Karakoram Range.\nKnown for its rugged terrain and harsh climate, the region has a sparse population.\nLadakh Range\nThe Ladakh Range lies to the north of the Zanskar Range and runs parallel to it.\nThis range is a part of the Trans-Himalayas and is located in the Union Territory of Ladakh.\nFamous for its arid, barren landscapes and high-altitude passes, it plays a crucial role in Ladakh\u2019s topography.\nPopular passes in this range include Khardung La and Chang La, which are among the highest motorable passes in the world.\nDhauladhar Range\nThe Dhauladhar Range is part of the Lesser Himalayas and lies to the south of the Pir Panjal Range.\nIt is known for its steep slopes and sharp ridges and is prominent in the Kangra Valley region of Himachal Pradesh.\nIt serves as a prominent tourist destination and is home to numerous trekking routes.\nTriund, a popular trekking spot, is located in the Dhauladhar Range.",
