        solution: "Solution\nThe correct answer is Option B.\n\nKey Points\nThe crop described requires a hot and humid climate, very high rainfall (over 200 cm), and consistently high temperatures (above 25\xB0C)-conditions typical of equatorial regions, but also found in parts of the tropics and sub-tropics.\nRubber is primarily an equatorial crop, thriving in regions with uniformly high temperatures, heavy and well-distributed rainfall, and high humidity. Hence, Option B is correct.\nPaddy requires high rainfall but can grow in a wider temperature range and is not strictly an equatorial crop. Hence, Option A is incorrect.\nTea prefers warm and humid conditions but grows best at moderate temperatures and often in highland areas with well-distributed rainfall. Hence, Option C is incorrect.\nSugarcane needs high temperatures but generally requires lower rainfall (75-150 cm) and extensive irrigation in many regions. Hence, Option D is incorrect.\nThus, the crop fitting the given climatic conditions is Rubber \u2192 Option B.\n\nAdditional Information\nRubber cultivation is sensitive to frost and prolonged dry seasons.\nIn India, rubber is mainly grown in Kerala, Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, and the Andaman & Nicobar Islands.\nLatex yield is highest where rainfall is well-distributed throughout the year.",
