        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is option 3.\n\nKey Points\nStatement I is correct: The Indian government has launched a six-year mission to boost pulses production, focusing on varieties like tur (pigeon pea), urad (black gram), and masoor (red lentils).\nThis initiative aims to achieve self-sufficiency in pulses by 2029-30, reducing dependence on imports.\nThe mission emphasizes the development of climate-resilient seeds, ensuring remunerative prices for farmers, and improving post-harvest management and storage.\nStatement II is incorrect: Contrary to increasing imports, the mission's objective is to reduce India's reliance on pulses imports by enhancing domestic production.\nThe government plans to procure pulses directly from farmers at guaranteed prices, thereby encouraging local cultivation and aiming for self-sufficiency.",
