        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is Colloidal solution\n\nConcept:\n\nColloidal solution:\n\nColloidal solution is the mixture in which one substance of dispersed insoluble particles is suspended throughout the other substance.\nColloidal solution is also known as colloids.\n\nHeterogeneous mixture:\n\nA colloid is a heterogeneous mixture.\nThe size of the particles of a colloid is too small to be individually seen by the naked eye.\nA solution in which the substances are regularly suspended in a fluid is a Colloidal Solution.\nA true solution is a homogeneous mixture of two or more substances in which the substance dissolved in the solvent has a particle size of less than 10-9 m or 1 nm.\n\nExplanation:\n\nWhen a paste of starch is added to boiling water, amylose dissolves and amylopectin remains as such. Therefore starch becomes partially soluble and forms a paste.\nA mixture of starch in water is an example of a colloidal solution.\n\nAdditional Information\nHomogeneous mixture:\n\nThe composition is uniform throughout the mixture. It is the same at every point in a Homogeneous mixture.\nComponents are not visible to the naked eye in a Homogeneous mixture.\nA Homogeneous mixture has the same proportion of its compound in a sample.\nFor example -Sugar in water is a homogeneous mixture.",
