        answer: "b",
        solution: `Solution

The correct answer is Option 2: Recovery in manufacturing and construction.

Key Points
The Technology Information, Forecasting and Assessment Council (TIFAC) is an autonomous organization set up in 1988 under the Department of Science & Technology, Government of India.
TIFAC's main objective is to assess the state-of-the-art technology and set directions for future technological development in India.
In the wake of the COVID-19 pandemic, TIFAC launched a project titled "RESTART" (Rebuilding, Reviving Economy through Science, Technology, and Research Translations) to support the economy's revival.
One of TIFAC's initiatives includes the development of a technology-fueled PDS (public distribution system) to ensure food security and efficient distribution of resources.

Additional Information
Technology Information, Forecasting and Assessment Council (TIFAC)
TIFAC is an autonomous body under the Department of Science & Technology, Government of India, and was established in 1988.
Its mission is to assess and forecast the technology trajectories in various sectors and set priority areas for future research and development.
TIFAC carries out critical policy analysis and provides recommendations to the government and various stakeholders on technology development.
Through its initiatives, TIFAC aims to foster innovation, enhance technological capabilities, and ensure sustainable development in India.
Public Distribution System (PDS)
The PDS is an Indian food security system established by the Government of India under the Ministry of Consumer Affairs, Food, and Public Distribution.
It distributes subsidized food and non-food items to India's poor.
Major commodities distributed include staple food grains, such as wheat and rice, and other essential items.
The system plays a crucial role in reaching out to the economically weaker sections of society and ensuring food security.
RESTART Project
RESTART stands for Rebuilding, Reviving Economy through Science, Technology, and Research Translations.
It is an initiative by TIFAC to provide strategic foresight and policy recommendations for reviving India's economy post the COVID-19 pandemic.
The project focuses on leveraging science and technology to address economic challenges, promote innovation, and support critical sectors.
Key areas include healthcare, agriculture, manufacturing, and digital infrastructure to enhance resilience and growth.`,
