        question: 'With reference to the integration of Princely States in post-independence India, consider the following statements:\n\n1) The "States Department" was established in 1947 specifically to handle matters related to the relationship between the Central Government and the Princely States.\n\n2) The department was headed by Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel, with G.V. Mavalankar serving as the Administrative Secretary.\n\n3) The "Carrot and Stick" policy used by the department involved offering privy purses and autonomy as incentives while maintaining the threat of military or political consequences for resistance.\n\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?',
