        solution: 'The States Department (later renamed Ministry of States) was established in 1947 under the Government of India to manage all negotiations and administrative matters with Princely States.\n\nIt coordinated their accession, merger, and integration into the Indian Union.\n\nThe Patel - Menon team indeed used a "Carrot and Stick" approach, offering:\n\nCarrot: Privy purses, guarantees of autonomy, titles, dignities.\nStick: Pressure through public opinion, political tactics, and if needed, military action (e.g., police action in Hyderabad).\n\nThe States Department was headed by Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel, but the secretary was V.P. Menon, not G.V. Mavalankar.\n\nMavalankar was the first Speaker of the Lok Sabha, not a secretary of the States Department.\n\nFurther Insights\nIndia had 565 princely states at the time of independence.\n\nThe Instrument of Accession (IoA) allowed states to join India on three subjects - defence, foreign affairs, and communications.\n\nThe integration process included accession, merger agreements, and reorganisation of states.\n\nHyderabad required military intervention under Operation Polo in 1948.\n\nJunagadh was integrated after a public plebiscite in 1948.',
