        solution: "\xB7 The Arjuna Award is given for outstanding performance in sports over a period of four years, not exclusively for lifetime contribution to sports.\n\n\xB7 The Arjuna Award is India's second-highest sporting honour, after the Major Dhyan Chand Khel Ratna Award.\n\n\xB7 The award is given annually by the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports for outstanding international-level sports performance over a four-year period, along with leadership and sportsmanship qualities.\n\nFurther insights:\n\xB7 Instituted in 1961, it is named after Arjuna from the Mahabharata, symbolising dedication, discipline, and focus.\n\n\xB7 Before the introduction of the Khel Ratna in 1991 - 92, the Arjuna Award was India's highest sporting honour.\n\n\xB7 Nominations are received from recognised sports bodies, government authorities, and previous awardees, and recipients are selected by a ministry-appointed committee.\n\n\xB7 As of 2020, the award includes a bronze statuette of Arjuna, a certificate, ceremonial dress, and a cash prize of \u20B915 lakh.\n\n\xB7 Over time, the award has been expanded and revised to include more disciplines, indigenous games, para-sports, and team events.\n\n\xB7 The latest 2018 guidelines limit the award to major international sports events (such as the Olympics, Asian Games, World Championships, and World Cups), recommend a maximum of 15 awards per year, and ensure representation for physically challenged athletes.",
