        answer: "c",
        solution: "Solution\n\nThe correct answer is 1, 2 and 4 only.\n\nKey Points\nWork done depends on the displacement of the object, as it represents the distance moved under the influence of force.\nThe angle between force and displacement determines the effective component of the force contributing to the work.\nThe magnitude of the force applied directly impacts the work done, as work is calculated as the product of force, displacement, and the cosine of the angle.\nInitial speed of the object does not influence work done directly; work depends on the change in kinetic energy or force-displacement dynamics.\nWork is mathematically expressed as W = F . d \xD7 cos(\u03B8), where F is force, d is displacement, and \u03B8 is the angle between force and displacement.\n\nAdditional Information\nWork: Work is defined as the transfer of energy when a force is applied to an object causing displacement.\nForce: It refers to an interaction that changes the motion of an object, impacting the calculation of work.\nDisplacement: This is the vector quantity describing the change in position of an object, essential for evaluating work.\nCosine of the angle: The angle \u03B8 between the force and displacement affects the effective force contributing to the work, with cos(\u03B8) ranging from -1 to +1.\nEnergy transfer: Work done on an object is directly related to the change in its energy, such as kinetic or potential energy.",
